{"raw": {"https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45595": {"title": "COORDINATOR/STUDY ABROAD", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | COORDINATOR/STUDY ABROAD Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. COORDINATOR/STUDY ABROAD Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. For best consideration, please submit application materials on or before Monday, October 26, 2026. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3990 Position Number 00440 Type of Recruitment External Position Title COORDINATOR/STUDY ABROAD Position Summary Under the general direction of the Director of Study Abroad, the Study Abroad Coordinator provides administrative and programmatic support for faculty led study abroad programs. This position assists with program development processes, faculty-led budget tracking, faculty support, faculty-led student inquiries, faculty study abroad proposals, faculty grant applications, and faculty/study advocacy. Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree from an accredited institution. Experience studying, working, or living abroad. Experience providing administrative or program support. Experience with financial tracking, budgeting support, or account reconciliation. Demonstrated strong written and verbal communication skills. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Ability to work effectively with students, faculty, and international partners Preferred Qualifications Experience working in international education, study abroad administration, or higher education. Experience using study abroad management systems such as Terra Dotta or Via Global TRM . Experience advising students or supporting academic programs. Duties & Responsibilities Program Development Support: Assists the Director with coordinating the faculty led study abroad program proposal process. Communicates with international partners and program providers regarding program logistics, documentation, collection of invoices, and contractual materials as directed by the Director. Communicates with faculty updates on program logistics, safety, and university policy updates as directed by the Director. Program Budget Coordination: Monitors program related purchasing activity, including faculty purchasing card charges associated with faculty led programs. Tracks purchases and assists with reconciliation. Assists faculty in understanding allowable program expenses and procedures related to program cash advances. Student Advocacy and Outreach: Advises student\u2019s general inquiries into faculty-led study abroad programs. Assists students with the application process. Maintains communication with participating students throughout the application and pre departure process. Participates in outreach, marketing, and promotion of study abroad opportunities. Assists with planning the annual Study Abroad Fair. Administrative Coordination: Coordinates the online application process using Via TRM Global software. Maintains and updates program information related to faculty led programs for the website, Via TRM Global, and printed materials. Maintains annual participation statistics and reporting related to faculty led study abroad programs. Additional Responsibilities: Supports Office of Global Engagement initiatives related to campus internationalization. Performs other duties as assigned. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. For best consideration, please submit application materials on or before Monday, October 26, 2026. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $45,000 - $55,000 Division Academic Affairs Department Global Engagement Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.00 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as required. Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a bachelor's degree from an accredited institution? Yes No * Do you have experience studying, working or living abroad? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents List of References Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45502": {"title": "DIRECTOR / ACADEMIC &amp; PROFESSIONAL PROGRAMS", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | DIRECTOR / ACADEMIC &amp; PROFESSIONAL PROGRAMS Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. DIRECTOR / ACADEMIC & PROFESSIONAL PROGRAMS Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3945 Position Number 70240 Type of Recruitment External Position Title DIRECTOR / ACADEMIC & PROFESSIONAL PROGRAMS Position Summary The director of academic and professional programs within the CMU Online department provides administrative oversite for undergraduate interdisciplinary academic degree programs and certificates, delivered online and at distance. The director is responsible for leading the effort to craft a strategic vision for prior learning credit initiatives, facilitating communication between main campus, faculty, staff, and those involved with the delivery of programs via CMU Online. The director also provides updates to the curriculum, reviews policies and procedures, seeks new opportunities for expansion, and optimizes effectiveness. The director oversees the academic operations of degrees and certificates including admissions, curriculum development, interdisciplinary council, collaborations among campus departments, student learning outcomes assessment, program review, resolution of student issues, and faculty approvals. Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree from an accredited institution. Three years of experience in higher education as a faculty member and/or administrator. Demonstrated experience with at distance program delivery, online course delivery, and educational programming for the adult and post-traditional learner. Demonstrated experience with curriculum development. Excellent communication skills and demonstrated leadership ability with various populations. Strong track record of facilitating collaboration and creativity. Preferred Qualifications Doctoral degree. Five years of experience in higher education as a faculty member and/or administrator. Demonstrated experience leading strategic planning, substantive and decisive evaluation of academic programs, learning outcomes assessment and accreditation, developing interdisciplinary programs and the application of new technologies. Demonstrated experience with supervision of faculty and staff. Demonstrated experience working with adult learners and business and community partners. Knowledge of relevant admission procedures at the undergraduate and graduate level. Duties & Responsibilities Provides academic oversite of certificates, undergraduate majors, and program(s), including admissions and operational support. Responsible for learning outcomes assessments for certificates and degrees within the academic portfolio. Evaluates curriculum and directs the development of new coursework, certificates, majors, and programs as needed. Leads initiatives to optimize the learning experience for online and at distance students. Identifies, evaluates, and develops innovative forms of academic delivery. Reviews marketing materials, webpages, and the Bulletin copy within the academic portfolio. Develops the yearly strategic enrollment plan for all programs within the academic portfolio. Facilitates communication between academic departments, faculty, and staff involved with the coordination and delivery of programs within the academic portfolio through CMU Online. Works with the Business and Community Outreach team to develop custom training programs and pipelines for regional employers. Represents programs within the academic portfolio through participation on various councils and committees at the university. Analyzes data to monitor student stop outs and implement intervention strategies. Manages executed articulation agreements, affiliation agreements, and memorandums of understanding/agreement with external partners. Reviews and recommends policies and procedures for efficiencies and effectiveness for programs within the academic portfolio. Assists with the identification and implementation of professional development activities and creating annual goals for noncredit programming, micro-credentials, and badges. Collaborates on strategic endeavors to increase enrollment for certificates and degrees within the academic portfolio. Oversees budget development and provides support for program financial activities to ensure compliance with college and university policies and procedures. Responsible for the academic program review process which occurs every seven years. Works jointly with the Office of Licensure, Regulatory Services, and Human Capital to manage the licensure, compliance, and regulation related to the academic portfolio. Oversees the hiring, training, development, and evaluation of professional and support staff. Performs other duties as assigned. Supervision Exercised Supervisors are expected to support the Leadership Standards of Central Michigan University and foster a culture that inspires excellence. The Leadership Standards define how we lead and treat others on our team. As leaders, it is our responsibility to seek input from our teams to continuously improve our leadership abilities and our demonstration of the standards. Additionally, it is our responsibility to encourage and support the growth and development of those whom we lead. At CMU , we encourage employees to grow both personally and professionally, and thus advance CMU\u2019s culture of excellence. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $80,000 - $95,000 per year Division Academic Affairs Department Academic and Professional Programs Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.00 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Supervisors are expected to support the Leadership Standards of Central Michigan University and foster a culture that inspires excellence. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position and click \u201cYes\u201d if you understand and support the culture that is important to CMU. Yes No * Do you have a Master\u2019s degree from an accredited institution? Yes No * Do you have at least three years of experience working in higher education as a faculty member and/or administrator? Yes No * Do you have experience with at-a-distance program delivery, online course delivery, and educational programming for the adult and post-traditional learner? Yes No * Do you have experience with curriculum development? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents List of References Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45216": {"title": "CUSTODIAN TEMPORARY (PART-TIME)", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | CUSTODIAN TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. CUSTODIAN TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3820 Position Number 99999 Type of Recruitment External Position Title CUSTODIAN TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Position Summary Temporary custodian positions. No benefits. A custodian is the key University and Facilities Management person in maintaining cleanliness of academic, residential, and administrative campus buildings and service areas. Performs manual custodial tasks in care of University buildings; performs related work as required. Required Qualifications High School education or equivalent. Possession of a valid Michigan driver\u2019s license may be required. Working knowledge of cleaning materials and methods. Demonstrated ability to follow and/or interpret verbal and/or written directions. Demonstrated positive interpersonal skills. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively and project a positive image. Ability to perform the essential functions and requirements of the job. Preferred Qualifications Duties & Responsibilities Operates mechanical cleaning and scrubbing equipment. Operates carpet shampooing and upholstery cleaning equipment. Sweeps, mops, strips, and waxes floor surfaces. Maintains entrances and areas surrounding buildings by picking up litter, cigarette butts, sweeping, shoveling snow, removing ice, spreading sand and salt, etc. Operates vacuum cleaning equipment. Cleans and waxes furniture, cases, fixtures and furnishings. Cleans mirrors and interior glass. Unplugs commodes, urinals, and sink drains without dismantling the fixture. Cleans restrooms and replenishes restroom supplies. Spot washes walls. Makes beds and changes linens in guest rooms. Collects and disposes of waste materials. Reports repair work and/or damages to the building. Sweeps, dusts, and wet-mops stairs and stairwells. Replaces light bulbs and broken globes as needed. Moves and arranges furniture and furnishings. Washes interior and exterior windows. Empties all trash containers and removes to pick-up stations. Keeps routine records and makes routine reports. Supervision Exercised Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Employee Group Temporary Staff Staff Pay Level Pay Range $15.81 per hour Division Finance and Administrative Services Department Facilities Management Position Status Temporary Position End Date Employment Status Part-Time FTE 0.00 Position Type Other Weekly Work Schedule Varies based on assignment; full-time hours available for summer assignments only Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a high school diploma or GED? Yes No * Do you have at least one year of work experience? Yes No * Do you possess a valid driver's license? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45553": {"title": "ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR / ONLINE STUDENT SERVICES", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR / ONLINE STUDENT SERVICES Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR / ONLINE STUDENT SERVICES Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3988 Position Number 78880 Type of Recruitment External Position Title ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR / ONLINE STUDENT SERVICES Position Summary The associate director of CMU Online Student Services provides operational leadership for student support and engagement services throughout the online student lifecycle. Under the direction of the executive director of Online Student Services, the associate director recruits, hires, develops, and manages a team of assistant directors who support CMU Online students throughout their educational journey. The associate director leads efforts that advance recruitment, enrollment, retention, persistence, and student success by ensuring effective service delivery, communication, and coordination. The position serves as a liaison between the student services team and university partners, fostering collaboration and alignment of services and initiatives. The associate director also monitors and reports student services data and analytics to assess performance, identify opportunities for improvement, and inform unit strategies and decision-making. Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s Degree. Three years of progressively responsible professional experience in higher education, student services, enrollment management, recruitment, advising, or a related area. Demonstrated experience supervising, training, coaching, or leading professional staff, including the ability to support staff development and performance. Demonstrated experience engaging, qualifying, and motivating prospective students and conducting proactive outreach to support student retention, persistence, and success. Demonstrated understanding of the student journey from recruitment through enrollment, engagement, retention, persistence, and completion. Established analytical and data-informed decision-making skills, including the ability to monitor, evaluate, interpret, and report data to inform goals, initiatives, and continuous improvement. Demonstrated ability to provide professional, positive, and exceptional customer service while working effectively as a collaborative team member. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities, balance competing demands, organize work, and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Ability to effectively manage and adapt to change, implement new processes and initiatives, and support others through organizational and operational transitions. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in business administration, educational administration, organizational leadership, higher education administration, or a related field. Demonstrated experience working with student information systems and related technology platforms, such as Slate, SAP , or comparable systems. Demonstrated experience supporting adult, nontraditional, and/or online students in a higher education environment. Duties & Responsibilities Works in collaboration with the executive director of online student services to develop, implement, and evaluate processes, procedures, and service models that promote best practices and support student recruitment, retention, engagement, and success. Provides administrative leadership in the hiring, onboarding, training, supervision, and development of assigned staff. Establishes, monitors, and evaluates team and program goals aligned with CMU Online priorities, using data and performance measures to track progress, identify opportunities, and drive continuous improvement. Serves as a primary liaison to assigned colleges, academic departments, and academic programs, providing data, analytics, enrollment reports, and presentations to support recruitment, enrollment, retention, and programmatic decision-making. Provides administrative leadership in addressing complex, sensitive, or escalated student and departmental matters, coordinating with appropriate stakeholders to facilitate timely and effective resolutions. Collaborates closely with CMU Online and university partners, including academic advisors, to improve student pathways, enhance the student experience, and support strategic enrollment and student success goals. Represents CMU Online Student Services on university committees, workgroups, and cross-functional initiatives, contributing expertise, advancing unit priorities, and fostering collaboration in support of institutional goals. Provides administrative oversight of the daily operations of the student services team, ensuring effective workflows, consistent service delivery, appropriate use of university systems and applications, and adherence to established policies and procedures. Provides applicable support as team liaison for admissions or retention and student success CRM platforms, collaborating with appropriate stakeholders to support system functionality, processes, and effective use to advance admissions and enrollment objectives. Represents CMU Online at recruitment, enrollment, retention, and student engagement events and outreach activities, as needed. Performs other duties as assigned. Supervision Exercised Supervisors are expected to support the Leadership Standards of Central Michigan University and foster a culture that inspires excellence. The Leadership Standards define how we lead and treat others on our team. As leaders, it is our responsibility to seek input from our teams to continuously improve our leadership abilities and our demonstration of the standards. Additionally, it is our responsibility to encourage and support the growth and development of those whom we lead. At CMU , we encourage employees to grow both personally and professionally, and thus advance CMU\u2019s culture of excellence. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $60,000 - $72,000 per year Division Academic Affairs Department CMU Online Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.00 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends O