idland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled No Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Please indicate the highest level of education you have achieved. High School diploma Associate's degree Bachelor's degree Master's degree Terminal degree * How many years of related experience do you have? None Less than 1 year 1-3 years 4-5 years 6+ years * What type of work are you interested in? (Open Ended Question) Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45618": {"title": "PROJECT MANAGER I/II/III/SR (3 POSITIONS)", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | PROJECT MANAGER I/II/III/SR (3 POSITIONS) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. PROJECT MANAGER I/II/III/SR (3 POSITIONS) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Applicants are strongly encouraged to submit letters of recommendation. If you wish to include recommendation letter(s) that are not required, please utilize the Recommendation Letters upload field. If there is another applicable document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the Other Document (1) upload field. If there is an applicable certification document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the 'Certification' upload field. * This is a hybrid position with both remote and on-campus responsibilities. The position is expected to work on the Mount Pleasant campus a minimum of three days per week. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3970 Position Number 72815, 72825, 72835 Type of Recruitment External Position Title PROJECT MANAGER I/II/III/SR (3 POSITIONS) Position Summary The project manager is responsible for planning, organizing, and overseeing projects to ensure they are completed on time, within scope, and within budget. This role involves collaboration with cross-functional teams, stakeholders, and university departments to deliver projects that support the university\u2019s strategic objectives. The level of the position (I, II, III , or Senior) reflects the scope of projects managed, years of experience required, and level of autonomy in performing tasks. Required Qualifications Project Manager I: High school diploma or GED . One year of increasingly responsible work experience in project coordination or management. Basic project management skills, effective communication, attention to detail, and proficiency in project management tools. Ability to plan and organize the phasing of development projects of small to medium size and duration. Listening, facilitation, negotiation, and conflict resolution skills. Analytical and problem-solving skills. Competency in Microsoft applications including Word, Excel, and Outlook. Ability to support small-scale projects with guidance from senior staff. Project Manager II: Possess all of the required qualifications of a Project Manager I, plus: Bachelor\u2019s degree or a combination of education and experience that equates to four years. Four additional years of project management experience, preferably in a higher education environment. Ability to independently manage multiple medium-scale/complexity projects, with knowledge of risk management and resource allocation. Project Manager III : Possess all of the required qualifications of a Project Manager II, plus: Four additional years of project management experience, including large, complex projects. Advanced project management skills, including budget management, strategic planning, and change management. Ability to lead large-scale, high-impact projects. Senior Project Manager: Possess all of the required qualifications of a Project Manager III , plus: Four additional years of project management experience, with a strong track record of delivering multi-departmental or enterprise-level projects. Exceptional leadership, strategic thinking, and stakeholder management skills. Expertise in managing complex portfolios and high-level initiatives. Ability to oversee the most critical and strategic projects that carry significant impact on the university. Preferred Qualifications Proficiency in project management software (Team Dynamix, MS Project, Trello). Familiarity with university environments and processes. PMP certification or progress toward PMP certification. Knowledge of the BABOK\u00ae Guide and the Agile Extension to the BABOK\u00ae Guide. Training and certification or progress toward certification in Agile approaches and techniques. Demonstrated experience in modeling notation and flowcharting. Ability to break-down complex business scenarios or problems into process and data models. Demonstrated track record of successful business analysis, design, and management of optimized processes, projects, and programs in a complex workforce environment. Demonstrated knowledge of the SDLC and Agile methodologies. Demonstrated experience with processes for contract work and vended solutions. Duties & Responsibilities Project Manager I: Defines project scope, objectives, and deliverables. Develops detailed project plans, including timelines, resources, and budgets. Ensures adherence to project management methodologies and university policies. Acts as a liaison between departments, faculty, and external vendors. Communicates project updates, risks, and solutions effectively. Identifies potential risks and develops mitigation strategies. Monitors project progress and resolves issues as they arise. Maintains accurate project documentation and records. Prepares reports for leadership and stakeholders. Performs other duties as assigned. Project Manager II: Performs all duties and responsibilities of the Project Manager I, plus: Manages multiple concurrent projects that are longer in term, greater in complexity, and medium to large in size, scope, budget, and/or impact. Supports the achievement of business objectives and goals and satisfaction of business needs by coordinating, implementing, managing, measuring, and monitoring the effectiveness of projects. Project Manager III : Performs all duties and responsibilities of the Project Manager II, plus: Leads large, high complexity programs consisting of multiple high- complexity projects. Provides direction, monitoring, training, coaching, and mentoring, and will possibly assign work to, other project managers. Engages with leadership on continuous project/program management process improvements. Engages with relevant University departments in the submission of RFQs/RFPs for contract work and vended solutions. Oversees project teams or mentors junior staff as requested. Senior Project Manager: Performs all duties and responsibilities of the Project Manager III , plus: Oversees the project portfolio of all projects, programs, and operations to achieve strategic objectives. Champions strong governance in the portfolio and project management framework. Leads and manages business system and process development for multiple, concurrent, complex programs and initiatives. Works with other project managers, providing direction, monitoring work, and training. Ensures alignment of large-scale initiatives with relevant enterprise considerations where applicable. Manages multiple project managers or project teams as requested. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Applicants are strongly encouraged to submit letters of recommendation. If you wish to include recommendation letter(s) that are not required, please utilize the Recommendation Letters upload field. If there is another applicable document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the Other Document (1) upload field. If there is an applicable certification document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the \u2018Certification\u2019 upload field. * This is a hybrid position with both remote and on-campus responsibilities. The position is expected to work on the Mount Pleasant campus a minimum of three days per week. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $52,000 - $92,000 per year (based on level) Division President Department University Transformation Office Position Status Provisional Position End Date 09/30/2031 Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI* About the Department Central Michigan University is engaged in a multi-year enterprise resource planning ( ERP ) transformation initiative. This provisional position has been established to support the successful implementation of the selected ERP solution and ensuring coverage for other University Transformation Office initiatives. About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Will you now or at any time in the future require CMU to file or support an immigration petition or application in order to begin or continue your employment authorization? Yes No * Do you have a high school diploma or GED? Yes No * Do you have at least one year of increasingly responsible work experience in project coordination or management? Yes No * Do you have experience implementing or supporting an ERP implementation (Yes/No)? If yes, please briefly explain your role. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have any project management training or certifications (PMP, Scrum Master, etc.) (Yes/No)? If yes, please explain. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have any change management training or certifications (Prosci Certified Change Practitioner, etc.) (Yes/No)? If yes, please explain. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have any business process analysis training or certifications (Six Sigma, etc.) (Yes/No)? If yes, please explain. (Open Ended Question) Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Recommendation Letters Other Document (1) Certification Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45590": {"title": "Assistant Dean, Faculty Development (Medical Faculty, Associate Professor/Professor)", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | Assistant Dean, Faculty Development (Medical Faculty, Associate Professor/Professor) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. Assistant Dean, Faculty Development (Medical Faculty, Associate Professor/Professor) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. To review Covenant HealthCare College of Medicine at Central Michigan University rank criteria please review the Faculty Appointment Manual . Position Information Position Information Posting Number F-1067 Position Title Assistant Dean, Faculty Development (Medical Faculty, Associate Professor/Professor) College/Unit College of Medicine Home Department Covenant HealthCare College of Medicine at Central Michigan University Employee Group Medical Faculty Employment Status Full-Time Position Type 12 month Position Classification Medical Faculty Position Begin Date Position End Date Position Summary The Assistant Dean for Faculty Development provides strategic leadership for faculty development initiatives that support the Covenant HealthCare College of Medicine at Central Michigan University\u2019s mission and priorities. This role oversees faculty development efforts for educators of medical students and residents and works closely with the Associate Deans for Pre-Clerkship and Clerkship Education to design, develop, implement, and evaluate programs aligned with the college\u2019s institutional goals and strategic initiatives. The Assistant Dean supports faculty in strengthening their individual interests and talents in ways that advance the educational, research, clinical, and service missions of both the faculty and the college. The role also serves as a key resource for discipline chairs as they mentor faculty through appointment, reappointment, promotion, and tenure across all academic ranks and tracks, and advises the Senior Associate Dean of Academic Affairs on best practices related to these policies and processes. In addition, the Assistant Dean oversees the development of educational initiatives such as courses, programs, workshops, seminars, and individualized consultation and mentorship opportunities that foster faculty growth as educators, scholars, and leaders. Required Qualifications Doctoral degree (e.g., PhD, MD/DO, EdD). Meets criteria for Associate Professor or Professor rank at CMU College of Medicine. Demonstrated experience in the areas of faulty development in an academic setting. Strong collaborative of interprofessional education. Established credentials and experience in medical education, leadership, and/or administration. Experience in the professional development and mentoring of medical school faculty. A record of scholarly activity with the expectation of continued scholarly activity preferably in educational research, but other areas will be considered. Successful attainment of extramural funding. Experience in health professions education and commitment to innovative approaches to advancement of educational pedagogies and learning. Ability to facilitate interactive learning in large and small group settings. Demonstrated commitment to ensuring members of the university community can thrive. Ability to perform the essential functions of the job with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Qualifications Experience providing effective faculty development programming within a distributed clinical educational model and across health systems. Experience with, or a strong knowledge of, pedagogical approaches such as problem and team-based and peer instruction. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. To review Covenant HealthCare College of Medicine at Central Michigan University rank criteria please review the Faculty Appointment Manual . About the Department The Covenant HealthCare College of Medicine at Central Michigan University educates diverse students and trains culturally competent physicians to provide comprehensive health care and services to underserved populations in Michigan and beyond. Our faculty, staff and graduates advance health and wellness through exceptional education, innovative research, quality patientcare and strategic collaborations to improve the health and well-being of individuals and communities. For more information please visit our website. Posting Begins 10/12/2026 Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Type of Recruitment External About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this vacancy? Please indicate the specific source by title (i.e., CMU website, HigherEdJobs.com, Higher Education Recruitment Consortium, The Chronicle, specific professional association, specific list serv, etc.): (Open Ended Question) Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Other Document (1) Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45458": {"title": "Speech-Language Pathology (Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor)", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | Speech-Language Pathology (Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. Speech-Language Pathology (Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Applications will begin to be reviewed on November 9, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number F-1055 Position Title Speech-Language Pathology (Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor) College/Unit The Herbert H. and Grace A. Dow College of Health Professions Home Department Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders Employee Group Tenure-Track Faculty - Academic Year Employment Status Full-Time Position Type 10 month Position Classification Tenure Track Faculty Position Begin Date 08/23/2027 Position End Date Position Summary The Speech-Language Pathology Division in the Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders at Central Michigan University ( CMU ) is recruiting for one full-time, 10-month tenure-track Assistant Professor, with a start date of August 23, 2027. The CMU Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders offers undergraduate and graduate degrees and is housed within The Herbert H. and Grace A. Dow College of Health Professions. Starting salary is commensurate with qualifications and experience. Attractive benefits package and research support are available. Required Qualifications Earned terminal doctorate degree is required; ABD will be considered if it is clear the degree will be completed by start of appointment. CCC - SLP is required. Licensed as an SLP in Michigan or eligible for MI licensure. Expertise in one or more of the following areas: dysphagia, motor speech, voice, cognition, medical speech-language pathology, or other related research areas. Effective oral/written communication skills. Demonstrated research agenda based on published works and/or external funding or potential for success. Ability to perform the essential functions of the job with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Qualifications Clinical supervision experience. Experience teaching at the university level. Experience or demonstrated interest in securing extramural grants and contracts. Evidence of involvement with professional associations and organizations. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Applications will begin to be reviewed on November 9, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. About the Department The Herbert H. and Grace A. Dow College of Health Professions consists of five academic units (Department of Physical Therapy, Department of Physical Education and Sport, Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders, the School of Health Sciences, and the School of Rehabilitation and Medical Sciences). It offers undergraduate and/or graduate degree programs in athletic training, audiology, communication sciences and disorders, exercise science, environmental health and safety, health administration, physical activity specialist, physical education, physical therapy, physician assistant, public health, school and public health education, speech-language pathology, and sport management, delivered by 100+ faculty/staff. For more information, CMU\u2019s website is http://www.cmich.edu , the Herbert H. and Grace A. Dow College of Health Professions website is http://www.chp.cmich.edu , and the Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders website is Communication Sciences and Disorders | College of Health Professions . Posting Begins 09/10/2026 Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Type of Recruitment External About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this vacancy? Please indicate the specific source by title (i.e., CMU website, HigherEdJobs.com, Higher Education Recruitment Consortium, The Chronicle, specific professional association, specific list serv, etc.): (Open Ended Question) Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research Certification List of References Optional Documents Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness Writing Sample Transcript Copies Personal Statement Other Document (1) Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45550": {"title": "SENIOR ENERGY FACILITY OPERATOR", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | SENIOR ENERGY FACILITY OPERATOR Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. SENIOR ENERGY FACILITY OPERATOR Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. If there is another applicable document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the Other Document (1) upload field. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3848 Position Number 42440 Type of Recruitment External Position Title SENIOR ENERGY FACILITY OPERATOR Position Summary Performs skilled work in the operation and maintenance of high pressure steam boilers, steam absorption and centrifugal chillers, air conditioning cooling towers, steam, diesel and gas turbine driven generators, air compressors, pumps, and related work as required. Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED . Completion of a formal apprentice program of a qualifying nature or equivalent training and experience. Possession of a valid driver\u2019s license. Ability to work from blueprints, diagrams, and sketches. Demonstrated ability to follow and/or interpret oral or written directions. Demonstrated positive interpersonal skills. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively and project a positive image. Ability to perform the essential functions and requirements of the job. Preferred Qualifications Duties & Responsibilities Operates with automated and manual controls high pressure steam boilers to maintain campus demand for steam. Performs maintenance on boilers, chillers, generators, cooling towers, steam traps, and related pumps. Maintain cleanliness of the Central Energy Facility. Maintain telephone and radio contact with campus and outside vendors and contractors as necessary. Keeps necessary operating records and logs. Performs touch up painting on equipment, pipes, floors, and walls. Performs minor carpentry work. Operates with automated and manual controls absorption and centrifugal chillers to maintain campus demand for chilled water. Operates diesel, steam, and gas turbine driven generators. Operates and maintains cooling towers. Performs preventative maintenance and lubricates Central Energy Facilities equipment. Monitors campus energy management system. Operates water treatment equipment and takes water tests as prescribed by supervisor. Maintains steam distribution and condensate return system in distribution tunnels. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. If there is another applicable document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the Other Document (1) upload field. Employee Group Service Maintenance Staff Pay Level 11 Pay Range $38.08 per hour (non-negotiable) / + recruitment bonus (and moving expense reimbursement, if applicable) Division Finance and Administrative Services Department Utility Operations Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule 12 Hour Rotating shifts; rotating days/nights - 30 day cycle, every other weekend off Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have a high school diploma or GED? Yes No * Have you completed a formal apprentice program of a qualifying nature or do you have equivalent training and experience? Yes No * Do you have a valid Driver's License? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document (1) Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/44740": {"title": "VICE PRES/RESEARCH &amp; SPONSORED PROGRAMS", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | VICE PRES/RESEARCH &amp; SPONSORED PROGRAMS Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. VICE PRES/RESEARCH & SPONSORED PROGRAMS Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. Greenwood Asher & Associates is assisting Central Michigan University in this search. Applications and nominations are now being accepted. Please submit resume and cover letter to one of the e-mails listed below: Jim Johnsen, Ed.D., Vice President of Executive Search jimjohnsen@greenwoodsearch.com Ann Bailey, Ph.D. Senior Executive Search Consultant annbailey@greenwoodsearch.com Submission of resume and cover letter as PDF attachments is strongly encouraged. The search will be conducted with a commitment to confidentiality for candidates until finalists are selected. Initial screening of applications will begin immediately and will continue until an appointment is made. Nominations and inquiries should be directed to: Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3861 Position Number 69780 Type of Recruitment External Position Title VICE PRES/RESEARCH & SPONSORED PROGRAMS Position Summary Central Michigan University ( CMU ) is classified as a Carnegie Research 2 (R2): High Research Spending and Doctorate Production institution, with high research activity and doctoral education. The Vice President for Research and Sponsored Programs ( VPRSP ) reports to the Provost/Executive Vice President and provides senior leadership across the university to develop and implement a clear vision for advancing and strengthening CMU\u2019s research enterprise. As a senior member of the university\u2019s leadership team, the VPRSP advises institutional leadership on research strategy, policy, investment, and risk, and represents CMU internally and externally on matters related to research, scholarship, creative work, and innovation. The VPRSP cultivates a strong culture of scholarship, creative work, research, development, and innovation; advances institutionally aligned, interdisciplinary, and community-engaged research initiatives; expands strategic research initiatives and partnerships; and further develops the university\u2019s infrastructure and administrative support for research and compliance in ways that enable institutional growth. The VPRSP provides leadership for the Office of Research and Sponsored Programs, which includes Research Compliance, Laboratory and Field Safety, and Animal Facilities (vivaria), and encompasses functions pertaining to sponsored programs, partnerships, intellectual property and technology transfer, human subjects research, biosafety, and export control. The VPRSP ensures these functions operate in a coordinated and efficient manner that supports responsible growth in research activity. Required Qualifications Doctorate or equivalent combined with an academic record sufficient to be granted advanced rank and tenure in one of the university\u2019s academic departments. Five years of successful leadership experience in research administration within a large, complex organization, preferably in a public research university setting. Demonstrated record of significant scholarship, research, or creative activity, including success in securing external funding. Demonstrated ability to facilitate and attract support for research, scholarship, and creative works\u2014from the public and private sectors\u2014 consistent with the expectations of a university fully engaged in both graduate and undergraduate education. Demonstrated ability to supervise and support the growth of a professional staff. Demonstrated commitment to ensuring that all members of the university community can thrive. Experience developing and supporting innovation through intellectual property, tech transfer, commercialization, and related activities. Commitment to research and creative activities as a core component of the academic enterprise and the ability to engage the entire institution around research, creative activities, and innovation to advance the university\u2019s mission. Experience in overseeing compliance programs including, but not limited to, human subject research, animal research, biosafety, and export controls. Experience in building collaborations with public and private sector organizations, higher education systems, and leaders and organizations in the community, region, and state. Understanding the needs of faculty from early career to senior level and to effectively support their research, creative activities, and innovation goals and objectives. Demonstrated ability to build positive, respectful relationships and communicate effectively\u2014both verbally and in writing\u2014with people from a wide range of backgrounds, identities, and perspectives. Demonstrated experience in the procurement and management of sponsored research programs. Demonstrated understanding of federal, state and regional funding agencies and mechanisms. Experience in research policy development and implementation. Proven ability to foster collaboration and bring together investigators across disciplines to develop large-scale research initiatives that foster a clear and compelling funding opportunity. Demonstrated ability to interpret and implement effective budgeting and fiscal management. Demonstrated experience working with senior-level leaders to advance institutional research and strategic initiatives. Preferred Qualifications Experience leading complex academic or industry organizations as a vice president, dean, or comparable senior leader. Training or certification in grants management, research administration,and other relevant specialties. Experience supporting proposals in medical research and clinical trials. Demonstrated ability to maintain research productivity under fluctuating budgets and funding levels. Demonstrate success in supporting and leading institution-wide, multidisciplinary research initiatives that align with strategic priorities. Duties & Responsibilities Supports the Leadership Standards of CMU and fosters a culture that inspires excellence. Provides strategic leadership to advance, expand, and elevate CMU\u2019s research, scholarly, creative, and innovate enterprise to align with strategic priorities. Facilitates and supports research, scholarship, and creative works consistent with the expectations of a Carnegie Research 2 (R2) institution engaged in significant graduate and undergraduate education. Leads efforts to engage on and off-campus communities to promote research and creative opportunities for faculty and students. Serves as the Research Integrity Officer ( RIO ) for CMU , responsible for the coordination and implementation of the university\u2019s Research Integrity and Misconduct Policy, compliance with federal and state research-misconduct regulations, and ensures that all allegations of research misconduct are promptly and fairly assessed and investigated in accordance with federal standards. Assists in the development and distribution of training on research ethics and integrity and regulatory requirements and serves as a liaison to external funding agencies and oversight bodies. Provides leadership and oversight to the Offices of Research Compliance and Laboratory and Field Safety and ensures university compliance with all federal and state guidelines and regulations related to research. Enhances and strengthens the infrastructure and organizational support required to enable increased research and creative endeavor activity, external funding, and technology transfer at CMU , enabling it to be capable of handling significant fluctuations in research activity and funding. Engages government agencies, foundations, and other public and private partners to proactively identify and promote public and private research funding opportunities. Collaborates with the CMU Research Corporation in creating a hub for innovation to enable and support entrepreneurial activity based on CMU intellectual property and expertise, including the tech transfer process. Advances innovation and translational activity through effective support for intellectual property creation, technology transfer, commercialization and related activities as well as experience in securing and managing sponsored research programs. Acts as an advocate by cultivating a research ecosystem that reduces barriers to participation and success, supports investigators across disciplines and career stages, and enhances access to resources, guidance, and opportunities that advance scholarly, creative, and sponsored research. Collaborates with and brings investigators together to conceptualize and develop large-scale, multidisciplinary research initiatives and translates them into compelling funding requests. Supervision Exercised Supervisors are expected to support the Leadership Standards of Central Michigan University and foster a culture that inspires excellence. The Leadership Standards define how we lead and treat others on our team. As leaders, it is our responsibility to seek input from our teams to continuously improve our leadership abilities and our demonstration of the standards. Additionally, it is our responsibility to encourage and support the growth and development of those whom we lead. At CMU , we encourage employees to grow both personally and professionally, and thus advance CMU\u2019s culture of excellence. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. Greenwood Asher & Associates is assisting Central Michigan University in this search. Applications and nominations are now being accepted. Please submit resume and cover letter to one of the e-mails listed below: Jim Johnsen, Ed.D., Vice President of Executive Search jimjohnsen@greenwoodsearch.com Ann Bailey, Ph.D. Senior Executive Search Consultant annbailey@greenwoodsearch.com Submission of resume and cover letter as PDF attachments is strongly encouraged. The search will be conducted with a commitment to confidentiality for candidates until finalists are selected. Initial screening of applications will begin immediately and will continue until an appointment is made. Nominations and inquiries should be directed to: Employee Group Senior Officer Staff Pay Level Pay Range Division Academic Affairs Department RESEARCH & SPONSORED PROGRAMS Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Typically Mon-Fri 8-5; evenings and weekends as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45594": {"title": "ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT II/PT", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT II/PT Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT II/PT Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3953 Position Number 78390 Type of Recruitment External Position Title ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT II/PT Position Summary Works in a team environment to schedule appointments and perform all check-in processes accurately and appropriately for all CMU Health Services patients (multiple clinics, multiple providers). Enters medical insurance and demographic information into the electronic medical record. Collects copays and past due balances. Performs daily reconciliation and reporting of payments. Stays current on basic health insurance specifics, guidelines, and rules. Maintains the confidentiality, security, and organization of CMU Health Services medical records. Releases patient information as appropriate following HIPAA and FERPA guidelines. Performs a variety of basic office duties. Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED . Three years of qualifying experience or a combination of education and experience that equates to three years. Experience with Microsoft Word. Customer service experience. Organizational skills with strong attention to detail. Demonstrated positive interpersonal skills. Effective verbal and written communication skills. Ability to project a positive attitude. Ability to manage multiple projects and meet deadlines with accurate results. Ability to compose, proofread and edit correspondence. Preferred Qualifications Associates degree in medical office secretarial or similar program Experience with electronic medical record systems and scanners Knowledge of SAP Knowledge of Epic ( EMR ) Experience using website resources such as WebDennis, Champs, etc Duties & Responsibilities Monitors and manages medical clinic schedules for multiple Providers according to Provider specifics and availability. Schedules patient appointments for all CMU Clinics while following all scheduling guidelines. Obtains insurance and demographic information and enters it into the electronic medical record with high accuracy. Verifies insurance coverage and policy information using various insurance company websites (Web Dennis, Champs, etc). Maintains basic knowledge regarding CMU medical insurance participation, insurance guidelines and pre-authorization processes. Completes all check-in processes, collection processes and reconciliation processes with a high degree of accuracy. Answers phones, transfers calls, prepares/changes voice mail and triage messages. Acts as the medical records custodian, releasing information as appropriate following HIPAA and FERPA guidelines. Participates in team workflow and other problem-solving initiatives for efficiency and effectiveness. Participates in training of new employees/student workers on electronic medical record and general office processes and procedures. Participates in regular communication with clinical staff and billing staff to help ensure efficient workflow between departments. Provides input for development and implementation of procedures, systems, and policies as it relates to the revenue cycle. Assists in supervision and assists in providing direction to student employees. Completes all medical record scanning and copying. Composes and mails various office correspondence. Supports and assists with scheduling of incoming and outgoing referrals. Performs other duties as assigned. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Employee Group Administrative Office Assistant Staff Pay Level Pay Range Minimum Starting Rate: $16.60 per hour Division Academic Affairs Department University Health Services Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Part-Time FTE 0.60 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule 24 hours per week (desired schedule MWF) Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a high school diploma or GED? Yes No * Do you have three years of qualifying experience or a combination of education and experience that equates to three years? Yes No * Do you have experience with Microsoft Word? Yes No * Do you have customer service experience? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents List of References Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45479": {"title": "Physical Therapy Instructor/Regional Clinical Coordinator", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | Physical Therapy Instructor/Regional Clinical Coordinator Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. Physical Therapy Instructor/Regional Clinical Coordinator Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled, although priority consideration will be given to applications completed by October 30, 2026. Applications must be submitted through an online process beginning at www.jobs.cmich.edu . Electronically attach a cover letter, Curriculum Vitae/Resume, and three professional references with contact information, including telephone numbers and e-mail addresses. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number F-1052 Position Title Physical Therapy Instructor/Regional Clinical Coordinator College/Unit The Herbert H. and Grace A. Dow College of Health Professions Home Department Department of Physical Therapy Employee Group Fixed-Term Faculty - Academic Year Employment Status Part-Time Position Type 9 month (Academic Year) Position Classification Fixed-Term Faculty Position Begin Date 01/07/2027 Position End Date Position Summary The Department of Physical Therapy at Central Michigan University invite applications for a 10-month, part-time, fixed-term position at the rank of instructor. The Department of Physical Therapy seeks a faculty member with experience in clinical education and didactic teaching for a Regional Clinical Coordinator ( RCC ) position. This faculty position has administrative and academic responsibilities consistent with the mission and philosophy of the academic program. As a member of the clinical education team, the primary responsibilities of the RCC are to coordinate, facilitate, and monitor the learning experiences of students participating in external clinical affiliation education experiences. The clinical education team includes the Director of Clinical Education, three additional RCCs, and a support staff member. This RCC position will primarily provide supervision and service for students assigned to clinical partners in the northern Lower Peninsula of Michigan and the Upper Peninsula of Michigan requiring significant travel in the region to visit and support students and clinical faculty at affiliating sites in the specified region. Specific RCC responsibilities include: facilitating quality learning experiences for students within the assigned region; mentoring clinical instructors; providing guidance and support to individual students and clinical instructors as needed; serving as a research advisor for completion of case report requirements; assisting and enhancing students\u2019 ability to problem-solve, critically think and self-reflect through advising and planned assignments during the clinical experience; organize and facilitate meetings for assigned students during the clinical experiences in the regions described above. Occasionally, this RCC will supervise and provide service for students that are assigned to clinical experiences in states other than Michigan. Technology may be used for communication for these agencies during clinical experiences. Responsibilities: Faculty members are expected to demonstrate a commitment to excellence in teaching, student advising. Teaching. Primary teaching responsibilities include students during external clinical experiences. Research. Directing graduate student research primarily in the form of case reports. Service. Involvement in campus, community, and professional service with emphasis on service related to external partnerships for clinical education and students. Clinical Practice . Participation to remain clinically active as a practicing clinician is encouraged as this facilitates knowledge and practice is authentically valuable for mentoring students during their clinical education. This position will begin with the Spring 2027 semester. Some training and orientation may be scheduled prior to the start of the semester to support a smooth transition into the position. Specific arrangements will be discussed with the selected candidate. Required Qualifications Licensed or eligible for physical therapy licensure in Michigan. Doctoral degree in physical therapy or post-physical therapy doctoral degree. Minimum of 5 years\u2019 experience as a licensed physical therapist. Minimum of 5 years\u2019 experience as a clinical instructor (CI) or combination of 5 years\u2019 experience as a CI and/or site coordinator of clinical education ( SCCE ). Adheres to American Physical Therapy Association, American Physical Therapy Association- Michigan\u2019s ethical and legal guidelines of practice. Exhibits current knowledge and skill in physical therapy practice, especially as applicable to clinical education. Entry level knowledge of educational, management, and adult learning theory and principle. Knowledge of case report research including clinical data interpretation, understanding of ethical guidelines, and relevant literature synthesis. Strong communication, organization, interpersonal, problem-solving, teaching, and learning principles. Current knowledge and skill in use of information and computer technology and/or ability to update these skills. Ability to work independently, travel and coordinate work with colleagues, peers, and students. Current valid driver\u2019s license, satisfactory driving record, and transportation for travel requirements. Ability to perform the essential functions of the job with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Qualifications Member of the American Physical Therapy Association and American Physical Therapy Association \u2013 Michigan. Member of the Academy of Education of the American Physical Therapy Association and/or Consortium for Clinical Education of the American Physical Therapy Association of Michigan. American Physical Therapy Association Credentialed Clinical Instructor or intent to pursue credentials. Knowledge of legislative, regulatory, legal and practice issues impacting clinical education, students, and the physical therapy profession. Active professional activities associated with physical therapy at the local, state, and/or national levels. Board certifications in ABPTS recognized specialty or other equivalent certifications (residency/fellowship). Knowledge of hospitals, rehabilitation facilities, and physical therapy practices in either or both Upper Lower Michigan or the Upper Peninsula. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled, although priority consideration will be given to applications completed by October 30, 2026. Applications must be submitted through an online process beginning at www.jobs.cmich.edu . Electronically attach a cover letter, Curriculum Vitae/Resume, and three professional references with contact information, including telephone numbers and e-mail addresses. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. About the Department CMU offers a doctoral degree program in physical therapy ( DPT ) through its Department of Physical Therapy within The Herbert H. and Grace A. Dow College of Health Professions. The Department of Physical Therapy offers a case-orientated curriculum with a mission of preparing knowledgeable, skillful, reflective, and ethical physical therapists who practice with sound clinical reasoning to enhance the health, function, and well-being of their patients, partners, and society. The program has a unique clinical education model which includes a sequence of five clinical education experiences \u2013 two integrated mock clinical experiences and three external full, time clinical education experiences and a clinical education team that works collaboratively and closely with students and clinical partners to bridge didactic experiences to authentical clinical practice. Faculty have access to state-of-the-art technology and outstanding facilities for education, research, and clinical practice, including a dedicated classroom, simulation center, and laboratory space. The Herbert H. and Grace A. Dow College of Health Professions consists of five academic units: Department of Physical Therapy, Department of Physical Education and Sport, Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders, the School of Health Sciences, and the School of Rehabilitation and Medical Science. It offers undergraduate and/or graduate degree programs in athletic training, audiology, communication sciences and disorders, exercise science, environmental health and safety, health administration, physical activity specialist, physical education, physical therapy, physician assistant, public health, school and public health education, speech-language pathology, and sport management, delivered by 100+ faculty/staff. The Herbert H. and Grace A. Dow College of Health Professions\u2019 website is www.chp.cmich.edu . Posting Begins 09/16/2026 Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Type of Recruitment External About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this vacancy? Please indicate the specific source by title (i.e., CMU website, HigherEdJobs.com, Higher Education Recruitment Consortium, The Chronicle, specific professional association, specific list serv, etc.): (Open Ended Question) Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Other Document (1) Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/44934": {"title": "PROJECT ADVISOR / UPWARD BOUND (2 POSITIONS)", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | PROJECT ADVISOR / UPWARD BOUND (2 POSITIONS) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. PROJECT ADVISOR / UPWARD BOUND (2 POSITIONS) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. 2 positions available in Detroit, Michigan. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3765 Position Number 71475, 71485 Type of Recruitment External Position Title PROJECT ADVISOR / UPWARD BOUND (2 POSITIONS) Position Summary This position is located in Detroit, Michigan and serves students within a Detroit Public Schools Community District High School and Charter Schools. The Project Advisor position is a federally-funded TRIO program providing opportunities for participants to succeed in their precollege performance and ultimately in their higher education pursuits. The Project Advisor assists in planning, implementing and administering the goals and objectives of the TRIO Upward Bound program. This job requires a level of independence to respond to requests from the Project Director, university personnel, school administrators, community partners, students, and parents within defined grant regulations, guidelines, and procedures. Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree in social work, education, counseling, or a related field from an accredited institution. Experience working with educational programs or similar projects. Experience developing and implementing programs and workshops. Experience with the college admissions and financial aid process. Experience and comfortability working with underrepresented students, parents, and community members. Possession of a valid driver\u2019s license and proof of current automobile insurance coverage. Ability to manage confidential information. Proven ability to be self-directed, a self-starter, and work independently. Strong written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills. Must have flexibility and availability to work evenings, weekends, irregular hours, and travel as required. Proficiency in Microsoft Office. Ability to perform the essential functions of the position, with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in education, social work, counseling, or a related field. Two years of experience working with TRIO , high school programs, or college access programs. Experience working with low-income, first-generation youth. Experience with pre-college summer residential programs. Ability to and familiarity with using social media outlets. Bilingual in English/Spanish with the ability to read and write. Duties & Responsibilities Orients target schools, personnel, community, parents, students, and stakeholders about the Upward Bound (UB) Program. Develops a working relationship with school administrators, counselors, teachers, parents, community agencies, CMU personnel, etc. Develops and executes strategies to identify, recruit, select, and retain eligible students within target schools. Manages curriculum development and facilitates program workshops/seminars related to college, career, and financial planning during the academic school year and summer. Manages the participant case load, which includes assessing participant needs, monitoring academic progress while in the UB program, and referring to supportive services as needed. Assists high school seniors with follow-up regarding post-secondary matriculation (e.g., FAFSA completion, Scholarship Essays, College Applications, and complete college transition). Works with students to establish both short-term and long-term educational goals and the steps needed to achieve them. Advises students on course selection, dual enrollment, college applications, and college entrance exams. Assists with the coordination and implementation of college tours, educational/cultural/social field trips, and events that promote college access, supervises students during such events. Disseminates college access/financial literacy information to students and parents/guardians during monthly meetings/workshops. Assists with preparing written communication, memos, flyers, and newsletters for key stakeholders. Serves as part of the team to assist with planning, developing, and achieving overall program goals. Responsible for accurate documentation of student records/progress and prepares reports as required in the database monthly. Maintains positive leadership, ethical/professional conduct, and confidentiality of program participants\u2019 information. Collects and tracks data for the grant and annual performance report utilizing the data management system. Supervises and oversees student activities, events, and programs, as well as overnight trips. Follows all project regulations to meet all program goals/objectives. Completes monthly reconciliations to track program spending. Monitors Upward Bound alumni after high school graduation to track post-secondary education attainment. Travels to target high schools and makes home visits as needed. Attends meetings, trainings, and conferences as assigned. Relocates to the Central Michigan University main campus during the summer academy component of the UB program to facilitate and manage day- to-day summer activities. Performs other duties as assigned. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. 2 positions available in Detroit, Michigan. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $40,000 - $47,000 per year Division Student Recruitment & Retention Department TRIO Programs - Detroit Position Status Provisional Position End Date 08/31/2027 Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Detroit, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Dispatcher Medical Faculty Office Professional P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have a bachelor's degree in social work, education, counseling or a related field from an accredited institution? Yes No * Do you have experience working with educational programs or similar projects? Yes No * Do you have experience developing and implementing programs and workshops? Yes No * Do you have experience with the college admissions and financial aid process? Yes No * Do you have experience and comfortability working with underrepresented students, parents, and community members? Yes No * Do you possess a valid driver's license? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45552": {"title": "RADIO REPORTER/PRODUCER I/II", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | RADIO REPORTER/PRODUCER I/II Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. RADIO REPORTER/PRODUCER I/II Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. To upload a writing sample, please utilize the Writing Sample upload field. To upload a work sample, please utilize the Work Sample upload field. Applicants are strongly encouraged to submit letters of recommendation. If you wish to include recommendation letter(s) that are not required, please utilize the Recommendation Letters upload field. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3983 Position Number 79890 Type of Recruitment External Position Title RADIO REPORTER/PRODUCER I/II Position Summary WCMU\u2019s radio reporter/producer plays a key role in producing daily content for WCMU\u2019s radio and digital platforms. WCMU covers 46 of Michigan\u2019s 83 counties, reporting on a wide range of issues, including local and state government, education, climate and the environment, the economy, and more. This position serves as WCMU\u2019s Great Lakes Bay Region reporter, with the primary responsibility of covering Midland, Bay, and Saginaw counties. Primary functions of this position include news reporting. Additional functions may include on-air hosting, editing and story assignment responsibilities in the absence of the News Director. Required Qualifications Radio Reporter/Producer I (BH-1) Bachelor\u2019s degree in Broadcasting, Journalism, Multimedia, Humanities or a related field, or a combination of education and work experience that equates to four years. Demonstrated experience in reporting situations, including impromptu interview questioning and scripted situations. Demonstrated experience in field news gathering or remote recording situations. Possession of a valid driver\u2019s license and reliable transportation. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively both verbally and in writing, and to project a positive image. General knowledge of digital editing and studio situations. Must possess basic announcing skills. Ability to maintain positive interpersonal relationships with faculty, students, visitors, and fellow work associates. Ability to complete tasks independently. Ability to work occasional evenings and weekends as needed. Radio Reporter/Producer II (BS-2) All qualifications listed for a Radio Reporter/Producer I (BH-1), plus: Two additional years of increasingly responsible experience with key elements of the job, including reporting situations, field newsgathering, digital editing, hosting and announcing. Preferred Qualifications Radio Producer/Reporter I (BH-1) Two years of experience in on-air situations and with field recording/news gathering. Knowledge of issues, communities, and stakeholders within Midland, Bay, and Saginaw counties. Demonstrated experience with community engagement, public listening sessions, or audience-centered journalism. Demonstrated experience hosting live radio. Demonstrated experience as talent for fundraisers, interviews, and programs. Demonstrated experience as a local host of NPR news magazines. Demonstrated experience filing stories with NPR . Demonstrated experience producing multimedia content for radio, web, and social media platforms. Proficient capabilities in basic digital editing and multitrack editing. Demonstrated ability to formulate interview segments and questions. Duties & Responsibilities Radio Reporter/Producer I (BH-1) Performs the following tasks under direct supervision: Serves as WCMU\u2019s primary reporter covering the Great Lakes Bay Region, which includes Midland, Bay, and Saginaw counties. Schedules, records, and edits interviews for radio station use. Researches story topics and/or guests for possible programs or segments. Acts as talent for fundraisers, interviews, and programs. Operates radio remote and radio studio equipment as required. Assists in the development of radio programs and materials and contributes to ongoing projects as needed. Assists with the logistics of interviews or guest appearances. Develops buildouts of radio news stories for WCMU\u2019s digital platforms. Occasionally serves as a back-up host for Morning Edition, All Things Considered, and other news programs. Develops contacts with Central Michigan University departments, local and state government officials, and various constituents. Develops and maintains relationships with community leaders, local governments, educational institutions, nonprofit organizations, businesses, advocacy groups, and residents throughout the Great Lakes Bay Region. Represents WCMU at various station events as requested. Pitches stories to NPR , Harvest Public Media, and other organizations for national distribution. Participates in professional development opportunities. Assigns and edits stories for student news reporters and fellow staff members as directed by the News Director. Edits reports submitted by freelance reporters as directed by the News Director. Participates in recruiting, interviewing, and training student news reporters and freelance news reporters. Contributes occasionally to WCMU\u2019s video productions. Travels for reporting trips and station events as required, including occasional overnight trips. Assists with documenting reporting outcomes, community engagement efforts, and audience impact metrics related to Great Lakes Bay Region coverage. Radio Reporter/Producer II (BS-2) Performs all duties and responsibilities of the Radio Reporter/Producer I under limited supervision and with increased confidence and responsibility, plus: Assists in filing stories with NPR , Harvest Public Media, and other organizations for national distribution. Performs confidently with live, on the scene, and breaking news coverage. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. To upload a writing sample, please utilize the Writing Sample upload field. To upload a work sample, please utilize the Work Sample upload field. Applicants are strongly encouraged to submit letters of recommendation. If you wish to include recommendation letter(s) that are not required, please utilize the Recommendation Letters upload field. Employee Group Public Broadcasting - Hourly Staff Pay Level Pay Range BH-1 = $17.10 - $22.00 per hour / BS-2 = $39,520 - $48,880 per year Division Government and External Relations Department Public Broadcasting Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.00 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have at least a Bachelor's degree in Broadcasting, Journalism, Multimedia, Humanities, or a related field, or a combination of education and work experience that equates to 4 years? Yes No * Do you have experience in reporting situations, including impromptu interview questioning and scripted situations? Yes No * Do you have experience in field news gathering or remote recording situations? Yes No * Do you possess a valid driver's license? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Work Sample Writing Sample Optional Documents Recommendation Letters Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45599": {"title": "LANDSCAPE MAINTENANCE OPERATOR I (2 POSITIONS)", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | LANDSCAPE MAINTENANCE OPERATOR I (2 POSITIONS) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. LANDSCAPE MAINTENANCE OPERATOR I (2 POSITIONS) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3943 Position Number 37620, 76740 Type of Recruitment External Position Title LANDSCAPE MAINTENANCE OPERATOR I (2 POSITIONS) Position Summary The Landscape Maintenance Operator keeps campus grounds well maintained, tidy, attractive and presentable year-round, ensuring that students, faculty, and staff can safely move about campus even during inclement weather. This position conducts the planting and routine care of lawns, trees, shrubs, landscape beds, athletic fields, and other campus horticultural spaces. This position may work irregular hours in response to scheduled events, seasonal workloads, and winter storm events, and remains available for campus grounds maintenance related emergencies. Required Qualifications LANDSCAPE MAINTENANCE OPERATOR I (SM-4): High school diploma or GED . Possession of a valid driver\u2019s license. Knowledge of landscape maintenance. Possession of a CMU Motorized Utility Vehicle operator certification within 6 months of employment. Ability to work in a manner that will not endanger the safety of other persons, oneself, equipment and property. Ability to work with limited supervision. Demonstrated ability to follow and/or interpret oral or written directions. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively and project a positive image. Ability to perform the essential functions of the position, with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Qualifications Duties & Responsibilities LANDSCAPE MAINTENANCE OPERATOR I (SM-4): Performs the full scope and range of landscape duties to include mowing, edging, trimming, sweeping, raking, fertilizing, seeding, watering, aerating, and other methods and techniques in caring of campus landscapes. Prunes, trims, and cares for trees, shrubs, and hedges; removes and properly disposes of plants, shrubs, trees, and leaves as needed. Maintains landscape beds to ensure a well-maintained appearance to include weeding, pruning, and mulching. Conducts proper planting of turf, trees, shrubs, plants, flowers, and other horticultural items. Inspects plant material for evidence of damage and takes appropriate corrective actions. Lays out, marks, and maintains athletic areas to include football fields, baseball diamonds, tracks, tennis courts, band fields, and other athletic fields. Maintains synthetic turf. Lays out, installs, repairs, maintains, and operates irrigation systems. Safely operates equipment to include vacuums, sweepers, trucks, mowers, tractors, plows, salt spreaders, and other motorized equipment. Safely operates, loads, and unloads light and medium duty trucks. Cleans, maintains, and performs operator maintenance and minor repair to campus grounds maintenance equipment. Coordinates with and assists other trade employees on projects or work orders requiring campus grounds maintenance equipment and assistance. Conducts safe and efficient operation of snow and ice control equipment used in the removal of snow and ice from roads, parking lots, and walkways. Repairs and paints picnic tables, trash baskets, playground equipment, dumpsters, exterior signage, and other campus grounds-related items. Installs and removes exterior signage as needed. Places concrete for footers, posts, poles, and other applications not requiring a smooth finish. Maintains and repairs pavements to include roads and parking lots. Maintains storm sewer inlets and storm water detention and retention ponds. Removes litter, trash, and debris from campus and empties exterior trash receptacles. Hauls waste, litter, equipment, materials, and supplies as assigned. Directs work to assigned support employees and provides instruction on proper methods and processes. Performs other duties as assigned. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Employee Group Service Maintenance Staff Pay Level 4 Pay Range $19.78 per hour (non-negotiable) Division Finance and Administrative Services Department Landscape Operations Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 7:30 a.m. - 4:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have a high school diploma or GED? Yes No * Do you possess a valid driver's license? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45507": {"title": "APPLICATION ADMINISTRATOR I/II/III", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | APPLICATION ADMINISTRATOR I/II/III Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. APPLICATION ADMINISTRATOR I/II/III Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. For best consideration, please submit application materials on or before Thursday, September 10th, 2026. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3958 Position Number 64870 Type of Recruitment External Position Title APPLICATION ADMINISTRATOR I/II/III Position Summary The Application Administrator supports the administration, maintenance, security, and continuous improvement of enterprise applications and related systems used across Central Michigan University. Working as part of a collaborative team, this position helps ensure these services are reliable, secure, and effective for the faculty, staff, and students who depend on them. The role includes technical support, system configuration, monitoring, documentation, troubleshooting, and participation in planning and improvement efforts that advance the Office of Information Technology\u2019s goals, service standards, and commitment to excellent customer support. Required Qualifications Application Administrator I: Associate\u2019s degree in computer science, information systems, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Foundational knowledge of application or system administration concepts. Familiarity with common operating systems such as Windows or Linux. Ability to troubleshoot technical issues, follow established procedures, and learn new systems and processes. Strong communication, customer service, and collaboration skills. Application Administrator II: All the qualifications of Application Administrator I, plus: Four years of experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience, related to application or system administration. Experience supporting, administering, or maintaining enterprise applications or related technologies. Experience with one or more enterprise application support technologies, such as collaboration platforms, messaging systems, learning management systems, document management systems, web technologies, commerce systems, or data services. Ability to recommend and implement improvements to application support, maintenance, or operational practices. Working knowledge of application deployment, configuration, and ongoing management processes. Experience with application monitoring, troubleshooting, or performance support. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and collaboration skills. Application Administrator III : All the qualifications of Application Administrator II, plus: Six years of experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience, related to application or system administration. Experience contributing to service planning, support strategies, or operational improvement efforts for enterprise applications and related systems. Strong working knowledge of application hosting, web, or server technologies used to support enterprise applications. Experience using scripting, automation, or other technical tools to support application deployment, maintenance, or administration. Experience working with cloud-hosted, vendor-managed, or hybrid application environments. Ability to mentor, support, or share knowledge with other staff. Experience supporting integrations or data exchange activities across multiple systems. Ability to contribute to the design, improvement, or long-term support of enterprise application solutions. Excellent communication, collaboration, and problem-solving skills. Senior Application Administrator: All the qualifications of Application Administrator III , plus: Eight years of experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience, related to application or system administration. Experience administering multiple complex enterprise applications or services. Strong understanding of security practices, risk mitigation, and operational reliability in application environments. Ability to lead or significantly contribute to the design, scalability, resiliency, and long-term support of enterprise application solutions. Demonstrated ability to identify improvement opportunities and develop practical recommendations for implementation. Demonstrated professionalism and sound judgment in working with faculty, staff, students, and other stakeholders. Demonstrated leadership in communication, coordination, or stakeholder engagement for complex work. Ability to model collaborative, service-oriented, and values-based behavior in support of team and university goals. Preferred Qualifications Experience with enterprise platforms and technologies such as Microsoft 365, SharePoint, Exchange, Blackboard, Perceptive Content, SQL Server, web services, cloud-hosted systems, or similar tools is helpful. Familiarity with scripting or automation tools, such as PowerShell or Python, to support routine administration tasks. Experience partnering with business units, user offices, or subject matter experts to identify needs and develop solutions using supported systems. Ability to gather, analyze, and document user needs or business requirements to support application improvements or implementations. Experience working in technical support, service desk, desktop support, or other customer-facing IT roles. Duties & Responsibilities Application Administrator I: Demonstrates ownership in supporting assigned systems, resolving routine end-user issues, and developing an understanding of system functionality, configuration, dependencies, and change impacts. Uses established procedures to troubleshoot routine application and system issues, document findings, and escalate issues requiring additional analysis or decision-making. Performs basic administration and support tasks in common operating system environments used by supported applications, including routine validation, access checks, and coordination with infrastructure teams. Participates in system testing approaches and test planning, and assists with test procedures that assess the impact of application and system upgrades on performance and reliability. Works with OIT staff and vendors to support systems on behalf of end users. Verifies system backups and assists with creating and maintaining technical documentation. Monitors system logs and investigates discovered issues or events. Ensures applications meet university security standards and requirements. Provides application functionality instruction to end users as needed. Serves as backup to peer staff for identified systems and applications. Maintains a positive, service-oriented approach with all faculty, staff, and students. Acts as a technical resource for application administration projects. Other duties as assigned. Application Administrator II: All the duties of Application Administrator I, plus: Assists in establishing system specifications and infrastructure. Contributes to production control and release management procedures, maintains system release documentation, and supports successful production deployments. Helps establish system access practices, monitoring and control procedures, and disaster recovery policies and procedures, including related testing. Assists with security incident investigations related to core OIT systems. Works with the Information Security team to mitigate risks related to core OIT systems. Establishes load and stress testing and participates in system capacity planning. Responsible for administering one or more low-complexity applications or systems. Application Administrator III : All the duties of Application Administrator II, plus: Develops service strategy for related systems, including support approach, operational practices, improvement priorities, and stakeholder and technical partner coordination. Develops production control and release management procedures, maintains system release documentation, and ensures successful production deployments. Uses scripting, automation, or other technical tools to support application deployment, maintenance, administration, monitoring, reporting, and repeatable operations. Supports integrations and data exchange across systems, including coordination with technical partners, data-flow validation, and integration troubleshooting. Onboards new or existing software solutions in alignment with organizational and industry software implementation best practices. Senior Application Administrator: All the duties of Application Administrator III , plus: Serves as an expert resource for complex troubleshooting. Responsible for administering one or more high-complexity applications or systems. Leads technical projects with broad organizational impact. Leads or significantly contributes to design, scalability, resiliency, and long-term support planning for complex enterprise application solutions and services. Leads communication, coordination, and stakeholder engagement for complex application work, ensuring stakeholders and technical partners understand impacts, decisions, timelines, and support expectations. Evaluates new software solutions and works with business offices to address business needs or improve processes. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. For best consideration, please submit application materials on or before Thursday, September 10th, 2026. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $55,000 - $85,000 Division President Department Applications & Systems - OIT Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule M-F 8-5; evenings, nights and weekends as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department The Office of Information Technology ( OIT ) serves as Central Michigan University\u2019s strategic technology partner, providing the infrastructure, services, security, and support that enable teaching, learning, research, and university operations. OIT works collaboratively across campus to deliver reliable technology solutions, improve efficiency, protect institutional information, and help advance the university\u2019s mission. About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have an associate's degree in computer science, information systems, or a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and experience? Yes No * Do you have foundational knowledge of application or system administration concepts? Yes No * Will you now or at any time in the future require CMU to file or support an immigration petition or application in order to begin or continue your employment authorization? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Recommendation Letters List of References Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45272": {"title": "HVACR / CONTROLS TECHNICIAN", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | HVACR / CONTROLS TECHNICIAN Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. HVACR / CONTROLS TECHNICIAN Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Work Schedule Note : additional hours for events, emergencies, and winter schedule changes will be required. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3950 Position Number 42390 Type of Recruitment External Position Title HVACR / CONTROLS TECHNICIAN Position Summary Performs skilled work in the installation, operation, maintenance and repair of heating, ventilating, air conditioning, and refrigeration systems in addition to HVACR controls and energy management systems. Required Qualifications Education equivalent to completion of an Associate\u2019s Degree in HVAC . Five years of work experience in commercial HVACR . Possession of Type II or IV Refrigerant Handling Technician Certification. Possession of a valid driver\u2019s license. Ability to obtain a cooling tower treatment, category 5B pesticide applicator certification within one year of employment. Working knowledge of HVACR controls and the ability to install/adjust digital and pneumatic control circuits. Working knowledge of computer controls and related equipment. Ability to work independently and in a team environment and provide a high level of service excellence to campus customers. Ability to work from blueprints, drawings, and sketches. Ability to effectively use technology to access e-mail and the internet. Demonstrated ability to follow and/or interpret oral or written directions. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively and project a positive image. Demonstrated positive interpersonal skills. Ability to become an approved driver under the university\u2019s vehicle policy. Ability to be on-call. Ability to lift 75 pounds. Ability to safely use a ladder and scaffolding. Ability to work in permitted/non-permitted confined spaces and areas with limited egress. Ability to safely use power equipment and hand tools. Ability to work outdoors in all seasons. Ability to work an 8-hour shift, overtime, weekends, nights, and holidays. Preferred Qualifications Experience with MIOSHA safety regulations. Experience with steam systems, steam traps, and food service equipment. Duties & Responsibilities Plans and performs a wide variety of skilled work in the installation, maintenance, and repair of heating, ventilation, air conditioning, refrigeration, and environmental control equipment (both electronic and pneumatic) and related systems. - Heating includes but is not limited to, gas fired boilers, furnaces, and roof top equipment. - Ventilating includes but is not limited to, make-up air systems, laboratory and kitchen hoods, and general exhaust. - Air conditioning includes but is not limited to, direct expansion air condition such as electric, unitary equipment, roof top units and chillers, steam absorption chillers with cooling towers, and associated equipment. - Controls include but are not limited to, pneumatic and digital direct controls and circuits up to 480 volts. - Refrigeration includes but is not limited to, reach-in and walk-in coolers and freezers, including ice machines and soft service ice cream machines. Performs routine maintenance and required repairs on steam traps and steam systems; serves as a backup to kitchen equipment mechanics on food service equipment repairs. Responsible for the adjustment and maintenance of HVAC controls and computer interfaces in assigned buildings. Analyzes HVACR and related mechanical system performance issues using TAB (testing/adjusting/balancing) techniques and control system analysis. Maintains, repairs, and replaces the following: - Water pumps, bearings, valves, fittings, and related systems. - Fans, bearings, blowers, mounts, and related systems. - Steam condensate receivers, pumps, piping, and related systems. - Compressed air systems and related systems. Performs preventative maintenance and lubricates related equipment. Maintains telephone and radio contact with campus, outside vendors, and contractors as necessary. Maintains a positive image with customers, vendors, and peers. Maintains cleanliness of environmental system, spaces, mechanical rooms, and equipment. Plans work and obtains necessary materials, equipment, and supplies. Operates all required tools and equipment to include but not limited to power equipment, hand tools, and multiple electronic and analog meters. Operates absorption and centrifugal chillers and cooling towers to maintain demand for cooling in satellite locations. Troubleshoots, develops, and implements solutions. Works effectively with other skilled trades. Keeps necessary records as required. Request supplies and equipment as necessary. Performs other duties related to the job classification as assigned. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Work Schedule Note : additional hours for events, emergencies, and winter schedule changes will be required. Employee Group Service Maintenance Staff Pay Level 10 Pay Range $34.00 per hour (non-negotiable) Division Finance and Administrative Services Department Refrigeration & Control - Central Energy Facility Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri 7:30 a.m. - 4:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed* Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have education equivalent to the completion of an Associate's degree in HVACR? Yes No * Do you have at least five years of work experience in commercial HVACR? Yes No * Do you possess a Type II or IV Refrigerant Handling Technician Certification? Yes No * Do you possess a valid driver's license? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45566": {"title": "Nuclear Physics Postdoctoral Research Fellow", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | Nuclear Physics Postdoctoral Research Fellow Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. Nuclear Physics Postdoctoral Research Fellow Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Please submit a cover letter discussing research interests and qualifications, a CV, and the names and contact information of 3 references. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Please direct questions about the position to Dr. Alfredo Estrade, estra1a@cmich.edu or Dr. Matthew Redshaw, redsh1m@cmich.edu Position Information Position Information Posting Number F-1062 Position Title Nuclear Physics Postdoctoral Research Fellow College/Unit College of Science and Engineering Home Department Department of Physics Employee Group Postdoctoral Research Fellow Employment Status Full-Time Position Type 12 month Position Classification Postdoctoral Research Fellow Position Begin Date 11/16/2026 Position End Date 11/15/2027 Position Summary The Nuclear Physics and Fundamental Symmetries group in the Department of Physics at Central Michigan University invites applications for a postdoctoral researcher position in experimental nuclear physics. The group performs research in low-energy nuclear physics to address questions in nuclear astrophysics, nuclear structure and reactions, and in fundamental symmetries. The group leads research programs at US and international particle accelerator laboratories, with a strong emphasis on experiments at the nearby Facility for Rare Isotope Beams ( FRIB ). Activities carried out locally at CMU include the development and characterization of radiation detectors and precision mass measurements with the CHIP - TRAP Penning trap. The selected candidate will be focused on the program of precision mass measurements at FRIB led by Professors Alfredo Estrade and Matthew Redshaw. These measurements have applications to nuclear astrophysics, nuclear structure, and fundamental symmetries. They include time-of-flight mass measurements with the S800 spectrometer, and Penning trap measurements with the LEBIT facility. As a postdoctoral researcher, the selected candidate will be expected to take a leading role in planning and running experiments at FRIB . The selected candidate may be involved in projects to develop nuclear physics instrumentation for ion traps and beam tracking detectors. The selected candidate will have the opportunity to supervise CMU graduate students, and will be encouraged to develop their own ideas for experiments at accelerator laboratories. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in nuclear physics or related field. Demonstrated experience with experimental nuclear physics techniques and data analysis. Strong scientific writing and communication skills. Strong interest in advancing topics of current research in nuclear physics and astrophysics. Ability to perform the essential functions of the job with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Qualifications Experience with ion beam optics and simulations of ion beam transport. Experience with data acquisition systems and event-by-event dataset analysis. Experience with radiation detectors and/or ion trapping techniques. Experience preparing and running experiments at nuclear physics laboratories. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Please submit a cover letter discussing research interests and qualifications, a CV, and the names and contact information of 3 references. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Please direct questions about the position to Dr. Alfredo Estrade, estra1a@cmich.edu or Dr. Matthew Redshaw, redsh1m@cmich.edu About the Department The Department of Physics offers B.S., M.S. and Ph.D. programs in physics and astronomy/astrophysics. The department also offers a full range of general education and service courses in physics, physical science, and astronomy. Further information about the department is available on the department website . Posting Begins 10/05/2026 Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Type of Recruitment External About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this vacancy? Please indicate the specific source by title (i.e., CMU website, HigherEdJobs.com, Higher Education Recruitment Consortium, The Chronicle, specific professional association, specific list serv, etc.): (Open Ended Question) Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Other Document (1) Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45603": {"title": "SPEECH LANGUAGE PATHOLOGIST MASTER CLINICAL EDUCATOR", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | SPEECH LANGUAGE PATHOLOGIST MASTER CLINICAL EDUCATOR Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. SPEECH LANGUAGE PATHOLOGIST MASTER CLINICAL EDUCATOR Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Applicants are strongly encouraged to submit letters of recommendation. If you wish to include recommendation letter(s) that are not required, please utilize the Recommendation Letters upload field. If there is an applicable certification document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the 'Certification' upload field. If there is another applicable document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the Other Document (1) upload field. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3952 Position Number 04020 Type of Recruitment External Position Title SPEECH LANGUAGE PATHOLOGIST MASTER CLINICAL EDUCATOR Position Summary The primary responsibilities of the Speech Language Pathologist ( SLP ) Master Clinical Educator are on-site clinical education in clinical and didactic classrooms and evaluation of students performing preventative, diagnostic, consultative, and individual and/or group treatment services in the speech-language pathology program. The SLP Master Clinical Educator schedules their assigned caseload each semester. In addition, the SLP Master Clinical Educator works to coordinate clinical experiences that involve inter-professional education and practice and simulated/standardized events. This position may also be involved in planning and implementing collaborative programs on and off-campus that involve clinical experiences, service learning, and/or programs of community engagement. The SLP Master Clinical Educator may also provide direct clinical services to the community on a twelve-month basis. This position functions under the direct supervision of the Director of Clinical Instruction and Speech-Language Pathology Services or a designated representative. This position also exercises supervision over student employees as assigned. Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree. Possession of an ASHA Certification of Clinical Competence: Speech- Language Pathology ( CCC - SLP ). Possession of a valid Michigan SLP license. Three years of professional experience as a Speech-Language Pathologist with pediatric and adult populations. Three years experience in the diagnosis and treatment of cognitive- communicative disorders across the lifespan. Experience providing clinical instruction to undergraduate and/or graduate students. Ability to perform the essential functions of the position, with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Qualifications Clinical supervisory experience and demonstrated evidence-based competence in clinical education of speech-language pathology students. Expertise in a range of communication and swallowing disorders, with interest in infants through geriatrics. Experience providing inter-professional education and practice. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively, both verbally and in writing. Demonstrated ability to maintain positive interpersonal relations. Demonstrated flexibility and ability to function in a dynamic environment. Duties & Responsibilities Provides clinical education in face-to-face and telepractice clinical settings, along with simulated settings, and didactic classroom settings of undergraduate and graduate speech-language pathology students. Evaluates and treats clients and monitors subsequent follow-up. Coordinates students at off-campus sites or as GAs, as assigned. Teaches or co-teaches either CSD 494, CSD 495 or SLP 749 or other academic courses as assigned. Attends university/college/department/division/clinic meetings as appropriate. Coordinates scheduling of assigned clinical caseload. Integrates inter-professional education and practice in clinical education and service delivery. Plans and coordinates simulated experiences to supplement and/or remediate clinical education. Performs other duties as assigned. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Applicants are strongly encouraged to submit letters of recommendation. If you wish to include recommendation letter(s) that are not required, please utilize the Recommendation Letters upload field. If there is an applicable certification document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the \u2018Certification\u2019 upload field. If there is another applicable document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the Other Document (1) upload field. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $72,000 - $84,000 per year Division Academic Affairs Department Communication Sciences & Disorders Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About the College The Herbert H. and Grace A. Dow College of Health Professions consists of five academic units (Department of Physical Therapy, Department of Physical Education and Sport, Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders, the School of Health Sciences, and the School of Rehabilitation and Medical Science). It offers undergraduate and/or graduate degree programs in athletic training, audiology, communication sciences and disorders, exercise science, environmental health and safety, health administration, physical activity specialist, physical education, physical therapy, physician assistant, public health, school and public health education, speech-language pathology, and sport management, delivered by 100+ faculty/staff. CMU\u2019s website is http://www.cmich.edu . The Herbert H. and Grace A. Dow College of Health Professions website is http://www.chp.cmich.edu . About the Department The Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders consists of three divisions: Speech-Language Pathology, Audiology, and American Sign Language. It offers a undergraduate major in Communication Sciences and Disorders, undergraduate minors in Communication Sciences and Disorders and American Sign Language, an undergraduate certificate in Deaf and Hard-of-Hearing Studies, graduate programs in Speech-Language Pathology and Audiology, and a graduate certificate in Structured Language and Literacy Intervention. To learn more about the department, visit the department website . About the Speech-Language Pathology Program The Speech-Language Pathology Program is a seven-semester program which provides the academic and clinical training to prepare its graduates to be certified and licensed to practice as speech-language pathologists across settings and populations. For more information about the Speech-Language Pathology Program, please visit our website . About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have at least a master's degree? Yes No * Do you possess an ASHA Certificate of Clinical Competence: Speech- Language Pathology (CCC-SLP)? Yes No * Do you posses a Michigan SLP license? Yes No * Do you have at least three years of professional experience as a Speech-Language Pathologist with pediatric and adult populations? Yes No * Do you have at least three years experience in the diagnosis and treatment of cognitive-communicative disorders across the lifespan? Yes No * Do you have experience providing clinical instruction to undergraduate and/or graduate students? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Recommendation Letters Other Document (1) List of References Certification Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45510": {"title": "COORDINATOR / INTERNATIONAL STUDENT WELCOME CENTER", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | COORDINATOR / INTERNATIONAL STUDENT WELCOME CENTER Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. COORDINATOR / INTERNATIONAL STUDENT WELCOME CENTER Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3980 Position Number 79240 Type of Recruitment External Position Title COORDINATOR / INTERNATIONAL STUDENT WELCOME CENTER Position Summary This position is responsible for providing day-to-day leadership and the delivery of service to international students in the International Student Welcoming Center. Managing a team of student employees, this position coordinates a one-stop-shop for information for international students pursuing degree programs at CMU . Under the direction of the Executive Director of International and Graduate Admissions, the coordinator will ensure relevant information is readily available to students and delivered with a high degree of accuracy and excellent customer service. The coordinator will also assist with other aspects of international student recruitment and onboarding such as international student orientation, check-in, and issuing or updating 1-20s. Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree. Experience advising international students at the higher education level. US citizenship or Permanent Residency required per Department of Homeland Security regulations. Demonstrated ability to learn and apply modern technology and software to position requirements. Demonstrated organizational and communication skills, both written and verbal, particularly in a cross-cultural environment. Familiarity with F-1 immigration regulations. Ability to work in a busy, cross-cultural setting maintaining accuracy and attention to detail. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in International Education, Educational Leadership, Student Affairs, or related field. Two years\u2019 experience as an international student advisor and working with SEVIS . Competency in a foreign language. Experience creating and delivering orientation programs or related academic programming at the university level. Experience working with Terra Dotta or other batch related immigration software. Duties & Responsibilities Responsible for the coordination and delivery of services to international students in the International Student Welcome Center and other areas of the university as needed. Hires, trains, and supervises student employees to assist CMU international students with questions they may have about CMU , our processes, policies, and procedures; assists with helping them find services in the Mount Pleasant area. Develops and maintains a virtual (website) and physical presence that is student focused and is known for a high degree of accuracy, customer service and support to the international student community. Develops, in collaboration with others, a communication and promotion plan to ensure students and the campus are aware of the services offered in the International Student Welcome Center. Collaborates with other campus employees and members of the Mount Pleasant community in the pursuit of these duties. Assists with the planning and implementation of check-in, orientation and other helpful and informational programs for international student onboarding and life at CMU and in Mount Pleasant Delivers face-to-face and online services to international students. Assists with issuing and updating I-20s and other documents that are related to international student status. Identifies emerging student issues and communicates them to the supervisor, anticipates how the university may best serve students. Functions as part of a team to support and serve international students at CMU . Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $45,000-$55,000 Division Student Recruitment & Retention Department International Affairs & Graduate Recruitment Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as required. Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have at least a bachelor's degree? Yes No * Do you have experience advising international students at the higher education level? Yes No * Are you a US citizen or have Permanent Residency, which is required per the Department of Homeland Security regulations for this position? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Recommendation Letters List of References Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45285": {"title": "CUSTODIAN (8 POSITIONS)", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | CUSTODIAN (8 POSITIONS) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. CUSTODIAN (8 POSITIONS) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. If there is another applicable document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the Other Document (1) upload field. 8 positions available in Mt. Pleasant, Michigan. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3854 Position Number 37210, 37110, 62850, 37540, 36870, 39970, 39880, 62110 Type of Recruitment External Position Title CUSTODIAN (8 POSITIONS) Position Summary Maintains the cleanliness of academic, residential, and administrative campus buildings and service areas. Performs manual custodial tasks in university buildings. Ensures spaces are presentable and sanitary for employees and visitors. Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED . One year of work experience. Ability to work independently and effectively in a team environment. Ability to provide a high level of service excellence to campus customers. Ability to effectively use technology to access e-mail and the internet. Demonstrated ability to follow and/or interpret oral or written directions. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively. Demonstrated positive interpersonal skills. Possession of a valid driver\u2019s license. Ability to become an approved driver under the university\u2019s vehicle policy. Ability to be on-call. Ability to lift 40 pounds. Ability to safely use a ladder. Ability to work in confined spaces. Ability to work outdoors in all seasons. Ability to work an 8-hour shift, overtime, weekends, nights, and holidays, as required. Preferred Qualifications Working knowledge of cleaning materials and methods. One year of custodial experience. Duties & Responsibilities Operates and maintains mechanical cleaning, scrubbing, carpet shampooing, upholstery cleaning, and vacuum-cleaning. Sweeps, mops, strips, and waxes floor surfaces. Cleans and waxes furniture, cases, fixtures and furnishings. Cleans mirrors and interior glass. Cleans restrooms and replenishes restroom supplies. Spot washes walls and wipes down touch points. Sweeps, dusts, and wet-mops stairs and stairwells. Collects and disposes of waste and biohazard materials according to protocol. Maintains entrances and areas surrounding buildings by completing tasks including but not limited to picking up litter, cigarette butts, sweeping, shoveling snow, removing ice, spreading sand and salt. Unclogs commodes, urinals, and sink drains without dismantling the fixture. Reports repair work and/or damages to the building or equipment to the service center. Replaces light bulbs and broken globes as needed. Moves and arranges furniture and furnishings. Washes interior and exterior windows. Empties all trash containers and removes trash from buildings to pick- up stations. Plans work and obtains necessary materials, equipment, and supplies. Keeps necessary records, and develops reports, as required. Requests supplies and equipment as necessary. Performs other duties related to the job classification as assigned. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. If there is another applicable document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the Other Document (1) upload field. 8 positions available in Mt. Pleasant, Michigan. Employee Group Service Maintenance Staff Pay Level 2 Pay Range $17.50 per hour (non-negotiable) Division Finance and Administrative Services Department Building Services Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Various Hours/Various Days (40 hours/week); weekends as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have a high school diploma or GED? Yes No * Do you have at least one year of work experience? Yes No * Do you possess a valid driver's license? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document (1) Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45571": {"title": "ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR / BUSINESS &amp; COMMUNITY OUTREACH", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR / BUSINESS &amp; COMMUNITY OUTREACH Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR / BUSINESS & COMMUNITY OUTREACH Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3989 Position Number 78530 Type of Recruitment External Position Title ASSOCIATE DIRECTOR / BUSINESS & COMMUNITY OUTREACH Position Summary The associate director of business and community outreach ( BCO ), within the CMU Online enterprise ( CMU IO), will be responsible for maintaining a portfolio of existing partners and continuously sourcing new partners that will lead to strategic partnerships focused on educational advancement of individuals and workforce development for organizations. Working within the assigned region of Southeast Michigan, the associate director will be based out of CMU\u2019s site in Troy, MI and will serve as the primary liaison between external partners and CMU Online, ensuring that all aspects of partnerships are communicated, facilitated, and supported by CMU Online. Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree. Two years of relevant experience in business development, sales, relationship building, education, human resources/training and development, or a related field. Possession of a valid Driver\u2019s License. Exceptional interpersonal and communication skills including ability and comfortability with presenting. Demonstrated ability to engage and skillfully influence a diverse clientele across a variety of industries. Demonstrated ability to project professionalism and a polished business acumen. Demonstrated ability to be results-oriented, follow through, prioritize, and manage multiple projects at various phases of their life cycle. Ability to effectively understand and relay the needs of clientele. Proven ability to work collaboratively within a cross-functional team, often times remotely. Ability to travel locally/regionally as needed. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree or progressively advanced experience in a related field. Demonstrated experience working with programs designed for training and development purposes. Demonstrated experience working with post-traditional, adult learners. Proficient in the use of relationship management or workflow management systems. Duties & Responsibilities Acts as a University steward by establishing and maintaining relationships with external stakeholders to form partnerships related to educational and professional learning opportunities for adult learners. Fosters and supports partner relationships by informing external stakeholders of their partnership status, opportunities for expansion, and outcomes of partnership agreements. Develops strategic partnerships whilst demonstrating an authentic commitment to and understanding of the organization\u2019s mission, values, and strategic imperatives/smart goals. Participates in a highly cross-collaborate environment in the development and implementation of partner agreements and programming that leads to measurable outcomes and impact. Promotes educational pathways and workforce development opportunities for governmental, business, and community-based organizations. Assists in preparing a comprehensive annual plan for regional outreach with an understanding of educational and workforce development needs specific to a region or industry. Works collaboratively within a team to ensure that focus and outreach areas align with the strategic mission and objectives of CMU Online. Responsible for aligning work efforts with established goals/targets for identifying and developing business and community partnerships within the Southeast Michigan region; this may include travel to and meeting with clients outside of the designated region as needed. Researches, recommends, attends, and participates in appropriate regional and professional organizations or events to represent CMU and extend reach and awareness. Engages university and stakeholder groups such as Alumni to supplement outreach efforts in the assigned region. Utilizes internal systems to document and track engagement efforts, contacts, and the status of partnerships. Performs other duties as assigned. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $69,300 - $80,300 per year Division Academic Affairs Department CMU Online Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.00 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Troy, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have a bachelor's degree? Yes No * Do you have at least two years of relevant experience in business development, sales, relationship building, education, human resources/training and development, or a related field? Yes No * Do you possess a valid driver's license? Yes No * Do you have the willingness and ability to travel independently and work evenings and weekends as needed? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents List of References Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45512": {"title": "COORDINATOR / GRADUATE RECRUITMENT", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | COORDINATOR / GRADUATE RECRUITMENT Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. COORDINATOR / GRADUATE RECRUITMENT Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3985 Position Number 77520 Type of Recruitment External Position Title COORDINATOR / GRADUATE RECRUITMENT Position Summary The Coordinator of Graduate Recruitment is responsible for coordinating varied and complex projects, many of a confidential nature, which include collecting, analyzing, and interpreting research data related to graduate enrollment management, working with department chairs and graduate program directors on promotional strategies and communications, and providing recommendations towards the creation and support of the Graduate Strategic Enrollment Management Plan. This position has a focus on recruiting international graduate students for Master of Science in Administration ( MSA ) degree programs and other graduate programs and graduate certificates. This position works closely with faculty and staff within the MSA unit and other academic units and service providers within the University to assist with developing targeted recruiting and communication strategies to support international graduate admission and enrollment. This position will work closely with academic units and other University offices to assist with developing targeted communication strategies to support international graduate recruiting and enrollment, in terms of quality and quantity as well as to design and prepare assessments of programs supporting CMU\u2019s strategic graduate recruiting process. In addition, this position will assist the Director of Graduate and International Recruitment with the development and execution of the graduate SEM plan, which includes assisting with and/or developing and distributing promotional messages and materials. This position assists with the daily operations of Graduate Recruitment and interacts regularly with prospective graduate students and their supporters in person, by email, or by phone. This position requires frequent travel by car, public transportation, or air. Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree in higher education, business or a closely related field. One year of professional experience, preferably in higher education or related field. Demonstrated experience working with data, databases, spreadsheets, and/or data reports. Demonstrated organizational and/or project management skills, with effective attention to detail. Willingness and ability to travel frequently and to work evenings and weekends when needed. Ability to independently manage multiple projects and complete assignments on time. Ability to work with information systems and financial records. Ability to accurately perform work assignments, construct documents, and generate reports. Ability to effectively communicate and interact with current and potential graduate students. Ability to maintain confidentiality of sensitive issues as needed. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree or equivalent. Experience in marketing, recruiting, or college admissions. Experience with specialized computer programs and systems such as SAP and CRM . Strong interpersonal and public communication skills. Experience writing and editing reports and/or project plans. Ability to create and/or enhance promotional communications and materials. Desire to continue learning and improving upon knowledge and skills. Duties & Responsibilities Utilizes SAP , Data Warehouse, CRM , and other information systems to generate reports and provide in-depth analysis on key success factors relating to all stages of graduate recruitment, including the accumulation and progression of graduate-level inquiries, applications, admissions, enrollment, persistence, degree completion, and continuing education. Provides data synthesis, interpretive assessment and trend analysis, and recommendations to academic units, key administrators, and stakeholders in Graduate Recruitment, Admissions, and Retention, and to various academic units across campus. Plans and conducts organizational, operational, and program-specific data collection and research among comparative universities and peer institutions, current and potential partner organizations, third-party organizations or associations, and feeder schools. Assists in review, analysis, and planning of promotional information, messaging, and other communications for graduate recruiting and admissions. Plans, creates, and schedules targeted communications for key target markets and niches at all stages of the graduate prospecting, recruiting, and student service experience; collects and analyzes data to more accurately and uniquely identify each market niche and to better understand the pertinent educational wants and needs; and writes general and highly specialized email, direct mail, web-based messaging, and telephone-based communications. Designs, prepares, and provides special analyses and vetted assessments, functional and progressive recruiting and enrollment reports, print-based assessments, and visual/auditory presentations as needed. Represents Graduate Recruitment in planning sessions with academic units, on committees, and in special cross-campus projects relating to enrollment history, forecasting, prospecting, recruiting, and student-based service and support. Directly and indirectly communicates with current and prospective students and their families, working with academic units while scheduling campus visits and appointments, and working with GRA and academic program leadership to coordinate related activities and follow-up communications. Develops communication plans and implements and maintains CRM communications, including preparation of letters, memos, responses, reports, and other correspondence. Updates content for each program and coordinates enhanced promotional messages and materials. Conducts presentations and meets with prospective students and their supporters individually or in large and small groups, meets with visiting professionals, and assists with coordinating department-based visits and tours. Answers the telephone, makes calls, and provides other communications for recruiting and admissions. Assists with marketing activities, including research, media review, advertising and other promotions. Creates, maintains, and updates databases, files, contact lists, and printed documents as needed. Conducts special projects and assignments as directed. Performs other duties as assigned. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $45,000 - $55,000 Division Student Recruitment & Retention Department International Affairs & Graduate Recruitment Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have at least a bachelor's degree? Yes No * Do you have at least one year of professional experience, preferably in higher education or related field? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Recommendation Letters List of References Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/42260": {"title": "ATHLETICS STAFF TEMPORARY (PART-TIME)", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | ATHLETICS STAFF TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. ATHLETICS STAFF TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering a broadly diverse and inclusive campus that respects all social identities, experiences, and perspectives. In an effort to further this initiative, we are especially interested in candidates who will advance and promote an inclusive and supportive environment for every member of our university community. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3542 Position Number 99999 Type of Recruitment External Position Title ATHLETICS STAFF TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Position Summary Temporary athletics position. No benefits. CMU occasionally has temporary athletics positions available. Duties and responsibilities vary based on assignment, which may include camp coach/counselor, color commentator, announcer, play-by-play broadcaster, table crew, working shot clock, on-court host/DJ, academic tutor, athletic trainer, etc. Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED ; a higher degree may be required based on assignment. Related experience. Excellent interpersonal and communication skills. Ability to work with others in a collaborative environment. Ability to initiate and complete tasks independently. Preferred Qualifications Duties & Responsibilities Duties and responsibilities vary based on assignment, which may include camp coach/counselor, color commentator, announcer, play-by-play broadcaster, table crew, working shot clock, on-court host/CJ, academic tutor, athletic trainer, etc. Supervision Exercised Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering a broadly diverse and inclusive campus that respects all social identities, experiences, and perspectives. In an effort to further this initiative, we are especially interested in candidates who will advance and promote an inclusive and supportive environment for every member of our university community. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Employee Group Temporary Staff Staff Pay Level 00 Pay Range Varies based on assignment Division President Department Athletics Position Status Temporary Position End Date Employment Status Part-Time FTE 0.00 Position Type Other Weekly Work Schedule Varies based on assignment Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU , an AA/EO institution, strongly and actively strives to increase diversity and provide equal opportunity within its community. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex\u2010based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight (see https://www.cmich.edu/offices-departments/ OCRIE ). If you wish to see \u201cEEO is the Law\u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a high school diploma or GED? Yes No * What type of work are you interested in? (Open Ended Question) Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45611": {"title": "DIRECTOR / WOMEN&#39;S BASKETBALL OPERATIONS", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | DIRECTOR / WOMEN&#39;S BASKETBALL OPERATIONS Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. DIRECTOR / WOMEN'S BASKETBALL OPERATIONS Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This job is a one\u2011year appointment starting on the hire date. The department may choose to extend the appointment at their discretion. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3997 Position Number 72855 Type of Recruitment External Position Title DIRECTOR / WOMEN'S BASKETBALL OPERATIONS Position Summary The Director of Basketball Operations oversees the day-to-day administrative and logistical operations of the Central Michigan University women\u2019s basketball program. This position manages team travel, meals, scheduling, budget support, and the student manager program so the head coach and coaching staff can focus on instruction, recruiting, and student-athlete development. The Director works closely with athletics administration, compliance, business operations, facilities, sports medicine, academic services, and campus partners to deliver a well-organized, compliant, and student-athlete centered program experience. Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree. One year of experience in collegiate basketball operations, including experience gained as a graduate assistant, student manager, or intern. Working knowledge of NCAA rules and regulations. Strong organizational, planning, and time management skills with attention to detail. Effective written and verbal communication and relationship-building skills. Ability to manage budgets and follow financial and travel procedures. Ability to work evenings, weekends, and holidays and to travel with the team. Ability to handle sensitive information with discretion and professionalism. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree. Experience in collegiate women\u2019s basketball operations. Experience supervising student employees. Experience with camp operations and university business systems. Familiarity with travel, scheduling, and team management platforms such as Teamworks. Duties & Responsibilities Team Travel and Logistics: Plans and coordinates all team travel, including transportation, lodging, meals, itineraries, and travel party rosters, in accordance with university travel policy and department procedures. Serves as the primary point of contact with host institutions, hotels, charter and bus companies, and restaurants for road competitions. Coordinates logistics for home competitions, including visiting team needs and game day timelines, in partnership with event management. Coordinates logistics for postseason play, exempt events, and any foreign tour, as applicable. Team Meals and Nutrition Coordination: Coordinates team meals, pregame meals, and travel meals in alignment with department nutrition guidance and NCAA and institutional rules. Scheduling and Program Administration Maintains the program calendar, including practices, competitions, travel, meetings, community events, and team activities. Coordinates facility requests and practice scheduling with facilities and event management staff. Coordinates staff meetings, team meetings, and program events as directed by the head coach. Budget and Business Operations: Assists the head coach and business office with the development and monitoring of the program operating budget. Processes purchase requests, travel authorizations, reconciliations, per diem, and expense documentation in compliance with university policy. Tracks expenditures and provide regular budget updates to the head coach. Student Manager Program: Recruits, hires, trains, schedules, and supervises student employees. Oversees student employee duties related to practice and game operations, equipment, laundry, video, and statistics, and approve student manager timekeeping. Program Support and Community Engagement: Coordinates team community service and outreach initiatives, including the program\u2019s signature Hoops for Hunger food drive. Supports official and unofficial visit logistics on campus in coordination with the coaching staff and compliance. Coordinates with equipment staff on team apparel and equipment orders and inventory. Assists with alumni, donor, and special event coordination as requested by the head coach and external relations staff. Maintains program records, historical information, and operations files. Collaboration and Compliance: Works collaboratively with athletics administration, compliance, business operations, facilities, sports medicine, strength and conditioning, academic services, student-athlete development, and communications staff. Ensures all activities comply with NCAA , Mid-American Conference, and university rules and policies, including restrictions that apply to noncoaching staff. Refrains from on-court instruction and off-campus recruiting activities consistent with the noncoaching staff designation. Perform other duties as assigned consistent with the scope of the position. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This job is a one\u2011year appointment starting on the hire date. The department may choose to extend the appointment at their discretion. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $40,000 - $50,000 Division President Department Athletics Position Status Provisional Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.00 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends 10/28/2026 Open Until Filled No Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have a bachelor's degree? Yes No * Do you have at least one year of experience in collegiate basketball, including experience gained as a graduate assistant, student manager, or intern? Yes No * Do you have working knowledge of NCAA rules and regulations? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter List of References Transcript Copies Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45370": {"title": "MEDICAL SUPPORT STAFF POOL (RN, CMA, RMA, LPN) TEMPORARY (PART-TIME)", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | MEDICAL SUPPORT STAFF POOL (RN, CMA, RMA, LPN) TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. MEDICAL SUPPORT STAFF POOL (RN, CMA, RMA, LPN) TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3692 Position Number 99999 Type of Recruitment External Position Title MEDICAL SUPPORT STAFF POOL (RN, CMA, RMA, LPN) TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Position Summary Under the supervision of full-time medical staff, individuals in this role support the daily operations of the Student Health Services Clinic or Primary Specialty Clinic. Responsibilities are determined by the licensure and qualifications of the individual and include direct patient care and administrative support. The clinic provides a broad range of services, including routine medical care, physicals, chronic disease management, allergy injections, immunizations, birth control management, full-service laboratory testing, STI screening and treatment, and travel health consultations. Team members are expected to contribute to the delivery of high-quality, patient-centered care in a collaborative, multidisciplinary environment. Required Qualifications RN: Graduation from an accredited school of nursing. Current registration with State of Michigan Board of Nursing as a Registered Nurse (RN), or eligibility for such. Demonstrated ability to effectively apply the nursing process to assessing patients, planning and implementing care measures, evaluating outcomes and addressing change in an appropriate and timely manner. CMA , RMA , LPN : Successful completion of a practical nursing education program approved or accepted by the State of Michigan, or a high school diploma or equivalent and graduation from a medical assistant program approved by the American Association of Medical Assistants ( AAMA ) or American Medical technologist ( AMT ). Licensure by the State of Michigan to practice as a Licensed Practical Nurse or a certified or registered Medical Assistant. At least one year of experience working as a Licensed Practical Nurse or certified or registered Medical Assistant. Preferred Qualifications Duties & Responsibilities Responsibilities vary based on assignment and qualifications of the hired individual. Supervision Exercised None Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Employee Group Temporary Staff Staff Pay Level Pay Range Division Academic Affairs Department University Health Services Position Status Temporary Position End Date Employment Status Part-Time FTE 0.00 Position Type Other Weekly Work Schedule Hours will vary based upon needs of the clinic. Not exceed 25 hours per week. Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Do you have current registration with the State of Michigan Board of Nursing as a Registered Nurse (RN), or registry eligible? Yes No Have you successfully completed a practical nursing education program approved or accepted by the State of Michigan, or a high school diploma or equivalent and graduation from a two year medical assistant program approved by the American Association of Medical Assistants (AAMA). or do you have a Licensure by the State of Michigan to practice as a Licensed Practical Nurse or a certified Medical Assistant? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45574": {"title": "Applied Clarinet (Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor)", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | Applied Clarinet (Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. Applied Clarinet (Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. The search committee will begin reviewing applications on November 2, 2026, and will continue to accept applications until finalists are selected. Online applications must include: Cover Letter - that specifically addresses position qualifications, duties and includes a brief statement of teaching philosophy. Curriculum Vitae - that provides detailed evidence of successful teaching of applied clarinet and other areas of expertise at the college level. Diversity Statement - that pertains to experiences fostering inclusion in higher education (upload under \"Other Document (1)\"). Transcript Copies - of undergraduate and graduate degree transcripts (upload as one document). Work Sample - single document listing direct online links of up to four video recordings created within the last three years. All links must be accessible by direct link (e.g., no further registration is required). Links should include at least three solo recordings of different works made within the last three years, preferably live concert performances or unedited recordings. A minimum of one must contain video, and one may be of a chamber performance. List of References - contact information for at least three references who may be contacted and/or asked to submit a letter of recommendation. Address inquiries to: Chair, Clarinet Search Committee School of Music Central Michigan University Mount Pleasant, MI 48859 Phone: (989) 774-3281 Fax: (989) 774-3766 Position Information Position Information Posting Number F-1063 Position Title Applied Clarinet (Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor) College/Unit College of the Arts & Media Home Department School of Music Employee Group Tenure-Track Faculty - Academic Year Employment Status Full-Time Position Type 9 month (Academic Year) Position Classification Tenure Track Faculty Position Begin Date 08/23/2027 Position End Date Position Summary Recruit and retain high-quality applied clarinet students at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Pursue scholarly and creative activity that meets CMU standards for tenure and promotion. Teach courses in clarinet techniques, coach chamber ensembles, clarinet repertoire, and other courses relevant to qualifications. Perform with the faculty Woodwind Quintet, the \u201cPowers Quintet.\u201d Serve on departmental, collegiate, and professional committees. Additional duties may be assigned in accordance with areas of expertise and in consultation with the Director of the School of Music. Required Qualifications Doctorate in clarinet performance ( ABD candidates may be considered, provided the degree is conferred by the start date of the appointment), or commensurate professional experience. Outstanding performance skills as soloist and chamber musician. Successful college teaching experience. Ability to teach and collaborate within the field of Woodwind Pedagogy. Ability to teach courses in clarinet techniques for music education majors, Music Theory, or general education survey courses of varying genres. Ability to perform the essential functions of the job with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Qualifications Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. The search committee will begin reviewing applications on November 2, 2026, and will continue to accept applications until finalists are selected. Online applications must include: Cover Letter \u2013 that specifically addresses position qualifications, duties and includes a brief statement of teaching philosophy. Curriculum Vitae \u2013 that provides detailed evidence of successful teaching of applied clarinet and other areas of expertise at the college level. Diversity Statement \u2013 that pertains to experiences fostering inclusion in higher education (upload under \u201cOther Document (1)\u201d). Transcript Copies \u2013 of undergraduate and graduate degree transcripts (upload as one document). Work Sample \u2013 single document listing direct online links of up to four video recordings created within the last three years. All links must be accessible by direct link (e.g., no further registration is required). Links should include at least three solo recordings of different works made within the last three years, preferably live concert performances or unedited recordings. A minimum of one must contain video, and one may be of a chamber performance. List of References \u2013 contact information for at least three references who may be contacted and/or asked to submit a letter of recommendation. Address inquiries to: Chair, Clarinet Search Committee School of Music Central Michigan University Mount Pleasant, MI 48859 Phone: (989) 774-3281 Fax: (989) 774-3766 About the Department The School of Music is located in a state-of-the-art 119,000 square foot facility with a 500-seat concert hall housing a 61-rank Casavant organ, a 100-seat recital hall, recording facilities, and 79 practice rooms. The School of Music has 38 full- and part-time faculty and an enrollment of over 300 undergraduate and graduate majors and minors. To learn more about the school, visit the school website . Posting Begins 10/07/2026 Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Type of Recruitment External About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this vacancy? Please indicate the specific source by title (i.e., CMU website, HigherEdJobs.com, Higher Education Recruitment Consortium, The Chronicle, specific professional association, specific list serv, etc.): (Open Ended Question) Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Other Document (1) Transcript Copies Work Sample List of References Optional Documents Other Document (2) Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45527": {"title": "AUDIOLOGY CLINICAL SUPERVISOR &amp; EXTERNSHIP COORDINATOR", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | AUDIOLOGY CLINICAL SUPERVISOR &amp; EXTERNSHIP COORDINATOR Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. AUDIOLOGY CLINICAL SUPERVISOR & EXTERNSHIP COORDINATOR Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Applicants are strongly encouraged to submit letters of recommendation. If you wish to include recommendation letter(s) that are not required, please utilize the Recommendation Letters upload field. If there is an applicable certification document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the 'Certification' upload field. If there is a Statement of Teaching Philosophy you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the Statement of Teaching Philosophy upload field. If there is another applicable document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the Other Document (1) upload field. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3982 Position Number 72455 Type of Recruitment External Position Title AUDIOLOGY CLINICAL SUPERVISOR & EXTERNSHIP COORDINATOR Position Summary The clinical supervisor and externship coordinator in Audiology is responsible for the clinical teaching and supervision of undergraduate and graduate students, the evaluation and treatment of clients, and the coordination of clinical externships for the program. This position supports both on-campus and off-campus training experiences, serves as a liaison to externship sites, and ensures compliance with accreditation and university requirements. Required Qualifications Doctoral Degree in Audiology (AuD and/or PhD) or Master\u2019s Degree in Audiology (MA/MS), if obtained prior to 2007. ASHA Certificate of Clinical Competence in Audiology ( CCC -A) or proven eligibility upon hire. Current Michigan License in Audiology or proven eligibility upon hire. Demonstrated expertise in one or more areas of audiology practice (e.g., diagnostics, amplification, electrophysiology, cochlear implants, auditory processing, vestibular assessment, or related areas). Effective oral and written communication skills. Ability to maintain positive interpersonal relations. Ability to perform the essential functions of the position, with or without reasonable accommodations. Preferred Qualifications Three years of professional experience as an audiologist. Two years of experience in the clinical supervision of audiology students. Experience coordinating externships, clinical placements, or academic practicum sites. Familiarity with clinical education management systems (e.g., Calipso). Duties & Responsibilities Provides clinical teaching and supervision of undergraduate and graduate audiology students in on-campus and off-campus settings. Performs audiologic evaluations, treatments, and follow-up care. Provides audiologic support services to Mobile Health Central and school personnel. Teaches academic courses such as AUD 759, 769, 849, 995, or others as assigned. Coordinates student placements, including: - securing and monitoring second-year summer and fourth-year externships. - maintaining and updating the Clinical Externship Manual; educating students on externship rules and expectations. - vetting externship sites, coordinating affiliation agreements, onboarding processes, and certificates of insurance with the College of Health Professions clinical compliance coordinator. - conducting regular site visits and tracking placement needs in consultation with program leadership. Manages site and accreditation requirements, including: - maintaining placement databases and Calipso records. - registering supervisors and students, verifying ASHA certification and licensure, and completing semester checklists. - reviewing supervisor evaluations, addressing concerns, and ensuring compliance with accreditation standards. Serves as liaison among students, faculty, preceptors, and clinical sites, providing communication, guidance, and troubleshooting. Reviews placement feedback and implements strategies for continuous improvement. Attends university, college, department, and division meetings as appropriate. Performs other duties and responsibilities as assigned. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Applicants are strongly encouraged to submit letters of recommendation. If you wish to include recommendation letter(s) that are not required, please utilize the Recommendation Letters upload field. If there is an applicable certification document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the \u2018Certification\u2019 upload field. If there is a Statement of Teaching Philosophy you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the Statement of Teaching Philosophy upload field. If there is another applicable document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the Other Document (1) upload field. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $80,000 - $90,000 per year Division Academic Affairs Department Communication Sciences & Disorders Position Status Provisional Position End Date 12/31/2028 Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department The Department of Communication Sciences and Disorder offers undergraduate programs in American Sign Language, communication sciences and disorders, deaf and hard-of-hearing students as well as graduate programs in Speech-Language Pathology and structured language and literacy intervention, and a Doctor of Audiology program. About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have a doctoral degree in Audiology (AuD and/or PhD) or a master's degree in Audiology (MA/MS) obtained prior to 2007? Yes No * Do you have a ASHA Certificate of Clinical Competence: Audiology (CCC-A) or the ability to become eligible upon hire for the certificate? Yes No * Do you have a current Michigan License in Audiology or the ability to become eligible for licensure upon hire? Yes No Do you have experience in one or more areas of audiology practice (e.g., diagnostics, amplification, electrophysiology, cochlear implants, auditory processing, vestibular assessment, or related areas)? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Recommendation Letters Other Document (1) Statement of Teaching Philosophy List of References Certification Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/42263": {"title": "GYNECOLOGICAL TEACHING ASSOCIATE (GTA) TEMPORARY (PART-TIME)", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | GYNECOLOGICAL TEACHING ASSOCIATE (GTA) TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. GYNECOLOGICAL TEACHING ASSOCIATE (GTA) TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3545 Position Number 99999 Type of Recruitment External Position Title GYNECOLOGICAL TEACHING ASSOCIATE (GTA) TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Position Summary In-house training for females to teach the sensitive exam, assess and provide feedback to learners about accurate pelvic, and/or breast examination techniques. The GTA uses their body to guide medical students and physician assistant students through the entire process of performing a thorough pelvic exam: a visual exam (checking for any lumps or bumps), a speculum exam, and a bi-manual exam. The GTAs coach students on their clinical skills and give hands on instruction, as well as comments on technique, language, and overall approach. The GTA also addresses the communication skills needed to provide a comfortable exam in a standardized manner, while using their body as a teaching tool in a supportive, non-threatening environment. Required Qualifications Must be healthy, both mentally and physically, to handle this work. Must be professional and dependable. Preferred Qualifications Medical background. Duties & Responsibilities Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Employee Group Temporary Staff Staff Pay Level 00 Pay Range $75/hour Division Academic Affairs Department College of Medicine Position Status Temporary Position End Date Employment Status Part-Time FTE 0.00 Position Type Other Weekly Work Schedule As needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU , an AA/EO institution, strongly and actively strives to increase diversity and provide equal opportunity within its community. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex\u2010based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight (see https://www.cmich.edu/offices-departments/ OCRIE ). If you wish to see \u201cEEO is the Law\u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Have your ever worked as a GTA before? Yes No * If you have worked as a GTA before, please explain your experience and identify where you were trained. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a medical background? Yes No * If you have a medical background, please explain your experience. (Open Ended Question) * Do you fully understand that learners will be performing sensitive exams on your body with your guidance? Yes No * Please share any additional skills, knowledge, or experience you have that you think might be helpful to our program. (Open Ended Question) Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45613": {"title": "DIRECTOR / CONTRACTING &amp; PURCHASING SERVICES", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | DIRECTOR / CONTRACTING &amp; PURCHASING SERVICES Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. DIRECTOR / CONTRACTING & PURCHASING SERVICES Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. For best consideration, please submit application materials by September 30th, 2026. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3968 Position Number 35610 Type of Recruitment External Position Title DIRECTOR / CONTRACTING & PURCHASING SERVICES Position Summary Responsible for the administration, operation and direction of activities associated with Contracting and Purchasing Services, University Stores, and Central Mailroom. Plans, develops and implements policies and practices related to contracting and purchasing of machinery, equipment, raw materials, software, leases, vehicles, furniture, contractual services and supplies necessary for the operation of the University. Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree. Five years increasingly relevant professional experience with at least two years in a management position. Experience in the area of purchasing services or contract negotiations. Demonstrated ability to organize and direct the work activities of others. Ability to develop and maintain positive interpersonal relationships. Demonstrated ability to project a positive attitude through excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to perform the essential functions of the job with or without accommodation. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree; Purchasing certification such as CPP or CPSM or similar. Experience with contract development, review and related legal issues. Experience with SAP or other integrated enterprise purchasing, logistics and/or accounting system. Experience in higher education environment. Experience in a unionized environment. Duties & Responsibilities Plans, develops and implements policies and procedures related to various functions of Contracting & Purchasing Services. Manages staff responsible for contracting, purchasing, receiving, storing, moving, distributing and monitoring goods and services for the University. Ensures compliance with contracting authority on the University Contract Review Policy and Process. Oversees and conducts competitive proposals and bidding process. Collaborates with and guides University departments through the RFI and RFP processes. Negotiates competitive contracts with vendors. Manages supplier relationships. Prepares cost analyses on university spend and contracts. Supports feasibility studies on proposed projects. Monitors and coordinates grant funded activities as they relate to purchasing. Monitors and communicates applicable local, state, and federal statutes and administrative regulations to ensure compliance. Leads process changes to improve efficiency and to better utilize University resources. Acts as liaison between University departments and vendors/suppliers. Coordinates and prioritizes work activities for the Contracting and Purchasing Services units. Establish and maintain measurable performance metrics for all levels of procurement activities. Maintains department budgets. Manages other special projects as assigned. Supervision Exercised Supervisors are expected to support the Leadership Standards of Central Michigan University and foster a culture that inspires excellence. The Leadership Standards define how we lead and treat others on our team. As leaders, it is our responsibility to seek input from our teams to continuously improve our leadership abilities and our demonstration of the standards. Additionally, it is our responsibility to encourage and support the growth and development of those whom we lead. At CMU , we encourage employees to grow both personally and professionally, and thus advance CMU\u2019s culture of excellence. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. For best consideration, please submit application materials by September 30th, 2026. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $110,000 - $125,000 Division Finance and Administrative Services Department Contracting & Purchasing Services Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have at least a bachelor's degree? Yes No * Do you have at least five years of increasingly relevant professional experience with at least two years in a management position? Yes No * Do you have experience in the area of purchasing services or contract negotiations? Yes No * Supervisors are expected to support the Leadership Standards of Central Michigan University and foster a culture that inspires excellence. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position and click \u201cYes\u201d if you understand and support the culture that is important to CMU. Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Recommendation Letters Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45426": {"title": "ASSOCIATE ATHLETIC TRAINER", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | ASSOCIATE ATHLETIC TRAINER Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. ASSOCIATE ATHLETIC TRAINER Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position primarily works with Women's Basketball. Applicants are strongly encouraged to submit letters of recommendation. If you wish to include recommendation letter(s) that are not required, please utilize the Recommendation Letters upload field. Applicants are strongly encouraged to submit transcripts (unofficial or official) as a part of the application process. If there is an applicable certification document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the \u2018Certification\u2019 upload field. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3969 Position Number 79290 Type of Recruitment External Position Title ASSOCIATE ATHLETIC TRAINER Position Summary The Associate Athletic Trainer is a certified and licensed healthcare professional responsible for delivering comprehensive athletic training services to Central Michigan University ( CMU ) intercollegiate student-athletes. This position plays an integral role within the Sports Medicine team and reports to the Senior Associate Athletic Director for Sports Medicine. Required Qualifications Bachelor s or Master\u2019s degree in Athletic Training from an accredited institution. Three years of full-time experience as a certified athletic trainer. Certified Athletic Trainer in good standing with the National Athletic Trainers Association Board of Certification ( NATABOC ). Current licensure, as an Athletic Trainer in the State of Michigan, or eligibility for licensure upon hire. Current CPR / AED certification for the healthcare provider or equivalent. Demonstrated ability to communicate clearly, effectively, and professionally with student-athletes, coaches, and healthcare professionals. Strong organizational skills with the ability to manage multiple responsibilities and priorities. Willingness and availability to travel and work irregular hours, including evenings, weekends, and holidays as needed. Preferred Qualifications Master s degree in Athletic Training, Sports Medicine, Kinesiology, or a related field. Four years of full-time experience as a certified athletic trainer. Experience as a certified athletic trainer at the professional, Olympic, national team, or NCAA Division I collegiate level. Extensive background in the rehabilitation of both surgical and non-surgical upper and lower extremity injuries. Advanced certifications such as Graston Technique, Instrument-Assisted Soft Tissue Mobilization ( IASTM ), Active Release Techniques ( ART ), Certified Strength and Conditioning Specialist ( CSCS ), Performance Enhancement Specialist ( PES ), or Corrective Exercise Specialist ( CES ). Familiarity with electronic medical records ( EMR ) and injury tracking software (e.g., ATS , Healthy Roster, SportsWare). Demonstrated supervisory experience in a clinical or athletic training setting. Proven ability to mentor and support the development of athletic training students, graduate assistants, interns, and/or professional staff members. Duties & Responsibilities Athletic Training & Student-Athlete Care: Serves as the primary Certified Athletic Trainer for assigned intercollegiate athletic team(s), providing comprehensive healthcare services. Provides comprehensive athletic training services, including injury prevention, evaluation, treatment, referral, and rehabilitation for orthopedic and non-orthopedic conditions. Provides care to additional teams as assigned by the Senior Associate Athletic Director for Sports Medicine. Coordinates individualized care plans in consultation with the Medical Director and team physicians. Develops and supervises both surgical and non-surgical rehabilitation programs for student-athletes. Facilitates outside medical referrals and manages in-house orthopedic and physician clinics. Documents all medical services and interactions in the department?s electronic injury tracking system, including treatments, progress notes, imaging, and physician communications. Retrieves and organizes outside medical records as needed for continuity of care. Collaboration & Communication: Maintains consistent communication with coaching staff, strength and conditioning personnel, and team physicians regarding student-athlete health statuses, progress, and participation limitations. Coordinates with Student-Athlete Services to manage academic accommodations and resolve potential class conflicts for injured studentathletes. Collaborates with the insurance coordinator regarding medical claims and acts as the point of contact for insurance-related needs of assigned team(s). Develops modified training plans for injured student-athletes in coordination with the strength and conditioning staff. Provides timely updates to relevant athletic department personnel on student-athlete limitations, return-to-play timelines, and medical accommodations. Program Administration & Operations: Oversees ordering, inventory, and maintenance of medical supplies, equipment, and training room facilities. Supports the Senior Associate Athletic Director for Sports Medicine in implementing program development and departmental initiatives. Participates in the execution of institutional and NCAA Substance Abuse Control Program policies. Ensures all policies, procedures, and best practices established by the CMU Sports Medicine Department are upheld. Leads the annual review, update, and development of Emergency Action Plans (EAPs). Serves as a liaison to Risk Management and oversees emergency medical equipment and preparedness. Assists with the recruitment, onboarding, and supervision of entry level staff members. Compliance & Record Keeping: Adheres to all HIPAA and FERPA regulations, ensuring confidentiality and proper handling of sensitive information. Ensures compliance with NCAA , Mid-American Conference ( MAC ), and university standards and policies. Additional Duties: Participates in departmental meetings, continuing education, and professional development. Performs other duties as assigned. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position primarily works with Women\u2019s Basketball. Applicants are strongly encouraged to submit letters of recommendation. If you wish to include recommendation letter(s) that are not required, please utilize the Recommendation Letters upload field. Applicants are strongly encouraged to submit transcripts (unofficial or official) as a part of the application process. If there is an applicable certification document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the \u2018Certification\u2019 upload field. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $50,000 - $58,000 Division President Department Athletics - Sports Medicine Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.00 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have a bachelor's or master's degree in athletic training from an accredited institution? Yes No * Do you have at least three years of full-time experience as a certified athletic trainer? Yes No * Do you possess a certification as an Athletic Trainer, in good standing, with the National Athletic Trainer Association Board of Certification (NATABOC)? Yes No * Are you currently licensed as an Athletic Trainer (AT) in the state of Michigan, or are you eligible for licensure upon hire? Yes No * Do you currently possess a CPR/AED certification for the healthcare provider or equivalent? Yes No * Applicants for this position are subject to the following NCAA Bylaws: click here to view the NCAA Bylaws. You may be asked about these Bylaws in an interview, and you may be asked to sign a future affirmation confirming the same prior to or upon your employment by CMU, if you are selected for employment. Do you understand that by submitting your application for employment you are affirming that you have read these Bylaws, and that such Bylaws would not preclude your employment by CMU? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents List of References Transcript Copies Certification Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45576": {"title": "Commercial Music (Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor)", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | Commercial Music (Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. Commercial Music (Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. The search committee will begin reviewing applications on November 2, 2026, and will continue to accept applications until finalists are selected. Online applications must include: Cover Letter - that specifically addresses position qualifications, duties and includes a brief statement of teaching philosophy. Additionally, please provide links to audio or video work relevant to this position in your cover letter and/or CV. All links must be accessible by direct link (e.g., no further registration is required). Curriculum Vitae \u2013 that provides detailed evidence of successful teaching, work developing commercial music labs, other areas of expertise at the college level. Diversity Statement \u2013 that pertains to experiences fostering inclusion in higher education (upload under \u201cOther Document (1)\u201d). Transcript Copies - of undergraduate and graduate degree transcripts (upload as one document). List of References - contact information for at least three references who may be contacted and/or asked to submit a letter of recommendation. Address inquiries to: Chair, Commercial Music Search Committee School of Music Central Michigan University Mount Pleasant, MI 48859 Phone: (989) 774-3281 Fax: (989) 774-3766 Position Information Position Information Posting Number F-1065 Position Title Commercial Music (Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor) College/Unit College of the Arts & Media Home Department School of Music Employee Group Tenure-Track Faculty - Academic Year Employment Status Full-Time Position Type 9 month (Academic Year) Position Classification Tenure Track Faculty Position Begin Date 08/23/2027 Position End Date Position Summary Teach courses as assigned in Commercial Music and related areas of expertise. Organize and lead the development of coursework in the Commercial Music degree in conjunction with other music, media arts, and entrepreneurship faculty. Additional duties may be assigned in accordance with areas of expertise and in consultation with the Director of the School of Music. Required Qualifications Graduate degree in music production, music engineering, music technology, recording arts, or similar field. Commensurate professional experience in music production may be considered in lieu of a graduate degree. Professional teaching experience in higher education (beyond GA duties) in the field of music technology, production, or related areas. Experience using and teaching a variety of Digital Audio Workstations and virtual instruments. Experience producing and teaching a variety of popular musical styles and genres. Ability to perform the essential functions of the job with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching music theory fundamentals and aural skills for audio engineers. Experience teaching class guitar (electric and acoustic). Experience organizing/coaching/leading student popular music ensembles. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. The search committee will begin reviewing applications on November 2, 2026, and will continue to accept applications until finalists are selected. Online applications must include: Cover Letter \u2013 that specifically addresses position qualifications, duties and includes a brief statement of teaching philosophy. Additionally, please provide links to audio or video work relevant to this position in your cover letter and/or CV. All links must be accessible by direct link (e.g., no further registration is required). Curriculum Vitae \u2013 that provides detailed evidence of successful teaching, work developing commercial music labs, other areas of expertise at the college level. Diversity Statement \u2013 that pertains to experiences fostering inclusion in higher education (upload under \u201cOther Document (1)\u201d). Transcript Copies \u2013 of undergraduate and graduate degree transcripts (upload as one document). List of References \u2013 contact information for at least three references who may be contacted and/or asked to submit a letter of recommendation. Address inquiries to: Chair, Commercial Music Search Committee School of Music Central Michigan University Mount Pleasant, MI 48859 Phone: (989) 774-3281 Fax: (989) 774-3766 About the Department The School of Music is located in a state-of-the-art 119,000 square foot facility with a 500-seat concert hall housing a 61-rank Casavant organ, a 100-seat recital hall, recording facilities, and 79 practice rooms. The School of Music has 38 full- and part-time faculty and an enrollment of over 300 undergraduate and graduate majors and minors. To learn more about the school, visit the school website . Posting Begins 10/07/2026 Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Type of Recruitment External About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this vacancy? Please indicate the specific source by title (i.e., CMU website, HigherEdJobs.com, Higher Education Recruitment Consortium, The Chronicle, specific professional association, specific list serv, etc.): (Open Ended Question) Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Other Document (1) Transcript Copies List of References Optional Documents Other Document (2) Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45534": {"title": "ASSOCIATE REGISTRAR", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | ASSOCIATE REGISTRAR Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. ASSOCIATE REGISTRAR Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. For best consideration, please submit application materials on or before Wednesday, October 14, 2026. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3986 Position Number 33610 Type of Recruitment External Position Title ASSOCIATE REGISTRAR Position Summary Provides operational leadership for the Registrar\u2019s Office, overseeing student records, systems, processes, and services to ensure accuracy, efficiency, compliance, and a positive student experience. Works with the Student Information System ( SIS ), including system configuration and performance, student record creation and maintenance, and support of related systems. Leads process improvement initiatives and works with campus stakeholders to enhance data integrity, operational effectiveness, protected student data practices, and academic space utilization. Coordinates with campus offices to ensure accurate tracking and reporting of student enrollment and academic performance in accordance with applicable regulations. Performs complex administrative functions and interprets FERPA requirements related to the release of student information. Assists students, faculty, and staff with academic policy issues overseen by the Registrar\u2019s Office and exercises professional judgment in making exceptions to established policies and procedures when appropriate. Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree. Five years of increasingly responsible professional work experience, including at least two years in a higher education setting with demonstrated experience in higher education related information systems, data analytics and regulatory compliance. One year of supervisory experience. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively and build and maintain collaborative relationships. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree. Experience in implementing new technologies. Experience with process improvements for efficiency and accuracy. Collegiate level professional experiences in enrollment and student services functions. Duties & Responsibilities Supervision of an office staff comprised of Administrative Office Assistants and Professional Administrative employees. Serves as a member of the leadership team for the Office of the Registrar. Directs the employment and termination of employees in areas of responsibility. Analyzes and provides guidance on the relationship between business processes in areas of supervision and within the Registrar\u2019s Office. Corresponds with students, former students, faculty, staff, administrators and the public concerning matters regarding student record management. Coordinates configurations and updates to Student Information System regarding curricular changes, compliance, and policies, along with affiliated systems and campus partners. Develops, reviews and implements revisions to policies and procedures and recommends, implements, and assesses quality and effectiveness in their assigned areas of responsibility. Ensures business processes are documented and maintained to support continuity, risk mitigation, and staff transitions. Ensures student record management per the provisions of the Family Educational Rights and Privacy Act and other applicable state and institutional policies. Maintains expertise and proficiency in Student Information System. Manages, organizes and assesses functions and policies related to academic records management and registration and academic space scheduling in the Office of the Registrar. Provides leadership, direction, and oversight for academic space and course scheduling, academic records, and registration functions. Reviews, manages, implements and assesses policies and procedures related to student record management. Serves as liaison and coordinator with various campus offices and operational units regarding academic, student services and enrollment management issues. Works closely with academic Dean\u2019s Offices, academic department chairperson or designee(s), and other university officials in all matters relating to records and registration. Supervision Exercised Supervisors are expected to support the Leadership Standards of Central Michigan University and foster a culture that inspires excellence. The Leadership Standards define how we lead and treat others on our team. As leaders, it is our responsibility to seek input from our teams to continuously improve our leadership abilities and our demonstration of the standards. Additionally, it is our responsibility to encourage and support the growth and development of those whom we lead. At CMU , we encourage employees to grow both personally and professionally, and thus advance CMU\u2019s culture of excellence. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. For best consideration, please submit application materials on or before Wednesday, October 14, 2026. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $70,000 - $78,000 Division Student Recruitment & Retention Department Registrar's Office Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00am -5:00pm; occasional evenings and weekends Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department The Registrar\u2019s Office is an engaged university partner committed to continuous improvement and dedicated to supporting the CMU community. Our team of professionals works with integrity to provide accurate and effective services aligning with institutional policies and priorities, as well as notable national best practices. Above all else, we strive to contribute to the ultimate success of our students. Our department offers a hybrid work schedule with 3 days on-campus in Mt. Pleasant and 2 days remote. About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Supervisors are expected to support the Leadership Standards of Central Michigan University and foster a culture that inspires excellence. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position and click \u201cYes\u201d if you understand and support the culture that is important to CMU. Yes No * Do you have a bachelor's degree? Yes No * Do you have at least five years of increasingly responsible professional work experience, including at least two years in a higher education setting with demonstrated experience in higher education related information systems, data analytics and regulatory compliance? Yes No * Do you have one year of supervisory experience? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Recommendation Letters List of References Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/43916": {"title": "TEMPORARY MiCAREER MENTOR (PART-TIME)", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | TEMPORARY MiCAREER MENTOR (PART-TIME) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. TEMPORARY MiCAREER MENTOR (PART-TIME) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3761 Position Number 99999 Type of Recruitment External Position Title TEMPORARY MiCAREER MENTOR (PART-TIME) Position Summary MiCAREER Mentors are experienced educators who guide candidates through the educator credentialing process while fostering professional growth and confidence. Mentors play a vital role in addressing the teacher shortage by supporting candidates\u2019 unique needs and strengthening school communities. Required Qualifications Experienced (credentialed) educator with a strong understanding of classroom practice and professional standards. Excellent interpersonal and leadership skills, with the ability to mentor adults using an asset-based, supportive approach. Commitment to relationship-based mentoring and building community within schools and among colleagues. Flexibility to adapt support to the diverse needs of candidates, especially in rural or under-resourced contexts. Preferred Qualifications Duties & Responsibilities Builds strong trust-based relationships with candidates from the start of their MiCAREER journey. Provides individualized support tailored to candidate logistical goals and challenges (MiCAREER tasks), including instructional practices, MTTC preparation, and professional development. Advances logistical questions and troubleshooting challenges. Serves as a knowledgeable guide through credentialing requirements and program expectations. Fosters collaboration, reflection, and resilience through coaching conversations and ongoing check-ins. Participates in mentor training and professional learning to ensure alignment with program practices. Contributes to the growth of the MiCAREER mentoring model by sharing insights, refining supports, and collaborating with fellow mentors. Supervision Exercised Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Employee Group Temporary Staff Staff Pay Level 00 Pay Range $25.00 per hour Division Academic Affairs Department Teacher & Special Education Position Status Temporary Position End Date Employment Status Part-Time FTE 0.00 Position Type Other Weekly Work Schedule Hours will vary based upon needs of MiCareer. Not to exceed 25 hours per week. Location Michigan About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled No Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Experienced (credentialed) educator with a strong understanding of classroom practice and professional standards. Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45615": {"title": "BUSINESS PROCESS ANALYST I/II/III/SR", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | BUSINESS PROCESS ANALYST I/II/III/SR Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. BUSINESS PROCESS ANALYST I/II/III/SR Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Applicants are strongly encouraged to submit letters of recommendation. If you wish to include recommendation letter(s) that are not required, please utilize the Recommendation Letters upload field. If there is another applicable document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the Other Document (1) upload field. If there is an applicable certification document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the 'Certification' upload field. * This is a hybrid position with both remote and on-campus responsibilities. The position is expected to work on the Mount Pleasant campus a minimum of three days per week. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3972 Position Number 72805 Type of Recruitment External Position Title BUSINESS PROCESS ANALYST I/II/III/SR Position Summary The Business Process Analyst supports the university by assisting with the documentation, analysis, and improvement of business processes. This role involves collaborating with stakeholders to gather information, identify inefficiencies, and recommend solutions to enhance operations. They will work with stakeholders across the university to define processes and specify solutions which enable units to become more efficient and may conduct process audits to ensure the effectiveness of new processes. The level of the position (I, II, III , or Senior) reflects the scope of work, years of experience required, and level of autonomy Required Qualifications Business Process Analyst I: High school diploma or GED . One year of experience in business/systems analysis. Demonstrated understanding of analytical techniques. Demonstrated understanding of modeling notations and flowcharting. Basic understanding of process improvement methodologies (e.g., Lean, Six Sigma). Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite and basic data analysis tools. Demonstrated ability to identify specific business opportunities. Strong written and verbal communication skills including technical writing skills. Strong active listening, critical thinking, and analytical skills. Demonstrated resourcefulness and an ability to devise creative solutions to problems. Ability to negotiate effectively and assist with facilitating meetings. Ability to meet expectations as a reliable member of a team. Ability to escalate issues appropriately. Business Process Analyst II: Possess all of the required qualifications of a Business Process Analyst I, plus: Bachelor\u2019s degree or a combination of education and experience that equates to four years. Four additional years of experience in business/systems analysis. Demonstrated experience analyzing data to draw business-relevant conclusions and in data visualization techniques and tools. Demonstrated experience facilitating meetings and requirements gathering sessions. Demonstrated experience testing and mapping various business processes and protocols. Demonstrated knowledge in generating process documentation. Strong organizational and project management skills. Demonstrated ability to write clear and well-structured business requirements/documents. Advanced skills in Microsoft Office Suite and data visualization tools (e.g., Tableau, Power BI). Ability to effectively communicate and influence key stakeholders to support proposed strategies, process improvements, and operational decisions. Ability to present information for decision making purposes with little to no direction. Ability to negotiate effectively and facilitate meetings. Strong time management skills and increased acumen for planning. Business Process Analyst III : Possess all of the required qualifications of a Business Process Analyst II, plus: Five additional years of experience in business/systems analysis. Proficiency in using business process modeling and analysis tools such as BPMN , UML , Visio, or other related programs. Ability to quickly learn the objectives, structures, operations, and policies of a new business area. Demonstrated expertise in leading large-scale initiatives with measurable outcomes. Strong problem resolution, negotiation, and influencing skills. Strong analytical skills with the ability to collect, study, and interpret complex data. Adaptability and a willingness to learn new skills. Proven ability to lead cross-functional teams and influence senior stakeholders. Business Process Analyst Sr: Possess all of the required qualifications of a Business Process Analyst III , plus: Five additional years of experience in business/systems analysis. Demonstrated ability to break-down complex business scenarios or problems into process and data models. Proven ability to ask tough questions and negotiate professionally and creatively to ensure the success of the organization and projects. Proven ability to easily balance the organization\u2019s strategic vision with the daily operations of projects. Comfortability with presenting at the senior executive level. Proven ability to successfully mentor others. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of the BABOK\u00ae Guide and the agile extension to the BABOK\u00ae Guide. Knowledge of the PMBOK\u00ae Guide and Standards. Knowledge of the Agile Software Development frameworks and principles. Demonstrated experience with change management methodologies. Expertise in process improvement methodologies (e.g., Lean, Six Sigma, BPMN ). Knowledge of various enterprise level platforms widely used in higher education. Ability to resolve conflicts through effective stakeholder engagement. Ability to identify and document project risks, issues, assumptions, and dependencies. Ability to apply end-to-end thinking to business and system problems to ensure \u2018right first time\u2019 documentation and solutions. Duties & Responsibilities Business Process Analyst I: Consults with stakeholders to identify, define, and document business needs and objectives, including current as-is workflows. Identifies and documents issues and risks, as well as the root causes to those issues and risks, and identifies areas for improvement. Uses various techniques to understand business requirements, such as interviews, workshops, surveys, site visits, and storyboards. Develops and documents business process models with standard notation and tools to represent the process structure, logic, roles, inputs, outputs, and performance indicators. Translates conceptual user requirements into clear functional requirements. Works with business and delivery teams to prioritize requirements. Identifies and assists in prioritizing opportunities to streamline business processes. Creates process documentation and guidelines, including standard operating procedures and workflow diagrams. Performs other duties as assigned. Business Process Analyst II: Performs all duties and responsibilities of the Business Process Analyst I, plus: Performs data discovery, analysis and modeling. Defines configuration specifications and business analysis requirements including reporting, alerting, integrations, and technical. Develops and implements optimized processes and procedures to enhance efficiency, productivity, and customer satisfaction. Presents information for decision making purposes. Collaborates with stakeholders to design and execute process improvement initiatives aligned with organizational goals. Communicates the tradeoffs of technical options, limitations, costs, and risks to business partners and works with them to shape requirements accordingly. Helps resolve competing priorities between stakeholder groups by facilitating stakeholder discussions and escalates issues where appropriate. Collaborates with cross-functional teams to implement process changes, ensuring smooth transitions and minimal disruptions to operations. Business Process Analyst III : Performs all duties and responsibilities of the Business Process Analyst II, plus: Monitors and evaluates the effectiveness of implemented process changes, measuring key performance indicators, and making necessary adjustments for continuous improvement. Manages end-to-end process improvement projects with minimal supervision. Conducts in-depth analysis of complex workflows and recommend innovative solutions. Presents information at the senior executive level. Provides mentoring to team members. Assists with stakeholder engagement and organizational change management as changes are implemented. Business Process Analyst Sr: Performs all duties and responsibilities of the Business Process Analyst III , plus: Leads university-wide process improvement initiatives with significant complexity and scope. Helps strategy and business leaders understand, apply, monetize, and operationalize existing, new, and emerging technologies to transform and optimize business and operating models. Serves as a subject matter expert in process improvement and automation technologies. Engages key business stakeholders to identify business and technology innovation opportunities that enable and drive business strategy. Constructs deliverables that demonstrate how to move business processes toward realizing the University strategic goals and desired business outcomes. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Applicants are strongly encouraged to submit letters of recommendation. If you wish to include recommendation letter(s) that are not required, please utilize the Recommendation Letters upload field. If there is another applicable document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the Other Document (1) upload field. If there is an applicable certification document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the \u2018Certification\u2019 upload field. * This is a hybrid position with both remote and on-campus responsibilities. The position is expected to work on the Mount Pleasant campus a minimum of three days per week. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $52,000 - $92,000 per year (based on level) Division President Department University Transformation Office Position Status Provisional Position End Date 09/30/2031 Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI* About the Department Central Michigan University is engaged in a multi-year enterprise resource planning ( ERP ) transformation initiative. This provisional position has been established to support the successful implementation of the selected ERP solution and related business process improvements, either through direct participation in project activities or by providing operational coverage for employees dedicated to the implementation effort. About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Will you now or at any time in the future require CMU to file or support an immigration petition or application in order to begin or continue your employment authorization? Yes No * Do you have a high school diploma or GED? Yes No * Do you have at least one year of experience in business/systems analysis? Yes No * Do you have experience implementing or supporting an ERP implementation (Yes/No)? If yes, please briefly explain your role. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have any project management training or certifications (PMP, Scrum Master, etc.) (Yes/No)? If yes, please explain. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have any change management training or certifications (Prosci Certified Change Practitioner, etc.) (Yes/No)? If yes, please explain. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have any business process analysis training or certifications (Six Sigma, etc.) (Yes/No)? If yes, please explain. (Open Ended Question) Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Recommendation Letters Other Document (1) Certification Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the securi"}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45585": {"title": "Associate Dean, Research (Medical Faculty, Associate Professor/Professor)", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | Associate Dean, Research (Medical Faculty, Associate Professor/Professor) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. Associate Dean, Research (Medical Faculty, Associate Professor/Professor) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Letters of interest may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. To review Covenant HealthCare College of Medicine at Central Michigan University rank criteria please review the Faculty Appointment Manual . Position Information Position Information Posting Number F-1058 Position Title Associate Dean, Research (Medical Faculty, Associate Professor/Professor) College/Unit College of Medicine Home Department Covenant HealthCare College of Medicine at Central Michigan University Employee Group Medical Faculty Employment Status Full-Time Position Type 12 month Position Classification Medical Faculty Position Begin Date Position End Date Position Summary As a member of the Dean\u2019s Executive Leadership Team, the Associate Dean for Research serves as the Dean\u2019s principal advisor and accountable leader for advancing Covenant HealthCare College of Medicine\u2019s ( CMED ) research strategy, strengthening faculty and trainee research capacity, supporting growth in extramural funding, and integrating the research mission with the school\u2019s clinical, educational, and service missions. This role is designed to complement, not duplicate, the broader Central Michigan University research administration structure. Serves as a strategic liaison and advocate for CMED investigators by fostering transparency, facilitating cross-functional collaboration, and promoting alignment among administrative units throughout the grant lifecycle. The position collaborates closely with Central Michigan University ( CMU ) research administration leaders to ensure alignment with enterprise research strategy, sponsored programs processes, compliance requirements, research infrastructure, and cross-institutional opportunities. The Associate Dean for Research will provide leadership across the continuum of medical school research, including basic science, translational research, clinical research, population health, community-engaged research, clinical trials, and student and trainee scholarship. The role will also support a disciplined governance structure for setting research priorities, monitoring key performance indicators, identifying barriers to research growth, and advising the Dean on resource needs and strategic investments. The position will collaborate on oversight of research, research facilities, research administration, legal and risk management programs as they relate to research, and information technology programs as they relate to research. Assure alignment with the university\u2019s mission, assure responsiveness to the needs of the state, and assure a program of superior quality meeting the standards of the LCME , ACGME , HLC and other accrediting bodies. Required Qualifications MD-DO, PhD, PharmD, DVM or other terminal degree. Understanding of both basic sciences and translational research. Meets criteria for Associate Professor or Professor rank at CMU College of Medicine. Five years\u2019 experience in a university-based medical or public health school or research institution overseeing and conducting research. Five years of leadership experience overseeing university-based medical or public health or research institutional research. Demonstrated experience of securing extramural funding. Demonstrated understanding of clinical, translational, and basic science research. Experience in building/growing new research programs, ideally multi- disciplinary and/or multi-organizational research collaborations. Demonstrated creativity in building research partnerships and identifying research funding opportunities within their own. Positive interpersonal, written and oral communication skills. Ability to work effectively with multiple and diverse stakeholders. Demonstrated commitment to ensuring that members of the university community can thrive. Experience in mentoring junior faculty to help them obtain research funding to pursue meaningful lines or inquiry. Ability to perform the essential functions of the job with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Qualifications Experience in building/growing new research programs in partnership with public and private community entities, corporate partners, foundations, and state/federal agencies. Demonstrated administrative and research management skills with experience in compliance with research regulations and accreditation. Demonstrated experience leading, developing, and coordinating strategic research plans that are consistent with an organizational mission. Experience serving as an externally facing representative of the institution to key partners and stakeholders in the community and beyond. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Letters of interest may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. To review Covenant HealthCare College of Medicine at Central Michigan University rank criteria please review the Faculty Appointment Manual . About the Department The Covenant HealthCare College of Medicine at Central Michigan University educates diverse students and trains culturally competent physicians to provide comprehensive health care and services to underserved populations in Michigan and beyond. Our faculty, staff and graduates advance health and wellness through exceptional education, innovative research, quality patient care and strategic collaborations to improve the health and well-being of individuals and communities. Since its foundation in 2010, the Covenant HealthCare College of Medicine at Central Michigan University strives to be a national leader in the pursuit of basic, translational, clinical, medical education and population health research. We aim to develop programs to advance medical and scientific knowledge and improve patient care and community wellness. The ultimate goal is to contribute to the health of the public, the practice of medicine and the education of health professionals; all while promoting the development of academically oriented physicians. Research is an important mission of the Covenant HealthCare College of Medicine at Central Michigan University. We have nationally recognized investigators advancing the understanding of health sciences across a broad continuum of research types. Basic \u2013 Investigative research that advances our scientific understanding of issues affecting health. Translational \u2013 Research that applies the discoveries made by basic research investigators to studies with patients or to best practices in the field of medicine. Clinical \u2013 Medical research directly or indirectly involving patients that seeks to better understand and manage human illnesses. Population Health/Health Services \u2013 Research that examines the health care system and access to care, and the effect that care has on patients. Medical Education \u2013 The systematic study and investigation of various aspects related to the education and training of health care professionals, particularly those in the field of medicine. This type of research aims to enhance the quality, effectiveness, and outcomes of medical education programs, curricula, teaching methodologies, and assessment methods. Posting Begins 10/08/2026 Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Type of Recruitment External About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this vacancy? Please indicate the specific source by title (i.e., CMU website, HigherEdJobs.com, Higher Education Recruitment Consortium, The Chronicle, specific professional association, specific list serv, etc.): (Open Ended Question) Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Interest Statement of Research List of References Optional Documents Other Document (1) Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45437": {"title": "ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / STUDENT ENGAGEMENT", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / STUDENT ENGAGEMENT Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / STUDENT ENGAGEMENT Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3824 Position Number 78180 Type of Recruitment External Position Title ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / STUDENT ENGAGEMENT Position Summary Reporting to the Director for the Office of Multicultural Academic Student Services ( MASS ), the Assistant Director of Student Engagement contributes to the overall mission of the MASS Office by providing advisement and education to students and Registered Student Organizations (RSOs). This position supports students through the exploration of identity development and fosters an active learning environment that enhances their awareness on the ways culture informs community and personhood. The assistant director provides support for MASS and the Division of University Engagement and Student Affairs with cultural programming that aligns with divisional goals. The assistant director also collaborates with campus partners on student engagement, recruitment, retention, progress, and completion initiatives. Further, they are responsible for various levels of academic support, post-secondary education preparation, student retention, and advocacy programs. Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree, preferably in education, psychology, social work/sociology, leadership, human development or related area. Three years of professional experience focused on program development, advising/counseling, community engagement, or equivalent combination of education and experience in the areas listed above. Experience with advising undergraduates, including directing their participation and observing their growth in learning. Demonstrated commitment to inclusive excellence as it relates to the academic, personal, intellectual development of all students, faculty and staff. Demonstrated experience with cultivating a culture of creativity, care, and concern. Demonstrated ability to leverage highly effective and engaging verbal and written communication skills. Demonstrated experience coordinating initiatives between different units, offices, divisions, organizations, and/or communities. Ability to establish learning outcomes and assessing program effectiveness. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively within a team environment. Ability to work in a self-directed manner to meet due dates and to manage multiple tasks and activities. Ability to work occasional nights and weekends. Experienced proficiency with software applications, including Microsoft Office Suite, Adobe, Canva, Articulate, and Teams/WebEx/Zoom. Ability to perform the essential functions of this position, with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree preferably in Latin American studies, higher education, social work, leadership, student affairs/personnel, human development and family studies or a related area of study. Experience with program development and mentoring initiatives. Demonstrated commitment to social justice, student support and student development. Knowledge of graphic design and statistical software. Duties & Responsibilities Oversees the planning, design, marketing, implementation, and assessment of campus-wide programs, events, cultural celebrations, and community service endeavors. Creates educational programs that foster learning around issues related to social location and identity. Serves as a resource person, advisor, advocate, and mentor for students. Fosters and maintains relationships with campus and community partners in providing services that support student retention, benefit student health and well-being, and provides opportunities for academic and professional growth. Analyzes institutional data related to issues that impact the student experience. Provides data and assessment reports and/or presentations that highlight relevant departmental accomplishments, challenges, opportunities and recommendations to divisional leadership. Maintains a detailed record of projects including workplans, student outcomes, and recommendations, where applicable. Evaluates programming and responds to evolving needs. Contributes to department/office operations and strategic planning and investigates/shares best practices to advance services, efficiencies, communication plans and initiatives. Serves on various campus committees, panels, and events. Performs related responsibilities as required. Conducts and attends some evening programs. Additional duties as assigned. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $46,000 - $53,000 Division University Engagement and Student Affairs Department Multicultural Academic Student Services Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m.- 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department Multicultural Academic Student Services ( MASS ) supports the academic success, well-being, and graduation of multicultural students by providing culturally responsive programs, mentoring, advocacy, and community-building that promote persistence, engagement, and holistic development. About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Dispatcher Medical Faculty Office Professional P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have at least a bachelor's degree, preferably in education, psychology, social work/sociology, leadership, human development, or a related area? Yes No * Do you have at least three years of professional experience focused on program development, advising/counseling, community engagement, or equivalent combination of education and experience in the areas listed above? Yes No * Do you have experience with advising undergraduates, including directing their participation and observing their growth in learning? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Recommendation Letters Other Document (1) List of References Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45547": {"title": "University Coordinator/Student Teacher Supervisor", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | University Coordinator/Student Teacher Supervisor Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. University Coordinator/Student Teacher Supervisor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number F-1061 Position Title University Coordinator/Student Teacher Supervisor College/Unit College of Education & Human Services Home Department Office of Educator Preparation Programs Employee Group Fixed-Term Faculty - Academic Year Employment Status Part-Time Position Type One Semester Position Classification Fixed-Term Faculty Position Begin Date 01/07/2027 Position End Date 05/12/2027 Position Summary Central Michigan University\u2019s Office of Educator Preparation Programs seeks applicants for University Coordinator/Student Teacher Supervisor, who will provide field supervision for Spring 2027 Teacher Candidates. University Coordinators represent Central Michigan University as the coordinator of the student teaching clinical experience in the classrooms and schools in one of five student teaching centers across Michigan. University Coordinators support teacher candidates in the field through observations and coaching, communicate with PK-12 partners regarding clinical fieldwork requirements and policies, and support the academic programs of the University. University Coordinators are appointed on a semester by semester basis. Workload will not exceed 11 teacher candidates per semester. Duties and Responsibilities: Participate in appropriate coordinator meetings, departmental professional development activities, and online trainings. Follow the master syllabus for EDU 458/ SPE 456/ SPE 458/ SPE 558 and utilize allotted cohort time for collaboration and intervention related to teacher candidate success. Support candidates\u2019 growth in the field through observations; help candidates assess classroom situations and troubleshoot problems in the field. Complete all required paperwork, i.e. surveys, observations, and evaluations by the given deadlines. Work with Associate Director for Clinical Experiences or designee to secure placements, process initial scheduling, documentation, and placement materials for candidates, cooperating teachers, and clinical faculty. Project a positive representation of the department, college and university and act as a liaison between CMU and PK-12 school district stakeholders. Maintain a high level of awareness of schools\u2019 unique policies and exemplify professional courtesy while representing CMU on-site by honoring district procedures and minimizing disturbances. Maintain up to date on school legislation, current practices, and the needs of P-12 students served in the partnership schools. Communicate important information and support the policies of the Office of Educator Preparation Programs and CMU with candidates and cooperating teachers. Confer with candidates, cooperating teachers, clinical faculty, and the Associate Director for Clinical Experiences regarding candidates\u2019 performance. Project a positive image and embody the CMU Leadership Standards. Other duties as assigned. Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in education or a related field. Valid teaching certificate. Five years of teaching or administrative experience in the PK-12 school structure. Demonstrated dispositions and ability to mentor adult learners. Experience with teacher evaluation systems and providing feedback for improvement. Exceptionally strong communication, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Capacity to plan, establish priorities, and handle multiple tasks and projects within a set time line. Strong technology skills; ability to learn and use new software systems. Ability to perform the essential functions of the job, with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree with additional studies in an education-related field. Ten years of PK-12 teaching or administrative experience. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. About the Department The Office of Educator Preparation Programs collaborates with faculty members and teacher candidates from each college and academic program represented in the Professional Education Unit. During clinical fieldwork at all levels, the staff provide comprehensive support and communication to teacher candidates, cooperating teachers, and clinical faculty. To learn more about the center, visit the center website . Posting Begins 10/01/2026 Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Type of Recruitment External About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 19,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this vacancy? Please indicate the specific source by title (i.e., CMU website, HigherEdJobs.com, Higher Education Recruitment Consortium, The Chronicle, specific professional association, specific list serv, etc.): (Open Ended Question) * Do you have at least five years of teaching or administrative experience in the PK-12 school structure? Yes No * Describe your experiences with teacher evaluation systems and providing feedback for improvement. (Open Ended Question) * Explain your experiences with mentoring adult learners. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a Masters Degree or higher in education or a related field? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter List of References Optional Documents Recommendation Letters Other Document (1) Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/44305": {"title": "ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT TEMPORARY (PART-TIME)", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3797 Position Number 99999 Type of Recruitment External Position Title ADMINISTRATIVE OFFICE ASSISTANT TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Position Summary Part-time temporary administrative office assistant positions. No benefits. CMU occasionally has temporary administrative office assistant positions available in various departments. Duties and responsibilities vary by department but are primarily focused on providing secretarial support for specific departments. Responsibilities may include scheduling meetings, answering the phone, drafting correspondence and maintaining records. Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED Two years of qualifying experience or a combination of education and experience that equates to two years. Experience with Microsoft Word. Customer service experience. Organizational skills with strong attention to detail. Demonstrated positive interpersonal skills. Effective verbal and written communication skills. Ability to project a positive attitude. Ability to manage multiple projects and meet deadlines with accurate results. Ability to compose, proofread and edit correspondence. Ability to perform the essential functions of the job. Preferred Qualifications Spreadsheet and/or database experience. Experience working with financial records. Experience with SAP . Duties & Responsibilities Duties may include: Front line customer service. Scheduling meetings, appointments, facilities, and services for work area or for staff. Recording, monitoring, and tracking data/information. Maintaining records. Entering data into record keeping or electronic systems. Coordinating mailings; opening, reviewing and processing mail. Typing, proofreading, editing, and preparing correspondence. Other duties may be assigned. Supervision Exercised Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Employee Group Temporary Staff Staff Pay Level Pay Range To be determined by the hiring department Division Finance and Administrative Services Department Various Position Status Temporary Position End Date Employment Status Part-Time FTE 0.00 Position Type Other Weekly Work Schedule up to 25 hours per week; schedule to be determined by the hiring department Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled No Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a high school diploma or GED? Yes No * Do you have at least two years of qualifying experience or a combination of education and experience that equates to two years? Yes No * Do you have experience with Microsoft Word? Yes No * Do you have customer service experience? Yes No * Are you currently a CMU student enrolled at least half-time? If so, please view Student Employment Services job postings. Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45617": {"title": "USER SERVICES SPECIALIST", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | USER SERVICES SPECIALIST Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. USER SERVICES SPECIALIST Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. For best consideration, please submit application materials on or before Friday, October 2nd, 2026. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3974 Position Number 31170 Type of Recruitment External Position Title USER SERVICES SPECIALIST Position Summary Oversees User Services Operations Sunday through Thursday evenings. Shares oversight and responsibilities of the User Services functions that include: Collection Maintenance, Inventory, Microforms Printers/Copiers/Scanners, patron safety and compliance, and stewardship of the building. Hires, schedules, trains, supervises and evaluates student employees in all aspects of customer service and other functions of the unit. Required Qualifications Associate\u2019s degree. One year of library work experience or equivalent. Demonstrated ability to supervise and direct the work of others. Effective organizational skills and strong attention to detail and accuracy. Ability to handle multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Ability to work in a team setting while also having the capability to work independently with independent judgment and with minimum supervision. Demonstrated verbal and written communication skills. Demonstrated positive interpersonal skills. Demonstrated customer service skills. Ability to work evenings and weekends as assigned. Demonstrated effective problem resolution skills. Demonstrated ability to perform work using a variety of online systems and productivity tools. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree. Library public services experience. Experience searching library catalogs and databases. Understanding of the mission and the organization of the library. Duties & Responsibilities Provides direct user support of all types: interacts with students, faculty, staff and community users to provide assistance, solve problems and respond to questions and complaints. Oversees the safety of library users, user compliance with library policies and procedures, and the stewardship of the collections within the Park Library during assigned hours. Shares responsibility for building supervision and opening and closing. Troubleshoots and oversees the Print Q, public printer/copiers/scanners and other equipment. Shares student supervision responsibilities, which includes hiring, budgeting, scheduling, training, evaluating and developing training material with other Access/User Services student supervisors. Oversees all aspects of collection maintenance, which includes, shifting for space management, shelf-reading, inventory, stack straightening, repair of materials, and cleaning of all library collections. Assists with events and room set-ups. Participates with other Access/User Services team members to use a variety of technology tools. Oversees in house use processes. Performs in depth searches for missing library materials. Manages moveable shelving, by troubleshooting and putting in a service request for repair. Conducts special projects and serves on library committees. Participates in the Access and User Services Department which includes attending staff meetings and performing related responsibilities. Meets with other Access/User Services supervisors on a regular basis to share information and work through issues and problems. Meets regularly with the Coordinator of Access/User Services concerning projects and shared goals, and for problem solving. Works cooperatively and regularly with staff in other Library and University departments. Participates in continuing education activities to foster professional development and enhance job skills. Other duties as assigned. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. For best consideration, please submit application materials on or before Friday, October 2nd, 2026. Employee Group Supervisory Technical Staff Pay Level 1 Pay Range Starting Rate Between: $16.50 - $17.50 per hour Division Academic Affairs Department Libraries - Access & User Services Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Sun-Thursday, Evenings Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have an Associate's Degree? Yes No * Do you have one year of library work experience or equivalent? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents List of References Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45589": {"title": "ACCOUNTANT", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | ACCOUNTANT Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. ACCOUNTANT Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Applicants are required to provide three professional references, and at least one reference must be a current or former supervisor. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3967 Position Number 63130 Type of Recruitment External Position Title ACCOUNTANT Position Summary Responsible for providing financial accounting support for the university community. This includes ensuring the university is in compliance with: Generally Accepted Accounting Principles ( GAAP ); Governmental Accounting Standards Board ( GASB ) pronouncements and federal and state accounting related laws and regulations such as the IRS and/or the Uniform Guidance. Developing accounting related policies and procedures and ensuring the university community is adhering to them. Analyzing accounting records, reviewing department transactions, preparing accounting reports, providing SAP system training and completing special projects. Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree, preferably in accounting or a related field, or equivalent experience. One year of qualifying experience in accounting or finance. Experience with an ERP accounting system and in-depth experience utilizing Excel, experience with other MS Office functionality. Demonstrated organizational and analytical skills with attention to detail. Demonstrated ability to meet deadlines. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively, project a positive image and work effectively in a team environment. Preferred Qualifications Experience with fund accounting. Experience working in a higher education environment. Demonstrated ability in ERP system report writing. Demonstrated knowledge of SAP . Duties & Responsibilities Monitors, reviews and analyzes financial data for all transactions flowing through the assigned funds. Fund assignments may include one or more of the following funds: General, Designated, Auxiliary, Expendable Restricted, Endowment, Plant, Agency, Retirement & Insurance or Treasury. Reconciles university-wide bank accounts monthly. Researches GASB pronouncements and develops university policies and procedures to ensure compliance with such pronouncements. Researches IRS publications and prepares tax forms as needed. Researches discrepancies and assists departments in preparation of their annual budget reports; resolves problems in regard to accounting issues. Prepares detailed financial statements for the assigned funds along with supporting documentation and variance analysis. Prepares and provides schedules, analysis and reconciliation reports to internal, external independent, state and federal auditors. Assists departments in meeting their accounting and auditing requirements for assigned funds. This may include federal, state or private grants and contracts, PBS or NCAA . Creates chart of accounts master data in SAP , updates data sets for all financial reports and communicates and/or trains departments on impact. Tests semi-annual updates to SAP financial modules (Finance, Funds Management, Controlling, Grants Management, Asset Management, Materials Management, Accounts Payable and Accounts Receivable). Collaborates with OIT and other departments to develop and test new functionality in SAP . Provides SAP training to employees. Develops and prepares specialized SAP reports for senior management and campus departments. Completes SAP month end close procedures in the financial system. Performs other duties as assigned. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Applicants are required to provide three professional references, and at least one reference must be a current or former supervisor. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $54,000 - $66,000 Division Finance and Administrative Services Department Accounting Services Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon - Fri, 8 a.m. - 5 p.m. / Evenings and weekends as necessary Location On-campus in Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department The department is committed to providing high-quality service and support to the Central Michigan University community. Team members work in a fast-paced environment that requires a high level of accuracy, attention to detail, and a commitment to excellence. Success in the department is built on both collaboration and individual initiative, requiring employees to work effectively as part of a team while also being self-motivated and accountable for their responsibilities. This is an on-campus position located in Mount Pleasant, Michigan, and requires regular in-person attendance. About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have a Bachelor's degree, preferably in accounting or a related field, or equivalent experience? Yes No * Do you have one year of qualifying experience in accounting or finance? Yes No * Do you have experience with an ERP accounting system and in-depth experience utilizing Excel and MS Office functionality? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents List of References Other Document (1) Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45457": {"title": "Environmental Engineering (Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor)", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | Environmental Engineering (Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. Environmental Engineering (Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Please submit the following materials: cover letter (2 page max) CV statement of teaching philosophy (2 page max) statement of research (2 page max) contact information for 3 professional references Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position is open until filled, although priority consideration will be given to applications completed by October 19, 2026. Position Information Position Information Posting Number F-1054 Position Title Environmental Engineering (Tenure-Track, Assistant Professor) College/Unit College of Science and Engineering Home Department School of Engineering and Technology Employee Group Tenure-Track Faculty - Academic Year Employment Status Full-Time Position Type 9 month (Academic Year) Position Classification Tenure Track Faculty Position Begin Date 08/23/2027 Position End Date Position Summary The School of Engineering & Technology at Central Michigan University invites applicants for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position to support the Environmental Engineering program. The start date for this position is August 2027. We seek a colleague with expertise in any aspect of Environmental Engineering, but preference will be given to candidates with backgrounds in one of the following areas: Environmental remediation Solid and hazardous waste engineering Molecular biology techniques for environmental engineering (e.g., qPCR, metagenomics, etc.) Air pollution engineering The selected candidate is expected to teach undergraduate and graduate courses and laboratories, develop an externally funded research program, advise students in research and capstone design projects, and contribute service to benefit the program, School, College, University, profession, and surrounding community. The selected candidate will teach required and elective courses in the Environmental Engineering program but may also teach general engineering and engineering technology courses (depending on specific expertise) that support all programs within the School. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Environmental Engineering, Ecological Engineering, Civil Engineering, Chemical Engineering or a related field. Candidates with a Ph.D. in a related, non-engineering field must have an undergraduate engineering degree in one of the disciplines listed above to be considered for this position. Exceptional ABD candidates will be considered if their degree is completed by the start of the appointment. Potential for outstanding teaching at the undergraduate and graduate levels and the ability to teach core and elective courses offered within the School. Demonstrated record of quality research and ability to develop a rigorous scholarship program that involves students. Strong commitment to research that attracts external funding and leads to publications in competitive peer-reviewed journals. Commitment to student success and fostering a supportive environment for every member of our university community. Excellent oral and written communication skills. Ability to perform the essential functions of the job with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated record of effective teaching as the lead instructor. Demonstrated record of securing external funding. Postdoctoral experience (academic or industry). Experience integrating high impact teaching practices (e.g., active learning, project-based learning) into the classroom. Professional engineering licensure, or possibility of obtaining licensure in the near future. Relevant industrial or government experience. Background in environmental remediation, solid and hazardous waste engineering, molecular biology techniques for environmental engineering (e.g., qPCR, metagenomics, etc.), or air pollution engineering. Message to Applicants You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Please submit the following materials: cover letter (2 page max) CV statement of teaching philosophy (2 page max) statement of research (2 page max) contact information for 3 professional references Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position is open until filled, although priority consideration will be given to applications completed by October 19, 2026. About the Department The School of Engineering and Technology ( SET ) is housed in the College of Science and Engineering ( CSE ). SET has four undergraduate Engineering (Mechanical, Electrical, Computer, and Environmental Engineering), three undergraduate Engineering Technology (Industrial, Mechanical, and Product Design Engineering Technology) and a graduate (MS in Engineering) program. All undergraduate programs are accredited by ABET . SET presently has 24 full-time faculty members. Courses are taught in an attractive 70,000 square foot engineering & technology building which houses more than twenty laboratories and support spaces. Posting Begins 09/14/2026 Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Type of Recruitment External About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this vacancy? Please indicate the specific source by title (i.e., CMU website, HigherEdJobs.com, Higher Education Recruitment Consortium, The Chronicle, specific professional association, specific list serv, etc.): (Open Ended Question) * Please select the discipline of your PhD degree. Environmental Engineering Ecological Engineering Civil Engineering Chemical Engineering Other engineering Other non-engineering * Please select the discipline of your undergraduate degree. Environmental Engineering Ecological Engineering Civil Engineering Chemical Engineering Other engineering Other non-engineering * Do you have expertise in one or more of the following areas? Environmental remediation Solid and hazardous waste engineering Molecular biology techniques for environmental engineering (e.g., qPCR, metagenomics, etc.) Air pollution engineering Other area of environmental engineering Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Statement of Teaching Philosophy Statement of Research List of References Optional Documents Evidence of Teaching Effectiveness Other Document (1) Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45620": {"title": "LABORATORY TECHNICIAN", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | LABORATORY TECHNICIAN Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. LABORATORY TECHNICIAN Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. For best consideration, please submit application materials on or before November 4, 2026. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3993 Position Number 76360 Type of Recruitment External Position Title LABORATORY TECHNICIAN Position Summary The Lab Technician works under the supervision of the Vivarium Manager to support the vivarium and the Office of Laboratory and Field Safety ( OLFS ). This position encompasses multiple tasks and areas in the vivarium and the registered laboratory spaces across campus to comply with all policies pertaining to the animal care program and laboratory health and safety. Required Qualifications Associate\u2019s degree preferably in veterinary technology or basic science or certification in veterinary technology. One year of experience in a lab animal research vivarium, or closely related environment. Strong skills in Microsoft Office, (Word, Excel, Outlook), databases and data collection systems. Demonstrated effective communication skills, both written and verbal. Knowledge of vivarium equipment and supplies. Willingness to work a flexible schedule, including nights, weekends and holidays as necessary. Ability to frequently lift between 25-75 lbs. Ability to wear Personal Protective Equipment which may include multiple types of respirators. Required to pass the Occupational Risk Assessment medical evaluation prior to starting in the position. Experience complying with health and safety regulations. Working knowledge of the care, handling, and treatment of research and teaching animals. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor of Science degree. AALAS certification at the LATG level. Two years of experience working in a lab animal vivarium environment. Two years of experience complying with health and safety regulations. Experience working with laboratory rodents. Experience managing rodent breeding colonies. Experience assisting with training. Duties & Responsibilities Performs animal husbandry and animal handling activities including but not limited to: observation, feeding, watering, sanitizing, cleaning, disinfecting, cage changes, cage washing, cage and accessory assembly and sanitation, facility disinfection, autoclaving procedures and monitoring consistent with facility SOPs, State, Federal and University regulations. Reports facility malfunctions and deficiencies to the vivarium manager. Maintains and records animal care and animal room information. Monitors the health and well-being of the animals, recognizes deviations from normal health status and communicates animal conditions to appropriate staff. Assists and/or performs documentation, data collection and record keeping of the animals, housing parameters, standard environmental and equipment requirements, as well as monitors and reports deviations to the vivarium manager. Operates equipment and uses supplies following safety guidelines; performs general housekeeping and adheres to safety procedures; complies with safety policies and procedures and safety data sheet ( SDS ) guidelines. Performs air sampling/monitoring, ventilation testing, wipe testing, safety inspections, and other tasks to support the health and safety programs (chemical, biological, laser, radiological, industrial, and field safety). Assists with managing SAP SuccessFactors online safety training platform- assigns training(s) for lab workers and addresses related processes for online training. Manages inventory and ordering for the vivarium and OLFS . Assists with Lab Registration Manager administration and oversees creation and posting of laboratory door signs. Processes incoming Facilities Management (FM) Lab Hazard and Area Preparation forms \u2013 carries out subsequent communication with FM and associated faculty/staff/departments. Assists with administrative tasks related to OLFS email, training record confirmation, access control, and lab coat rental program (MSforms processing/organizing, recordkeeping). Other duties as assigned. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. For best consideration, please submit application materials on or before November 4, 2026. Employee Group Supervisory Technical Staff Pay Level 2 Pay Range Starting Rate Between: $19.00 - $22.00 per hour Division Academic Affairs Department Laboratory & Field Safety Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule M-F, 8-5, occasional flexible schedule, including nights, weekends, and holidays as necessary. Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have an associate's degree preferably in veterinary technology or basic science or certification in veterinary technology? Yes No * Do you have one year of experience in a lab animal research vivarium, or closely related environment? Yes No * Do you have the ability to lift between 25 - 75 pounds with or without reasonable accommodation? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents List of References Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45549": {"title": "JOURNEYMAN PLUMBER (3 POSITIONS)", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | JOURNEYMAN PLUMBER (3 POSITIONS) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. JOURNEYMAN PLUMBER (3 POSITIONS) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. If there is another applicable document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the Other Document (1) upload field. 3 positions available in Mt. Pleasant, Michigan. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3849 Position Number 42570, 42470, 69920 Type of Recruitment External Position Title JOURNEYMAN PLUMBER (3 POSITIONS) Position Summary Performs skilled plumbing work in the installation, maintenance, inspection, and repair, of plumbing systems and related fixtures in accordance with applicable codes, safety standards, and industry best practices. This work involves diagnosing issues, interpreting blueprints, selecting appropriate materials, and ensuring proper functioning of water supply and waste disposal. This position may also coordinate with contractors or other trades and is responsible for ensuring high-quality workmanship, customer service, and compliance with local and state plumbing regulations. Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED . Possession of a State of Michigan Journeyman Plumbing License. Possession of a valid driver\u2019s license. Ability to become an approved driver under the university\u2019s vehicle policy. Ability to obtain ASSE Backflow Prevention Certification within 12 months of hire. Ability to work independently and effectively in a team environment. Ability to provide a high level of service excellence to campus customers. Ability to work from blueprints, drawings, and sketches. Ability to effectively use technology to access e-mail and the internet. Demonstrated ability to follow and/or interpret oral or written directions. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively. Demonstrated positive interpersonal skills. Ability to be on-call. Ability to lift 75 pounds. Ability to safely use a ladder. Ability to work in confined spaces. Ability to safely use power equipment and hand tools. Ability to work outdoors in all seasons. Ability to work an 8-hour shift, overtime, weekends, nights, and holidays. Preferred Qualifications Duties & Responsibilities Repairs, replaces, maintains, and installs the following: - Fixtures, faucets, and fixture fittings - Water heaters - Water supply and distribution lines - Sanitary drainage - Indirect/special waste - Plumbing vents - Traps, interceptors, and separators - Storm drainage systems - Special piping and storage systems - Potable/non-potable water systems - Subsurface gray water Maintains and repairs swimming, rehabilitation, and hydrotherapy pool systems. Plans work and obtains necessary materials, equipment, and supplies. Operates all required tools and equipment including but not limited to power equipment and hand tools. Conducts preventive maintenance. Troubleshoots, develops, and implements solutions. Conducts miss dig utility location services. Works effectively with other skill trades. Keeps necessary records as required. Requests supplies and equipment as necessary. Performs other duties related to the job classification as assigned. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. If there is another applicable document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the Other Document (1) upload field. 3 positions available in Mt. Pleasant, Michigan. Employee Group Service Maintenance Staff Pay Level 10 Pay Range $32.85 per hour (non-negotiable) / + recruitment bonus (and moving expense reimbursement, if applicable) Division Finance and Administrative Services Department PLUMBING SHOP Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon - Fri, 7:30 a.m. to 4:00 p.m. / some nights and weekends as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have a high school diploma or GED? Yes No * Do you possess a State of Michigan Journeyman Plumbing License? Yes No * Do you have a valid Driver's License? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document (1) Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/44324": {"title": "ACADEMIC TUTOR/FACILITATOR TEMPORARY (PART-TIME)", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | ACADEMIC TUTOR/FACILITATOR TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. ACADEMIC TUTOR/FACILITATOR TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3806 Position Number 99999 Type of Recruitment External Position Title ACADEMIC TUTOR/FACILITATOR TEMPORARY (PART-TIME) Position Summary Provides academic assistance to students in all academic areas and workshop facilitation as needed. Tutors work with TRIO Detroit Upward Bound and Educational Talent Search programs in Southwest and Northwest, Detroit within our target schools. Required Qualifications High school diploma or GED . Completion of at least one year of college courses. Demonstrated knowledge and competence in all subject matters. Ability to explain concepts to others effectively. Effectively communicate study strategies to ensure academic success. Ability to work comfortably with people from diverse backgrounds. Possess good organizational skills. Exhibits patience and positive attitudes in establishing an encouraging learning environment. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree. Prior teaching or tutoring experience. Duties & Responsibilities Reports to TRIO Staff on student progress. Provides academic assistance to students, either in a group or individually. Instructs on all academic areas such as math, reading, science to improve basic skills. Assists students with SAT preparation. Maintains records on each student who is being tutored, including follow-up. Assists students in developing the study skills necessary for academic success. Provides interventions to address observed barriers that may reduce the participant\u2019s chances of successfully completing the program or academics. Utilizes a variety of teaching resources to develop program participants\u2019 knowledge of subject area. Facilitates workshops as needed. Performs other tasks as assigned. Supervision Exercised Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Employee Group Temporary Staff Staff Pay Level Pay Range To be determined Division Student Recruitment & Retention Department TRIO PROGRAMS - DETROIT Position Status Temporary Position End Date Employment Status Part-Time FTE 0.00 Position Type Other Weekly Work Schedule Up to 20 hrs/week; M-F and occasional Saturdays Location Detroit, MI within partnering Middle and High Schools. About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a high school diploma or GED? Yes No * Have you completed at least one year of college level courses? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45591": {"title": "COORDINATOR - ASSESSMENT &amp; PROGRAM EVALUATION / COLLEGE OF MEDICINE", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | COORDINATOR - ASSESSMENT &amp; PROGRAM EVALUATION / COLLEGE OF MEDICINE Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. COORDINATOR - ASSESSMENT & PROGRAM EVALUATION / COLLEGE OF MEDICINE Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3973 Position Number 79400 Type of Recruitment External Position Title COORDINATOR - ASSESSMENT & PROGRAM EVALUATION / COLLEGE OF MEDICINE Position Summary The Office of Assessment and Evaluation is responsible for collecting and reporting data necessary to evaluate the performance of the Medical Degree curriculum and continuation of LCME accreditation. Within this office, the assessment and program evaluation coordinator primarily supports projects related to institutional and program evaluations. This position oversees data reporting from both quantitative and qualitative methods. The assessment and program evaluation coordinator\u2019s primary role is to create, monitor, and report on evaluations using questionnaires and surveys to support these efforts. The position will provide mission-critical administrative support for all evaluation, monitoring, and reporting activities necessary for accreditation and continuous quality improvement. Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree or a combination of education and experience that equates to four years. Two years of progressively responsible, relevant experience of a qualifying nature. Demonstrated experience with Microsoft Word and Excel or other related software. Demonstrated experience with basic evaluation and survey programs such as Microsoft Forms or Qualtrics. Ability to organize and document work effectively. Ability to handle multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment. Demonstrated organizational, project management, and time management skills. Ability to work independently and commit to teamwork and collaboration. Written and oral communication skills, with attention to detail and accuracy. Strong interpersonal and customer service skills. Ability to multitask and complete work within required timelines. Proficiency with computers and databases. Ability to maintain confidentiality. Preferred Qualifications Demonstrated experience working in higher education. Demonstrated experience with accreditation. Strong analytical skills. Familiarity with medical education. Demonstrated experience in database management. Duties & Responsibilities Builds, manages, and reports on institutional evaluations, including student, course, and faculty surveys and evaluations. Plans and designs surveys/evaluations. Maintains a schedule for timely generation and distribution of course, student, faculty, and institutional surveys/evaluations. Implements and manages live surveys/evaluations, promptly resolving any inconsistencies or issues. Ensures high-quality output across all surveys/evaluations through ongoing review of survey-building processes and methodologies. Works with the director to analyze data collected in evaluations. Prepares findings for review of courses, clerkships, segments, and the overall curriculum. Prepares detailed reports and presentations for administrative and committee review. Participates in institutional meetings, including the continuous quality improvement committee and other committees as appointed or directed. Prepares materials and reports for accreditation, ensuring the curriculum meets standards set by medical education accrediting bodies. Coordinates with other Office of Assessment and Evaluation team members on evaluation and assessment projects as requested/assigned. Proctors exams. Performs other related duties as assigned. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $50,000 - $60,000 per year Division Academic Affairs Department College of Medicine Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have a bachelor\u2019s degree or a combination of education and experience that equates to four years? Yes No * Do you have two years of progressively responsible, relevant experience of a qualifying nature? Yes No * Do you have experience with Microsoft Word and Excel, or other related software? Yes No * Do you have experience with basic evaluation and survey programs such as Microsoft Forms or Qualtrics? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents List of References Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45474": {"title": "Bachelor of Science in Nursing Lecturer", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | Bachelor of Science in Nursing Lecturer Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. Bachelor of Science in Nursing Lecturer Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Position Information Position Information Posting Number F-1037 Position Title Bachelor of Science in Nursing Lecturer College/Unit The Herbert H. and Grace A. Dow College of Health Professions Home Department School of Rehabilitation and Medical Sciences Employee Group Fixed-Term Faculty - Academic Year Employment Status Full-Time Position Type 10 month Position Classification Fixed-Term Faculty Position Begin Date 08/24/2026 Position End Date Position Summary The Nursing Program at Central Michigan University invites applications for a full-time fixed-term faculty position beginning in August 2026 for the Fall 2026 semester. The successful candidate will provide instructional leadership in maternity and pediatric nursing, including didactic teaching and oversight of clinical instructors assigned to related clinical courses. The faculty member will also teach other nursing courses as assigned based on program needs. Other teaching-related activities of this position may include student advising and satisfying accreditation or professional standards, where applicable. This position requires collaboration with faculty, staff, and clinical instructors to support student success, course quality, and program effectiveness. The successful candidate is expected to contribute to course coordination, curriculum implementation, and ongoing program development. Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Nursing from an accredited institution. Current unencumbered registered nurse license. Eligibility for registered nurse licensure in the State of Michigan. Recent clinical expertise in maternity, pediatric, or related nursing practice. Demonstrated effective oral and written communication skills. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with students, faculty, staff, and community partners. Ability to perform the essential functions of the job with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Qualifications Earned doctorate in Nursing or related field (e.g., DNP , PhD, EdD). Prior teaching experience in prelicensure nursing education. Experience teaching maternity and/or pediatric nursing content. Experience coordinating courses and working with clinical instructors. Experience with curriculum development, course revision, and student evaluation. Demonstrated commitment to student success and excellence in nursing education. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. About the Department The Pre-Licensure Bachelor of Science in Nursing Program is located within the School of Rehabilitation and Medical Sciences in The Herbert H. and Grace A. Dow College of Health Professions. The Herbert H. and Grace A. Dow College of Health Professions consists of five academic units (Department of Physical Therapy, Department of Physical Education and Sport, Department of Communication Sciences and Disorders, the School of Health Sciences, and the School of Rehabilitation and Medical Science). The college offers undergraduate and/or graduate degree programs in athletic training, audiology, communication sciences and disorders, exercise science, environmental health and safety, health administration, physical activity specialist, physical education, physical therapy, physician assistant, public health, school and public health education, speech-language pathology, and sport management, delivered by 100+ faculty/staff. To learn more about the College, please visit our website . Posting Begins 05/13/2026 Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Type of Recruitment External About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this vacancy? Please indicate the specific source by title (i.e., CMU website, HigherEdJobs.com, Higher Education Recruitment Consortium, The Chronicle, specific professional association, specific list serv, etc.): (Open Ended Question) Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Statement of Teaching Philosophy Transcript Copies Personal Statement Optional Documents Other Document (1) Certification Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45551": {"title": "CONTRACT MANAGER", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | CONTRACT MANAGER Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. CONTRACT MANAGER Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. For best consideration, please submit application materials by October 22, 2026. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3987 Position Number 00420 Type of Recruitment External Position Title CONTRACT MANAGER Position Summary Responsible for all activities concerning the purchase of complex commodity assignments of material and service for the operation of the university. Responsibilities include assignments of major contracts and significant authority to independently make purchasing decisions for the university. Serves as support and backup to the Director of Contracting & Purchasing. Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree or combination of education and experience that equates to four years, preferably in business administration, legal studies, contracting or a closely related field. At least 3 years\u2019 experience of a qualifying nature. Ability to perform complex financial analysis. Demonstrated organizational and prioritization skills. Strong analytical skills, sound decision making skills. Demonstrated negotiation skills/confidence. Ability to develop and maintain interpersonal relationships. Demonstrated ability to project a positive attitude through excellent written and verbal communication skills. Preferred Qualifications Advanced degree, such as Master of Business Administration ( MBA ), Juris Doctor (J.D.), or related field. 5 or more years of experience of a qualifying nature. Certification in the procurement field ( CPM , CPPB , etc.) Experience in public construction procurement. Experience in contract management (including training of others). Experience with Uniform Guidance procurement requirements. Technical experience with a modern ERP including procurement and contract management systems. Duties & Responsibilities Prepares and reviews contracts (including independent contracts), processes RFP\u2019s and purchase orders. Ensures compliance with contracting authority on the University Contract Review Policy and Process Trains CMU faculty and staff with contracting authority on the Contract Review Policy and Process Supports the administration and optimization of procurement and contracting technology platforms and ensure related business processes and policies are in alignment with the technology platforms. Coordinates Contracting and Purchasing Services ERP technical/programming needs between areas and ERP functional analyst. Oversees Contract renewal process to ensure timely renewals in compliance with contractual requirements. Liaison functions between Purchasing, Facilities Management, and campus departments for construction/renovation projects. Investigates and negotiates conflict resolution regarding claims related to delivery, invoicing or vendor non-performance. Works with the Director of Contracting & Purchasing Services to develop, review/revise administrative and purchasing procedures to ensure efficient department operations. Oversees Conflict of Interest policy and disclosure statement process. Monitors and coordinates grant funded activities as they relate to purchasing. Acts as liaison with other departments supporting and managing grants. Ensures University is current with all purchasing trends. Monitors and communicates applicable local, state, and federal statutes and administrative regulations to ensure compliance. Meets with departments and end users to develop professional relationships and to provide education. Other duties as assigned. Supervision Exercised Supervisors are expected to support the Leadership Standards of Central Michigan University and foster a culture that inspires excellence. The Leadership Standards define how we lead and treat others in our teams. As leaders, it is our responsibility to seek input from our teams to continuously improve leadership abilities and demonstration of the standards. Additionally, it is our responsibility to encourage and support the growth and development of those whom we lead. At CMU , we encourage employees to grow both personally and professionally, and thus advance CMU\u2019s culture of excellence. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. For best consideration, please submit application materials by October 22, 2026. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $72,000 - $87,000 Division Finance and Administrative Services Department Contracting & Purchasing Services Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule M-F 8 am-5 pm, other times as needed. Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have at least a bachelor's degree or a combination of education and experience that equates to four years, preferably in business administration, legal studies, contracting, or a closely related field? Yes No * Do you have at least 3 years' experience of a qualifying nature? Yes No * Supervisors are expected to support the Leadership Standards of Central Michigan University and foster a culture that inspires excellence. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position and click \u201cYes\u201d if you understand and support the culture that is important to CMU. Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Other Document (1) Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/44897": {"title": "INDUSTRIAL HYGIENIST TEMPORARY", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | INDUSTRIAL HYGIENIST TEMPORARY Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. INDUSTRIAL HYGIENIST TEMPORARY Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3886 Position Number 99999 Type of Recruitment External Position Title INDUSTRIAL HYGIENIST TEMPORARY Position Summary Temporary position. No benefits. Assists the Director of the Office of Laboratory and Field Safety with implementing various lab safety programs on campus. Works in coordination with campus community while providing laboratory safety services (chemical, biological, radiological, and laser). Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree in industrial hygiene, environmental health & safety, health physics, chemistry, biology, or a related field. One year of experience in a health and safety profession or in a laboratory setting. Effective written and verbal communication skills, including experience with group presentations. Demonstrated computer experience with business software applications, including MS Word, Excel and/or Access. Ability to work varied hours depending on campus activities, training schedules, etc. Experience with OSHA and EPA regulations and their application in a laboratory setting. Ability to pass a HAZMAT medical examination and be medically qualified to wear respiratory protection devices. Ability to lift safety equipment weighing up to fifty pounds and move fifty-five gallon drums with appropriate equipment. Must possess a valid driver\u2019s license and be able to drive University vehicles and respond to after-hours emergencies. Knowledge of use and operation of health & safety monitoring/testing equipment including but not limited to gas monitors and personal protective equipment. Report writing experience. Demonstrated ability to build rapport, communicate effectively, and project a positive image. Preferred Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in Industrial Hygiene, Occupational/Environmental Health, Health Physics or a related scientific discipline. OSHA HAZWOPER Technician Training Experience working in a higher education environment. Research experience. Knowledge of use and operation of radiation survey equipment. Certified Industrial Hygienist preferred. Duties & Responsibilities Assists the director of the Office of Laboratory and Field Safety with the implementation of lab safety programs to safeguard employees and ensure legal compliance. Conducts lab inspections, generates reports and ensures resultant violations are addressed by the department and laboratory with appropriate timeframes. Conducts lab accident investigations. Assists with hazard assessments to develop lab door signage. Performs ventilation testing and air sampling. Assists in safe transportation and/or disposal of hazardous material. Calibrates and maintains equipment. Maintains databases for biological, chemical, radiological and laser safety items. Assists the director of the Office of Laboratory and Field Safety with safety committee duties and activities (Lab Safety Committee, Radiation Safety Committee, Laser Safety Committee, Institutional Biosafety Committee). Develops and conducts training (conventional and online) to employees and students on environmental, health and safety topics. Responds to hazardous materials releases on campus and assists in/or abates the release of hazardous materials. Supervision Exercised None Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Employee Group Temporary Staff Staff Pay Level Pay Range TBD Division Academic Affairs Department Laboratory & Field Safety Position Status Temporary Position End Date Employment Status Part-Time FTE 0.00 Position Type Other Weekly Work Schedule TBD (up to 40 hours/week through 8/29/26 then up to 25 hours/week starting 8/30/2026) Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Do you have a bachelor's degree in industrial hygiene, environmental health & safety, health physics, chemistry, biology or a related field? Yes No * Do you have at least one year of experience in a health and safety profession or in a laboratory setting? Yes No * Do you have experience with OSHA and EPA regulations and their application in a laboratory setting? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Cover Letter Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45624": {"title": "DIRECTOR / FACULTY DEVELOPMENT - COLLEGE OF MEDICINE", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | DIRECTOR / FACULTY DEVELOPMENT - COLLEGE OF MEDICINE Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. DIRECTOR / FACULTY DEVELOPMENT - COLLEGE OF MEDICINE Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Applicants are strongly encouraged to submit letters of recommendation. If you wish to include recommendation letter(s) that are not required, please utilize the Recommendation Letters upload field. If there is another applicable document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the Other Document (1) upload field. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3995 Position Number 73420 Type of Recruitment External Position Title DIRECTOR / FACULTY DEVELOPMENT - COLLEGE OF MEDICINE Position Summary As a member of the Office of Medical Education team, the director of faculty development will provide oversight of faculty development activities focusing primarily on those associated with improvement of teaching, assessment and evaluation skills. The director will be expected to assist faculty in the development of educational scholarship. The director is expected to possess a strong understanding of instructional methodology and learning pedagogy, and be able to design and evaluate training and development programs to support faculty in the design and evaluation of quality learning experiences. Under the direction of the faculty appointed assistant dean of faculty development, the director will develop, deliver, and evaluate professional development activities for faculty and learners (students and residents). Required Qualifications Master\u2019s degree in medical education, higher education, psychology, or a related field. Four years of relevant experience in a higher education environment. Demonstrated ability to work effectively with multiple diverse stakeholders, including faculty, administrators, and students. Demonstrated scholarly activity, such as publication/presentation of educational and/or training materials activities. Demonstrated ability to work effectively in a complex environment. Excellent interpersonal, written, and verbal communication skills. Organizational skills sufficient to handle multiple tasks, manage multiple projects, prioritize workload, and meet deadlines. Ability to travel and work a flexible schedule. Demonstrated commitment to ensuring members of the university community can thrive. Preferred Qualifications Doctorate degree. Demonstrated experience with LCME medical school accreditation and ACGME accreditation in a school or survey team capacity. Demonstrated experience with grant writing. Demonstrated experience in health professions education. Demonstrated experience in developing and implementing faculty development programs. Knowledge of graduate medical education program requirements and competencies. Appreciation for the importance of interdisciplinary education. Demonstrated ability to coach and facilitate faculty performance in delivery of instruction and in the design/adaptation of tools for student assessment. Duties & Responsibilities Participates in the development of enduring and innovative educator and professional development materials. Participates in developing the direction, goals, and implementation of the educator, clinician, and professional development program for the Covenant HealthCare College of Medicine ( CMED ) community faculty (primarily comprised of physicians) throughout Michigan. Designs and conducts workshops on topics including, but not limited to, classroom teaching, learner assessment, small group facilitating, clinical teaching, and portfolio development. This includes training that may be delivered by a variety of methods, including the web, video, in person, etc. Provides individual and systematic consultation to faculty on both the Mt. Pleasant and Saginaw campus to enhance their teaching and assessment skills and educational scholarship development. Monitors and evaluates outcomes of educator and clinical development programs. Collaborates and partners with CMED leadership to optimize the medical school learning/teaching environment. Establishes a database for clinical and educator development programs. Identifies resources and assists in writing and submitting grants to support program activities. Works with advisory groups for clinical and educator development and programs. Develops and implements professional development program and strategic plans related to faculty engagement for both the Mt. Pleasant and Saginaw campus. Implements program and trainings for diverse audiences to build a continuous learning environment that addresses learning needs, develops talent, and fosters engagement. Performs additional duties as assigned. Supervision Exercised Supervisors are expected to support the Leadership Standards of Central Michigan University and foster a culture that inspires excellence. The Leadership Standards define how we lead and treat others on our team. As leaders, it is our responsibility to seek input from our teams to continuously improve our leadership abilities and our demonstration of the standards. Additionally, it is our responsibility to encourage and support the growth and development of those whom we lead. At CMU , we encourage employees to grow both personally and professionally, and thus advance CMU\u2019s culture of excellence. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Applicants are strongly encouraged to submit letters of recommendation. If you wish to include recommendation letter(s) that are not required, please utilize the Recommendation Letters upload field. If there is another applicable document you wish to include that is not required, please utilize the Other Document (1) upload field. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $90,000 - $105,000 per year Division Academic Affairs Department College of Medicine Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Saginaw, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have at least a Master\u2019s degree in medical education, higher education, psychology or related field? Yes No * Do you have at least four years of relevant work experience in a higher education environment? Yes No * Supervisors are expected to support the Leadership Standards of Central Michigan University and foster a culture that inspires excellence. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position and click \u201cYes\u201d if you understand and support the culture that is important to CMU. Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Recommendation Letters Other Document (1) List of References Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45628": {"title": "Counseling Center - Counselor", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | Counseling Center - Counselor Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. Counseling Center - Counselor Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Visa sponsorship for this position/recruitment is not supported. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position will remain open until filled. Position Information Position Information Posting Number F-1057 Position Title Counseling Center - Counselor College/Unit Student Affairs / Residence Life Home Department Counseling Center Employee Group Fixed-Term Faculty - Academic Year Employment Status Full-Time Position Type 9 month (Academic Year) Position Classification Fixed-Term Faculty Position Begin Date 10/15/2026 Position End Date Position Summary The Central Michigan University Counseling Center has a full time, 9 month, in-person mental health counseling position available. This position is aimed at furthering the emotional health and well-being of CMU students. This is a non-teaching, fixed-term faculty position. The Counseling Center provides free and confidential, short term counseling services to currently enrolled CMU students dealing with personal issues that may negatively impact their academic success, interpersonal relationships, health, or well-being. Services are provided in person and via tele-mental health and offered in a variety of formats. The Counseling Center recognizes that each student is a unique individual with different stories, experiences, and needs. We strive to create an open, safe, and inclusive environment where students can freely explore and express all identities, beliefs, and values they hold. This collaborative and supportive team environment offers an excellent work/life balance with a flexible work schedule and opportunities for creativity in student engagement. In addition to counseling services, this position allows for outreach across campus, collaboration with campus partners, professional development, and supervision opportunities. Estimated salary range is between $52,000 and $64,000. Counselor responsibilities: Provide culturally responsive and identity-informed individual, couples, and group counseling services Provide campus outreach and prevention services Responsible for 25 client contact hours per week, 12 paperwork hours and attendance at scheduled staff meetings Provide consultation to colleagues, faculty, staff, and parents Provide crisis intervention services during office hours Participate in professional development within and outside of the center Adhere to Counseling Center scope of practice and procedures Maintain all professional, ethical, and legal standards in the State of Michigan Maintain licensure to provide confidential mental health services in the State of Michigan and meet any related professional development requirements for that license Required Qualifications Masters or doctoral degree in counseling, clinical psychology, social work or related field. Eligibility for licensure in Michigan within one month of start date. Understanding and use of cultural humility in providing counseling services to a diverse group of students. Clinical skills related to short term counseling and crisis intervention. Ability to effectively present outreach programming on mental health topics. Experience working as part of a collaborative and team-based approach to clinical services in a fast-paced work setting. Ability to work autonomously and collaboratively, strong communication skills, as well as commitment to workplace integrity and professional ethics. Ability to perform the essential functions of the job with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Qualifications Full Michigan licensure. Experience working in a college counseling center. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Visa sponsorship for this position/recruitment is not supported. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position will remain open until filled. About the Department The Counseling Center provides free, confidential, short term counseling services to currently enrolled students living in the State of Michigan. Counselors assist students with personal issues that may negatively impact their academic success, interpersonal relationships, health, or safety. A variety of service modalities are used to best meet student\u2019s unique needs. Counseling Center staff value ongoing professional development and the advancement of services to honor the diversity and richness of the CMU community. To learn more about the Counseling Center, please click here. Posting Begins 09/15/2026 Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Type of Recruitment External About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this vacancy? Please indicate the specific source by title (i.e., CMU website, HigherEdJobs.com, Higher Education Recruitment Consortium, The Chronicle, specific professional association, specific list serv, etc.): (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently licensed in Michigan as a counselor, psychologist, or social worker or will you be eligible at the time of hire? (Open Ended Question) Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents List of References Other Document (1) Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45622": {"title": "AUDITOR / SENIOR AUDITOR", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | AUDITOR / SENIOR AUDITOR Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. AUDITOR / SENIOR AUDITOR Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. For best consideration, please submit application materials by September 15th, 2026. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3957 Position Number 34610 Type of Recruitment External Position Title AUDITOR / SENIOR AUDITOR Position Summary Reporting to the Director of Internal Audit, this position plans, performs, and documents risk-based operational, financial, information technology, and compliance audits and other projects independently to evaluate university governance, risk management, and control processes. This position performs all phases of audits/investigations including conducting an audit risk assessment, conducting audit research, preparing the audit programs, evaluating risks and controls, testing control effectiveness to ensure compliance (with regulations, laws, policies, procedures), documenting audit work papers, drafting audit reports (including findings and recommendations), and presenting findings to auditee and management. Work assigned to the Auditor is expected to be carried out with an appropriate and reasonable amount of supervision. The Auditor should be proactive in initiating audit steps and checking with the supervisor when clarity is needed. Work assigned to the Senior Auditor is expected to be carried out with minimal supervision. Required Qualifications Auditor: Bachelor\u2019s degree in accounting, finance, business, or a related field. Two years of auditing or related experience, including some IT auditing. Demonstrated intellectual curiosity and critical thinking skills, with the ability to identify inconsistencies, recognize potential issues, and ask probing questions to ensure accuracy and understanding. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively with individuals at all organizational levels and project a positive attitude. Ability to work as a team, both within and outside of Internal Audit. Demonstrated experience with audit report writing. Analytical, interpersonal, and communication skills both verbal and written. Strong understanding of internal controls. Demonstrated skillset as a self-directed, service-oriented, forward-thinking, and creative individual with high ethical standards. Ability to learn processes and apply to future scenarios. Ability to handle confidential and sensitive information with discretion. Demonstrated time management skills with the ability to prioritize and plan multiple projects and activities. Ability to prepare recommendations and reports in a professional and timely manner. Proficiency with Microsoft Office software, including Outlook, Word, Excel, and PowerPoint. Ability to apply or develop a baseline understanding of IT audit practices, including information systems, IT general controls, and technology infrastructure. Ability to apply or develop a baseline understanding of Agile audit practices. Senior Auditor: All qualifications listed for an Auditor, plus: Experience in conducting the full life cycle of an audit with minimal supervision and guidance. Four additional years of auditing or related experience. Certification as a CPA , CIA , CISA or other relevant professional certification Preferred Qualifications Masters degree or relevant professional certification. Familiarity and work experience in a higher education environment. Familiarity and work experience with SAP . Public accounting or relevant experience. Ability to organize and lead the work of others on an audit team. Knowledge of relevant external regulations such as HIPAA , FERPA , PCI Standards, and GLBA . Experience in or familiarity with vulnerability scanning and penetration testing. Advanced knowledge and/or experience in completing IT audits. Experience in computer assisted audit techniques using data analytics software. Familiarity with diverse computing environments and architecture, data centers and co-locations facilities/operations. Advanced knowledge and/or experience in Agile auditing skills. Experience in risk assessment and risk management activities. Active in professional auditing organizations. Knowledge of IT control objectives including NIST , COBIT , and GTAG Thorough knowledge and experience applying auditing theory and practice in accordance with the IIA standards, ISACA standards, and IIA Code of Ethics. Duties & Responsibilities Auditor: Performs the following tasks under direct supervision: Actively participates in the annual risk assessment and audit plan creation process and proactively keeps the Director informed of the progress of audits. Performs planning activities with the audit client to gain an understanding of client operations. Conducts a risk assessment for each audit to identify potential risks and what controls should be in place. Designs audit objectives and procedures for each audit, prepares audit programs, and performs audits, following applicable standards ( IIA , ISACA ,), as well as review for integrity, security, adequacy of controls, effectiveness and efficiency, compliance with policy, regulations or legal requirements, and consistency with management objectives. Conducts entrance meetings with audit clients to discuss audit objectives, scope and methodology, and timing of the audit. Performs operational, financial, compliance and IT audit procedures of University departments, processes, systems and procedures to assure appropriate internal controls are present. Examines transactions for accuracy, reasonableness, and compliance with University policy. Meets with and/or communicates with audit clientele throughout the audit process, providing regular status updates. Thoroughly and logically documents audit work papers. Identifies internal control weaknesses and recommends improvements to effectiveness and efficiency. Drafts potential audit findings and audit recommendations. Drafts audit reports and conducts closing meetings with audit clients to discuss findings, recommendations, and management responses. Delivers oral presentations to management in all phases of audits, including presentation of recommendations and reports to appropriate senior management personnel (provost, vice presidents, deans, department heads, etc.) as required. Evaluates adequacy of the management responses for corrective action to ensure responses are accurate, comprehensive, reflect the position of the University and will be addressed in an appropriate time frame. Reviews allegations of fraud and fraudulent activity reported through the University\u2019s confidential ethics hotline or from other sources and performs audit procedures as appropriate. Stays abreast of current developments in higher education, compliance requirements, IT auditing, information privacy and security and information systems technology to maintain and/or build technical competence and proficiency. Assists with the maintenance of in-house audit tools. Learns, explores and creates data analytic and continuous monitoring tools. Assists external auditors, as required. Ensures that all audit assignments are completed in accordance with the annual audit plan approved by the Board of Trustees\u2019 Audit Committee. Performs special audit projects as assigned by the Director. Assists student intern(s) on assigned audit projects. Assists other Auditors or works on team audits as necessary. Performs consulting activities with University departments as requested. Completes 10-20 hours (40 hours if certified) of continuing professional education annually on topics related to auditing. Attends Board of Trustees meetings as requested by the Director. Performs other duties as assigned. Senior Auditor: Performs all duties and responsibilities of the Auditor with limited supervision, plus: Performs more complex and in-depth audits with increased confidence and proficiency. Provides audit assistance and guidance to less senior audit staff. Completes 40 hours of continuing professional education annually on topics related to auditing that are in line with certification requirements. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. For best consideration, please submit application materials by September 15th, 2026. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range Auditor: $60,000-$75,000 / Senior Auditor: $75,000-$90,000 Division President Department Internal Audit Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have at least a bachelor's degree in accounting, finance, business, or a related field? Yes No * Do you have at least two years of auditing or related experience, including some IT auditing? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Recommendation Letters Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45625": {"title": "Medical Mycology Postdoctoral Research Fellow", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | Medical Mycology Postdoctoral Research Fellow Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. Medical Mycology Postdoctoral Research Fellow Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Letters of interest may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. Position Information Position Information Posting Number F-1060 Position Title Medical Mycology Postdoctoral Research Fellow College/Unit College of Medicine Home Department Covenant HealthCare College of Medicine at Central Michigan University Employee Group Postdoctoral Research Fellow Employment Status Full-Time Position Type 12 month Position Classification Postdoctoral Research Fellow Position Begin Date 01/06/2027 Position End Date Position Summary The Nosanchuk Laboratory at the Covenant HealthCare College of Medicine at Central Michigan University is seeking two postdoctoral fellows to work on basic medical mycology. The work focus of these positions includes: Understanding the role of fungal extracellular vesicles; Deciphering the biology of fungal melanin; Exploring the molecular basis of fungal virulence including through genetic manipulation and next-generation sequencing approaches; Testing of novel antifungal compounds on fungal critical threat pathogens; Developing novel fungal diagnostics. The positions have an initial 36-month appointment, with the potential for an additional 24-month extension depending on funding and satisfactory performance. Required Qualifications PhD, MD, PharmD or DVM with clear basic and/or translational science experience in medical mycology, microbiology, molecular biology, genetics, cell biology, or a related field. Peer-reviewed publications. Motivation to lead independent research projects. Ability to perform the essential functions of the job with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Qualifications Experience working on extracellular vesicle biology, animal pathogenesis models ( Galleria and mice), genetic techniques, and/or microscopy. Demonstrated evidence of independence. Effective oral and written communication skills. Ability to collaborate and mentor individuals at diverse stages of their careers including undergraduate and graduate students. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an online application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Letters of interest may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. About the Department The Covenant HealthCare College of Medicine at Central Michigan University educates diverse students and trains culturally competent physicians to provide comprehensive health care and services to underserved populations in Michigan and beyond. Our faculty, staff and graduates advance health and wellness through exceptional education, innovative research, quality patientcare and strategic collaborations to improve the health and well-being of individuals and communities. Since its foundation in 2010, the Covenant HealthCare College of Medicine at Central Michigan University strives to be a national leader in the pursuit of basic, translational, clinical, medical education and population health research. We aim to develop programs to advance medical and scientific knowledge and improve patient care and community wellness. The ultimate goal is to contribute to the health of the public, the practice of medicine and the education of health professionals; all while promoting the development of academically oriented physicians. Posting Begins 10/01/2026 Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Type of Recruitment External About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you learn of this vacancy? Please indicate the specific source by title (i.e., CMU website, HigherEdJobs.com, Higher Education Recruitment Consortium, The Chronicle, specific professional association, specific list serv, etc.): (Open Ended Question) Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Letter of Interest List of References Optional Documents Other Document (1) Statement of Research Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45629": {"title": "ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / ADMISSIONS (2 POSITIONS)", "description": "CMU Applicant Portal | ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / ADMISSIONS (2 POSITIONS) Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Log In /Create Account Help Administrative Office Assistant Custodial / Landscape / Skilled Trades Dispatcher Faculty Lieutenant Police Post-Doctoral Research Professional & Admin-Hourly Professional & Admin-Salary Public Broadcasting-Hourly Public Broadcasting-Salary Senior Officer Sergeant Supervisory Technical Temporary Staff For Career Opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP), please read the following: CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a joint partner with Central Michigan University (CMU), Covenant Healthcare, and St. Mary\u2019s of Michigan. CMEP is located in Saginaw, Michigan, and is a separate nonprofit legal entity from CMU. The faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty at CMU to deliver an innovative curriculum to CMU medical students. Because CMU Medical Education Partners (CMEP) is a separate legal entity (and employer) from CMU, the employment opportunities available through CMEP are not employment positions with CMU. When you click the link below, you will be leaving the CMU Career Opportunities webpage. CMU is not responsible for the content of the webpage to which you are being redirected. After reading the above information, please click here if you are interested in employment opportunities with CMU Medical Education Partners. ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / ADMISSIONS (2 POSITIONS) Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening. To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark this Job link. If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. If you need to finish applying, click on the Continue this Job Application button. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. For best consideration, please submit application materials by October 30, 2026. Position Information Position Information Posting Number S-3998 Position Number 66340, 68800 Type of Recruitment External Position Title ASSISTANT DIRECTOR / ADMISSIONS (2 POSITIONS) Position Summary The Assistant Director of Admissions is responsible for the promotion and marketing of Central Michigan University within the continental United States in a defined travel territory. Travel includes attending college fairs, professional conferences, community-partnership events, and alumni activities. This position acts as a liaison between the University and high school and community college officials, providing academic, career, and admissions advice to prospective students, representing the University at numerous public speaking engagements, and assisting in the daily operation of the Office of Undergraduate Admissions. This position also represents international, graduate, and global admissions as needed. Required Qualifications Bachelor\u2019s degree. One year of experience; preferably in marketing, sales, public relations, higher education, or student-related professions. Experience working with individuals from a variety of backgrounds including low socio-economic, multicultural, and non-traditional students. Possession of a valid Driver\u2019s License. Willingness and ability to travel independently and work evenings and weekends as needed. Working knowledge of computer applications and industry-related systems. Demonstrated positive interpersonal skills. Ability to work well with the public, communicate effectively, and project a positive image. Demonstrated ability to work collaboratively and the desire to work as part of a team. Strong oral and written communication skills. Ability to perform the essential functions of the position, with or without reasonable accommodation. Preferred Qualifications Experience dealing with the public and presenting information in large venues or forums. Experience in maintaining data, report writing, and the evaluation of high school or college transcripts. Demonstrated experience sharing University policies, procedures, and regulations. Demonstrated ability to resolve conflict peacefully. Duties & Responsibilities Responsible for meeting enrollment goals for a defined travel territory. Represents Central Michigan University during statewide and national recruiting events. Coordinates campus recruitment programs designed to assist prospective freshmen and transfer students. Works with high schools and community colleges to plan and arrange onsite visits and provide campus tours; coordinates high school, community college, and individual visitor appointments, and conducts onsite admissions programs. Assists colleges with admissions presentations and tours of campus. Participates in recruitment campaigns via email, social media platforms, and through media outlets (i.e. newspaper, magazine, radio, and television). Reviews undergraduate admission applications, responds to requests for information, and determines the status of admissions (i.e. acceptance or denial). Plans, organizes, and implements receptions for prospective students and their guests. Provides information concerning academic programs, career options, housing, financial aid, and transfer credit evaluation. Serves as a representative of and ad hoc recruiter for graduate, international, and global/online admissions. Works with alumni to promote Central Michigan University. Supervises volunteers, student employees, office interns, and graduate assistants as needed. Performs other duties as assigned. Supervision Exercised None. Message to Applicants Central Michigan University is dedicated to fostering an environment that is reflective of the communities we serve. We are especially interested in highly qualified candidates who will advance and promote CMU\u2019s mission, vision, and leadership standards. You must submit an on-line application in order to be considered as an applicant for this position. Cover letters may be addressed to the Hiring Committee. This position will remain open until filled. The university reserves the right to close the recruitment process once a sufficient applicant pool has been identified. For best consideration, please submit application materials by October 30, 2026. Employee Group Professional & Administrative -Salary Staff Pay Level Pay Range $44,000 - $52,000 Division Student Recruitment & Retention Department Undergraduate Recruitment - Admissions Position Status Regular Position End Date Employment Status Full-Time FTE 1.0 Position Type 12 month Weekly Work Schedule Mon-Fri, 8:00 a.m. - 5:00 p.m. / weekends and evenings as needed Location Mount Pleasant, MI About the Department About CMU Central Michigan University has a more than 125-year legacy of preparing students to become leaders and changemakers in their communities and in their personal and professional lives. We serve nearly 15,500 students on our Mount Pleasant campus, in satellite locations around the state and throughout the country, and through flexible online programs. Many of our approximately 300 undergraduate, master\u2019s, specialist and doctoral programs in the arts, media, business, education, human services, health professions, liberal arts, social sciences, medicine, science and engineering are nationally ranked for excellence. CMU leads the nation in leadership development programming through our Sarah R. Opperman Leadership Institute, and we are proud to be among only 5% of U.S. universities in the top two Carnegie research classifications. Our faculty work with graduate and undergraduate students in areas such as Great Lakes research, medical innovation, engineering technology and more. Central is home to 17 men\u2019s and women\u2019s Division 1 sports including football, basketball, gymnastics, baseball, wrestling and more. Our student-athletes achieve great success in competition and in the classroom, capturing Mid-American Conference championships and maintaining an average cumulative GPA of 3.17. CMU is located in Mount Pleasant, a community that blends the best of small-town living with big-city amenities. It\u2019s part of the culturally varied and vibrant Great Lakes Bay Region that also includes Saginaw, Bay City, Midland and the state\u2019s largest Native American community, centered on the Saginaw Chippewa Isabella Reservation in Mount Pleasant. Area residents enjoy the mix of outdoor activities, cultural events, shopping and dining options, and family attractions. Other major Michigan destinations and attractions \u2014 Lansing, Grand Rapids, Detroit, Traverse City, wineries, beaches, golf and ski resorts, and many more \u2014 are within easy reach of the city\u2019s central location in Michigan\u2019s Lower Peninsula. CMU employees enjoy access to a nationally recognized wellness program along with health care and benefits that exceed regional, state and national norms. CMU Leadership Standards Central Michigan University is a place where we value students and work for their success, where we act as family, and where employees are engaged, appreciated and have extraordinary opportunities to make a difference. We intentionally maintain and strengthen the hallmark CMU culture that sets us apart from our peers by expecting CMU leaders and employees to model the following Leadership Standards and develop them within their teams. Please review the Leadership Standards before applying for this position. EEO Statement CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. If you wish to see \u201cKnow Your Rights \u201d posters, please click here . CMU does not discriminate on the basis of sex in the education program or activity that it operates, including admission and employment, and is required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972 not to discriminate in such a matter. Inquiries about the application of Title IX can be made to CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator, the US Department of Education\u2019s Assistant Secretary, or both. CMU\u2019s Title IX Coordinator can be reached at: Phone: 989-774-3253 Office: 103 E. Preston St. Bovee University Center, suite 306 Mount Pleasant, MI 48858 Email: titleix@cmich.edu Posting Ends Open Until Filled Yes Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * How did you first learn of this job opportunity? Please list the specific advertising source or indicate if it was word of mouth. (Open Ended Question) * Are you currently an internal employee of CMU according to the university's definition? Yes No * If yes, to which employee group do you belong? (If not applicable, select \"Not Applicable\"). Not Applicable Administrative Office Assistant Dispatcher Lieutenant Medical Faculty P&A, SO or Faculty Police Public Broadcasting Sergeant Service Maintenance Supervisory/Technical * Do you have a bachelor's degree? Yes No * Do you have at least one year of experience; preferably in marketing, sales, public relations, higher education, or student-related professions? Yes No * Do you have experience working with individuals from a variety of backgrounds including low socio-economic, multicultural and non-traditional students? Yes No * Do you possess a valid driver's license? Yes No Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Resume/Curriculum Vitae Cover Letter Optional Documents Recommendation Letters Other Document (1) List of References Staff postings - Human Resources | Contact HR | (989)774-2010 | 109 Rowe Faculty postings - Faculty Personnel Services | Contact FPS | (989)774-3368 | 308 Warriner CMU is an Equal Opportunity Employer and institution. CMU does not discriminate against persons based on age, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, height, marital status, national origin, political persuasion, pregnancy, childbirth or related medical conditions, race, religion, sex, sex-based stereotypes, sexual orientation, transgender status, veteran status, or weight. Copyright \u00a9 Central Michigan University, Mount Pleasant, Mich. 48859 | Phone 989-774-4000 All data submitted via this site is secure and encrypted using Secure Socket Layer (SSL) technology. SSL protects information as it crosses the Internet. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}}, "rows": {"https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45595": {"school_id": 654, "posting_url": "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45595", "job_title_in_post": "COORDINATOR/STUDY ABROAD", "position_type": "Research_Fellow", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "faculty of CMEP works collaboratively and interactively with the College of Medicine faculty", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "October 26, 2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.jobs.cmich.edu/postings/45502": {"school_id": 654, "posting_url": "h